{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758154574,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_AGixzTHWN2fDl4D3TyihNU73","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs","offset":2260,"limit":390},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n2260: \n2261:       // Sandbox resolution stays write-capable by default even for review lineages:\n2262:       // the review subprocess writes its own iteration artifacts (iterations/iteration-NNN.md,\n2263:       // deep-review-state.jsonl, review-report.md, resource-map.md) INTO lineageDir, so a\n2264:       // blanket read-only default would break those writes. The lineageDir-only write boundary\n2265:       // is enforced by the prompt ('Do not touch any path outside lineageDir') rather than by a\n2266:       // narrower sandbox; a path-scoped workspace-write would be the stronger fix if the CLIs\n2267:       // exposed one. Callers can still pass an explicit sandboxMode to override.\n2268:       const resolvedSandbox = resolveSandboxMode(lineage.sandboxMode);\n2269:       const resolvedPermission = resolveClaudePermissionMode(lineage.sandboxMode);\n2270: \n2271:       const effectiveSandbox = resolvedSandbox;\n2272:       const effectivePermission = resolvedPermission;\n2273: \n2274:       const { command, args: cmdArgs, input } = buildLineageCommand(\n2275:         lineage,\n2276:         prompt,\n2277:         effectiveSandbox,\n2278:         effectivePermission,\n2279:         {\n2280:           loopType,\n2281:           specFolder,\n2282:           lineageDir,\n2283:           sessionId,\n2284:           convergenceThreshold,\n2285:           stopPolicy,\n2286:           researchTopic,\n2287:         },\n2288:       );\n2289: \n2290:       // Advertise a per-replica state dir hint to the child via SPECKIT_<KIND>_STATE_DIR.\n2291:       // This is DETECTION-ONLY: the native CLIs read their own home env (OPENCODE_HOME /\n2292:       // OPENCODE_HOME / CLAUDE_CODE_HOME), not this var, so it does NOT relocate the\n2293:       // native lockfile. Real same-kind-replica isolation comes from each lineage's\n2294:       // unique artifact dir (lineage.label); remapping the CLI home to isolate the lock\n2295:       // is deliberately avoided here because relocating the home breaks credential/auth\n2296:       // lookup (the \"Not logged in\" failure the dispatch-env allowlist guards against).\n2297:       const stateEnvKey = SPECKIT_STATE_ENV_BY_KIND[lineage.kind];\n2298:       const extraEnv = {\n2299:         SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID: lineage.label,\n2300:         // A fan-out lineage is an orchestrated sub-session running an autonomous\n2301:         // workflow: it has no user turn to answer Gate 3, so the spec-gate must be\n2302:         // fully inert. ENFORCE=0 alone is NOT enough — that only stops the deny, while\n2303:         // the classify step still injects the Gate-3 question, which a cli-opencode\n2304:         // child then answers instead of doing its work. DISABLED makes both classify\n2305:         // and enforce no-ops; AI_SESSION_CHILD lets the worktree wrapper exec in place.\n2306:         // buildExecutorDispatchEnv filters these keys (outside the per-kind allowlist),\n2307:         // so they are re-injected here to reach the child. Harmless for the codex path.\n2308:         MK_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED: '1',\n2309:         AI_SESSION_CHILD: '1',\n2310:         ...(stateEnvKey ? { [stateEnvKey]: stateDir } : {}),\n2311:         ...(lineage.kind === 'cli-claude-code' && lineage.configDir\n2312:           ? { CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR: validateClaudeConfigDir(lineage.configDir) }\n2313:           : {}),\n2314:       };\n2315: \n2316:       // Recursion guard (fail closed): the executor stack can already name the hosting\n2317:       // runtime before the first detached fan-out spawn. The lineage marker is added only\n2318:       // to a spawned seat, so both signals are required to prove that a seat is trying to\n2319:       // fan out its own executor kind again.\n2320:       const inheritedLineageId = process.env.SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID;\n2321:       const isInsideFanoutLineage = typeof inheritedLineageId === 'string'\n2322:         && inheritedLineageId.trim() !== '';\n2323:       if (\n2324:         isInsideFanoutLineage\n2325:         && detectSameKindFromStack(process.env[CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV], lineage.kind)\n2326:       ) {\n2327:         throw new Error(\n2328:           `recursive ${lineage.kind} dispatch blocked for lineage ${lineage.label}: ${lineage.kind} already on ${CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV}`,\n2329:         );\n2330:       }\n2331: \n2332:       // Stamp the dispatch stack with this lineage's executor kind so a seat that\n2333:       // tries to recursively launch the same kind is detectable by the runtime\n2334:       // recursion guard (detectSameKindFromStack reads SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK).\n2335:       // buildExecutorDispatchEnv filters the parent env to the per-kind allowlist,\n2336:       // so the SPECKIT_* lineage/state-dir keys are applied AFTER the filter to\n2337:       // preserve the per-replica lockfile isolation they provide.\n2338:       const dispatchEnv = { ...buildExecutorDispatchEnv(lineage, process.env), ...extraEnv };\n2339: \n2340:       const timeoutMs = computeLineageTimeoutMs(lineage, lineageTimeoutHoursOverride);\n2341:       let lastLineageEventAtMs = Date.now();\n2342:       const markLineageEvent = () => {\n2343:         lastLineageEventAtMs = Date.now();\n2344:       };\n2345:       const stopStallWatchdog = startLineageStallWatchdog({\n2346:         thresholdMs: stallWatchdogMs,\n2347:         label: lineage.label,\n2348:         ledgerPath,\n2349:         getLastEventAtMs: () => lastLineageEventAtMs,\n2350:         getGauges: () => latestGauges,\n2351:       });\n2352: \n2353:       const stopProgressHeartbeat = startLineageProgressHeartbeat({\n2354:         cadenceMs: progressHeartbeatMs,\n2355:         label: lineage.label,\n2356:         ledgerPath,\n2357:         getGauges: () => latestGauges,\n2358:       });\n2359: \n2360:       // A codex leaf runs workspace-write, which can write anywhere in the repo.\n2361:       // Snapshot the out-of-artifact dirty paths BEFORE dispatch so the post-\n2362:       // dispatch guard can isolate the leaf's own NEW out-of-scope writes and\n2363:       // never touch unrelated pre-existing dirty work. Native/cli-opencode/cli-\n2364:       // claude-code lineages are intentionally excluded: their dispatch models may\n2365:       // legitimately write outside lineageDir, and codex is the unguarded path.\n2366:       const containmentEnabled = lineage.kind === 'cli-codex';\n2367:       // Sibling lineages run concurrently and write their own artifacts after this\n2368:       // leaf's baseline is captured. Those writes are indistinguishable from this\n2369:       // leaf's, so treating them as its violations reverts a sibling's legitimate\n2370:       // in-flight work — a completed lineage can be erased by an unrelated leaf\n2371:       // tripping containment. Exclude them from attribution; everything outside\n2372:       // both this leaf's dir and its siblings' stays guarded.\n2373:       const siblingLineageDirs = allLineages\n2374:         .filter((other) => other.label !== lineage.label)\n2375:         .map((other) => path.join(lineagesDir, other.label));\n2376:       const preDispatchDirtyPaths = containmentEnabled\n2377:         ? snapshotOutOfScopeDirtyPaths({\n2378:           repoRoot: process.cwd(),\n2379:           artifactDir: lineageDir,\n2380:           unattributableDirs: siblingLineageDirs,\n2381:         })\n2382:         : [];\n2383: \n2384:       let result;\n2385:       try {\n2386:         result = await runLineageProcess(command, cmdArgs, {\n2387:           cwd: process.cwd(),\n2388:           timeoutMs,\n2389:           env: dispatchEnv,\n2390:           maxBuffer: 20 * 1024 * 1024,\n2391:           abortSignal: context.signal,\n2392:           onOutput: markLineageEvent,\n2393:           onSpawn: ({ pid }) => {\n2394:             lineageProcessLiveness.set(livenessKey, { alive: true, pid });\n2395:           },\n2396:           onExit: ({ pid, exitedAtMs }) => {\n2397:             lineageProcessLiveness.set(livenessKey, { alive: false, pid, exitedAtMs });\n2398:           },\n2399:           ...(typeof input === 'string' ? { input } : {}),\n2400:         });\n2401:       } finally {\n2402:         stopProgressHeartbeat();\n2403:         stopStallWatchdog();\n2404:       }\n2405: \n2406:       // Save subprocess stdout for salvage sweep (write failures in weak CLI executors).\n2407:       const logsDir = path.join(lineageDir, 'logs');\n2408:       fs.mkdirSync(logsDir, { recursive: true });\n2409:       const savedStdout = typeof result.stdout === 'string' ? result.stdout : '';\n2410:       fs.writeFileSync(path.join(logsDir, 'fanout-lineage.out'), savedStdout, 'utf8');\n2411: \n2412:       // Recover missing iteration files from captured stdout when possible. Runs\n2413:       // BEFORE the failure throw below so iteration recovery is never lost.\n2414:       const salvage = runSalvageSweep(lineageDir, loopType, savedStdout);\n2415:       const slotAccounting = buildSlotAccounting(hrStart, slotIntervalMs);\n2416:       lineageSlotAccounting.set(lineage.label, slotAccounting);\n2417: \n2418:       // Structural write-containment for codex leaves: diff the working tree for\n2419:       // NEW out-of-artifact-dir writes, revert exactly those paths, log a\n2420:       // containment_violation event, and fail the iteration fail-closed. The leaf\n2421:       // must still be free to write its iteration file/delta/state record inside\n2422:       // lineageDir; only OUT-of-lineageDir writes are violations. Fails open when\n2423:       // the artifact dir is outside the git worktree (hermetic test lineages).\n2424:       if (containmentEnabled) {\n2425:         const containment = enforceWriteContainment({\n2426:           repoRoot: process.cwd(),\n2427:           artifactDir: lineageDir,\n2428:           unattributableDirs: siblingLineageDirs,\n2429:           preDispatchDirtyPaths,\n2430:           iteration: attempt,\n2431:           label: lineage.label,\n2432:         });\n2433:         if (containment.violations.length > 0) {\n2434:           if (containment.event) {\n2435:             appendFanoutStatusLedger(ledgerPath, {\n2436:               ...containment.event,\n2437:               at: new Date().toISOString(),\n2438:               label: lineage.label,\n2439:               run_id: runId,\n2440:               loop_type: loopType,\n2441:               spec_folder: specFolder,\n2442:               gauges: latestGauges,\n2443:             });\n2444:           }\n2445:           const failure = new Error(\n2446:             `lineage ${lineage.label} violated write containment: reverted `\n2447:               + `${containment.violations.length} out-of-scope path(s): `\n2448:               + `${containment.violations.map((v) => v.path).join(', ')}`,\n2449:           );\n2450:           failure.label = lineage.label;\n2451:           failure.exitCode = 1;\n2452:           failure.timedOut = false;\n2453:           failure.containmentViolation = containment.violations;\n2454:           failure.salvage = salvage;\n2455:           throw failure;\n2456:         }\n2457:       }\n2458: \n2459:       const exitCode = result.status ?? (result.error ? 1 : 0);\n2460:       const timedOut = result.signal === 'SIGTERM';\n2461:       // Any signal-kill is abnormal, not just the orchestrator's own SIGTERM timeout — a\n2462:       // stall-watchdog / lag-ceiling abort or an external SIGKILL leaves result.status null,\n2463:       // so exitCode computes to 0 and the lineage would otherwise be masked as success.\n2464:       const killedBySignal = result.signal != null;\n2465:       const missingArtifacts = findMissingLineageArtifacts(loopType, lineageDir);\n2466:       const stateRead = readLineageStateRecords(loopType, lineageDir);\n2467:       const stopPolicyViolation = findMaxIterationsPolicyViolation({\n2468:         loopType,\n2469:         stateRead,\n2470:         lineage,\n2471:         stopPolicy,\n2472:         lineageDir,\n2473:       });\n2474: \n2475:       // A lineage whose CLI exits non-zero or is killed by the timeout is a FAILURE,\n2476:       // not a success. Throw so the pool settles this item as rejected and counts it\n2477:       // in summary.failed/all_failed, which drives the process exit code. Returning a\n2478:       // plain object here would let the pool record any completed worker as fulfilled\n2479:       // regardless of the underlying CLI exit, masking failed/timed-out lineages.\n2480:       //\n2481:       // Pi is the exception: it returns a non-zero exit code non-deterministically even\n2482:       // on a successful dispatch (identical unauthenticated runs returned 0 then 1), so\n2483:       // for cli-pi a non-zero exit is not a failure signal. The artifact validation below\n2484:       // is its success gate instead — a genuinely failed pi run produces no artifact and\n2485:       // is rejected there. Timeouts and signal kills remain real failures for every kind.\n2486:       const exitCodeIsFailure = exitCode !== 0 && lineage.kind !== 'cli-pi';\n2487:       if (timedOut || killedBySignal || exitCodeIsFailure) {\n2488:         const reason = timedOut\n2489:           ? 'timed out'\n2490:           : killedBySignal\n2491:             ? `killed by signal ${result.signal}`\n2492:             : `exited with code ${exitCode}`;\n2493:         const failure = new Error(`lineage ${lineage.label} ${reason}`);\n2494:         failure.label = lineage.label;\n2495:         failure.exitCode = exitCode;\n2496:         failure.timedOut = timedOut;\n2497:         failure.killedBySignal = killedBySignal;\n2498:         failure.salvage = salvage;\n2499:         throw failure;\n2500:       }\n2501: \n2502:       if (missingArtifacts.length > 0) {\n2503:         const failure = new Error(\n2504:           `lineage ${lineage.label} exited 0 but did not produce expected artifact: ${missingArtifacts.join(', ')}`,\n2505:         );\n2506:         failure.label = lineage.label;\n2507:         failure.exitCode = exitCode;\n2508:         failure.timedOut = false;\n2509:         failure.salvage = { salvaged: salvage.salvaged, failed: Math.max(1, salvage.failed) };\n2510:         failure.missingArtifacts = missingArtifacts;\n2511:         throw failure;\n2512:       }\n2513: \n2514:       if (stopPolicyViolation) {\n2515:         const failure = new Error(\n2516:           `lineage ${lineage.label} violated max-iterations stop policy: ${stopPolicyViolation}`,\n2517:         );\n2518:         failure.label = lineage.label;\n2519:         failure.exitCode = exitCode;\n2520:         failure.timedOut = false;\n2521:         failure.salvage = salvage;\n2522:         failure.stopPolicyViolation = stopPolicyViolation;\n2523:         throw failure;\n2524:       }\n2525: \n2526:       // An exit-0 lineage whose salvage sweep could not recover every iteration\n2527:       // markdown is NOT fulfilled, even when the top-level report exists. Returning\n2528:       // here would let a lineage with a fanout_salvage_failed marker pass as complete,\n2529:       // dropping durable per-iteration evidence from merge/synthesis. Throw so the\n2530:       // pool retries it (the classifier maps salvage.failed > 0 to artifact_miss).\n2531:       if (salvage && salvage.failed > 0) {\n2532:         const failure = new Error(\n2533:           `lineage ${lineage.label} exited 0 but ${salvage.failed} iteration markdown file(s) were unrecoverable`,\n2534:         );\n2535:         failure.label = lineage.label;\n2536:         failure.exitCode = exitCode;\n2537:         failure.timedOut = false;\n2538:         failure.salvage = { salvaged: salvage.salvaged, failed: salvage.failed };\n2539:         failure.missingArtifacts = [];\n2540:         throw failure;\n2541:       }\n2542: \n2543:       const output = { label: lineage.label, exitCode, timedOut, salvage, ...slotAccounting };\n2544:       if (stateRead.statePath && !stateRead.missing && !stateRead.parseError) {\n2545:         const slotWindowEndIso = new Date().toISOString();\n2546:         try {\n2547:           const timestampCheck = checkLineageTimestampWindow(stateRead.records, {\n2548:             windowStart: slotWindowStartIso,\n2549:             windowEnd: slotWindowEndIso,\n2550:             toleranceMs: DEFAULT_LINEAGE_TIMESTAMP_TOLERANCE_MS,\n2551:           });\n2552:           if (timestampCheck.anomalous > 0) {\n2553:             const timestampAnomaly = buildTimestampAnomalyPayload({\n2554:               lineage,\n2555:               statePath: stateRead.statePath,\n2556:               check: timestampCheck,\n2557:             });\n2558:             appendFanoutStatusLedger(ledgerPath, {\n2559:               event: 'timestamp_anomaly',\n2560:               status: 'warning',\n2561:               severity: 'warning',\n2562:               label: lineage.label,\n2563:               at: new Date().toISOString(),\n2564:               ...timestampAnomaly,\n2565:             });\n2566:             output.timestamp_anomaly = timestampAnomaly;\n2567:           }\n2568:         } catch {\n2569:           // Timestamp telemetry is advisory and cannot affect lineage fulfillment.\n2570:         }\n2571:       }\n2572: \n2573:       return output;\n2574:     },\n2575:   });\n2576: \n2577:   const timestampAnomalies = collectTimestampAnomalies(results);\n2578:   const finalSummary = timestampAnomalies.length > 0\n2579:     ? { ...summary, timestamp_anomalies: timestampAnomalies }\n2580:     : summary;\n2581: \n2582:   writeOrchestrationSummary(summaryPath, {\n2583:     run_id: runId,\n2584:     loop_type: loopType,\n2585:     spec_folder: specFolder,\n2586:     base_artifact_dir: baseArtifactDir,\n2587:     total_cli_lineages: cliLineages.length,\n2588:     orphaned_lineages: orphanedLineages,\n2589:     ...finalSummary,\n2590:   });\n2591: \n2592:   const exitCode = finalSummary.all_failed ? 3 : finalSummary.failed > 0 ? 2 : 0;\n2593:   jsonOut({ status: exitCode === 0 ? 'ok' : 'partial', run_id: runId, results, summary: finalSummary });\n2594:   process.exit(exitCode);\n2595: }\n2596: \n2597: if (require.main === module && isTsxLoaded) {\n2598:   main().catch((err) => {\n2599:     const code = classifyExitCode(err);\n2600:     jsonOut({\n2601:       status: 'error',\n2602:       error: err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err),\n2603:       code: err && err.code ? err.code : 'SCRIPT_ERROR',\n2604:     });\n2605:     if (code === 1) {\n2606:       process.stderr.write(\n2607:         JSON.stringify({ error: err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err), stack: err && err.stack }) + '\\n',\n2608:       );\n2609:     }\n2610:     process.exit(code);\n2611:   });\n2612: }\n2613: \n2614: module.exports = {\n2615:   DEVIN_ALLOWED_MODELS,\n2616:   DEVIN_DEFAULT_MODEL,\n2617:   CURSOR_ALLOWED_MODELS,\n2618:   CURSOR_DEFAULT_MODEL,\n2619:   PI_ALLOWED_MODELS,\n2620:   PI_DEFAULT_MODEL,\n2621:   buildLineageCommand,\n2622:   buildInvocationFingerprintPayload,\n2623:   isCodexBinaryAvailable,\n2624:   isCursorBinaryAvailable,\n2625:   isDevinBinaryAvailable,\n2626:   isPiBinaryAvailable,\n2627:   buildLoopPrompt,\n2628:   findMaxIterationsPolicyViolation,\n2629:   isMaxIterationsStopReason,\n2630:   computeLineageTimeoutMs,\n2631:   assertLineageTimeoutHoursOverrideWithinCeiling,\n2632:   computeLineageBudgetUpperBound,\n2633:   evaluateLineageBudgetCap,\n2634:   computeAggregateBudgetUpperBound,\n2635:   evaluateAggregateBudgetCap,\n2636:   normalizeAggregateBudgetGuards,\n2637:   normalizeProgressHeartbeatMs,\n2638:   normalizePostExitGraceMs,\n2639:   normalizeLineageBudgetGuards,\n2640:   normalizeStallWatchdogMs,\n2641:   computeSkippedCount,\n2642:   decorateSlotAccountingEvent,\n2643:   startLineageProgressHeartbeat,\n2644:   startLineageStallWatchdog,\n2645:   statusForLedgerEvent,\n2646:   updateLineageSnapshot,\n2647:   applyFlatPoolAssignmentGuard,\n2648: };\n\n(End of file - total 2648 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\n      // Sandbox resolution stays write-capable by default even for review lineages:\n      // the review subprocess writes its own iteration artifacts (iterations/iteration-NNN.md,\n      // deep-review-state.jsonl, review-report.md, resource-map.md) INTO lineageDir, so a\n      // blanket read-only default would break those writes. The lineageDir-only write boundary\n      // is enforced by the prompt ('Do not touch any path outside lineageDir') rather than by a\n      // narrower sandbox; a path-scoped workspace-write would be the stronger fix if the CLIs\n      // exposed one. Callers can still pass an explicit sandboxMode to override.\n      const resolvedSandbox = resolveSandboxMode(lineage.sandboxMode);\n      const resolvedPermission = resolveClaudePermissionMode(lineage.sandboxMode);\n\n      const effectiveSandbox = resolvedSandbox;\n      const effectivePermission = resolvedPermission;\n\n      const { command, args: cmdArgs, input } = buildLineageCommand(\n        lineage,\n        prompt,\n        effectiveSandbox,\n        effectivePermission,\n        {","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs","text":"\n      // Sandbox resolution stays write-capable by default even for review lineages:\n      // the review subprocess writes its own iteration artifacts (iterations/iteration-NNN.md,\n      // deep-review-state.jsonl, review-report.md, resource-map.md) INTO lineageDir, so a\n      // blanket read-only default would break those writes. The lineageDir-only write boundary\n      // is enforced by the prompt ('Do not touch any path outside lineageDir') rather than by a\n      // narrower sandbox; a path-scoped workspace-write would be the stronger fix if the CLIs\n      // exposed one. Callers can still pass an explicit sandboxMode to override.\n      const resolvedSandbox = resolveSandboxMode(lineage.sandboxMode);\n      const resolvedPermission = resolveClaudePermissionMode(lineage.sandboxMode);\n\n      const effectiveSandbox = resolvedSandbox;\n      const effectivePermission = resolvedPermission;\n\n      const { command, args: cmdArgs, input } = buildLineageCommand(\n        lineage,\n        prompt,\n        effectiveSandbox,\n        effectivePermission,\n        {\n          loopType,\n          specFolder,\n          lineageDir,\n          sessionId,\n          convergenceThreshold,\n          stopPolicy,\n          researchTopic,\n        },\n      );\n\n      // Advertise a per-replica state dir hint to the child via SPECKIT_<KIND>_STATE_DIR.\n      // This is DETECTION-ONLY: the native CLIs read their own home env (OPENCODE_HOME /\n      // OPENCODE_HOME / CLAUDE_CODE_HOME), not this var, so it does NOT relocate the\n      // native lockfile. Real same-kind-replica isolation comes from each lineage's\n      // unique artifact dir (lineage.label); remapping the CLI home to isolate the lock\n      // is deliberately avoided here because relocating the home breaks credential/auth\n      // lookup (the \"Not logged in\" failure the dispatch-env allowlist guards against).\n      const stateEnvKey = SPECKIT_STATE_ENV_BY_KIND[lineage.kind];\n      const extraEnv = {\n        SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID: lineage.label,\n        // A fan-out lineage is an orchestrated sub-session running an autonomous\n        // workflow: it has no user turn to answer Gate 3, so the spec-gate must be\n        // fully inert. ENFORCE=0 alone is NOT enough — that only stops the deny, while\n        // the classify step still injects the Gate-3 question, which a cli-opencode\n        // child then answers instead of doing its work. DISABLED makes both classify\n        // and enforce no-ops; AI_SESSION_CHILD lets the worktree wrapper exec in place.\n        // buildExecutorDispatchEnv filters these keys (outside the per-kind allowlist),\n        // so they are re-injected here to reach the child. Harmless for the codex path.\n        MK_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED: '1',\n        AI_SESSION_CHILD: '1',\n        ...(stateEnvKey ? { [stateEnvKey]: stateDir } : {}),\n        ...(lineage.kind === 'cli-claude-code' && lineage.configDir\n          ? { CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR: validateClaudeConfigDir(lineage.configDir) }\n          : {}),\n      };\n\n      // Recursion guard (fail closed): the executor stack can already name the hosting\n      // runtime before the first detached fan-out spawn. The lineage marker is added only\n      // to a spawned seat, so both signals are required to prove that a seat is trying to\n      // fan out its own executor kind again.\n      const inheritedLineageId = process.env.SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID;\n      const isInsideFanoutLineage = typeof inheritedLineageId === 'string'\n        && inheritedLineageId.trim() !== '';\n      if (\n        isInsideFanoutLineage\n        && detectSameKindFromStack(process.env[CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV], lineage.kind)\n      ) {\n        throw new Error(\n          `recursive ${lineage.kind} dispatch blocked for lineage ${lineage.label}: ${lineage.kind} already on ${CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV}`,\n        );\n      }\n\n      // Stamp the dispatch stack with this lineage's executor kind so a seat that\n      // tries to recursively launch the same kind is detectable by the runtime\n      // recursion guard (detectSameKindFromStack reads SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK).\n      // buildExecutorDispatchEnv filters the parent env to the per-kind allowlist,\n      // so the SPECKIT_* lineage/state-dir keys are applied AFTER the filter to\n      // preserve the per-replica lockfile isolation they provide.\n      const dispatchEnv = { ...buildExecutorDispatchEnv(lineage, process.env), ...extraEnv };\n\n      const timeoutMs = computeLineageTimeoutMs(lineage, lineageTimeoutHoursOverride);\n      let lastLineageEventAtMs = Date.now();\n      const markLineageEvent = () => {\n        lastLineageEventAtMs = Date.now();\n      };\n      const stopStallWatchdog = startLineageStallWatchdog({\n        thresholdMs: stallWatchdogMs,\n        label: lineage.label,\n        ledgerPath,\n        getLastEventAtMs: () => lastLineageEventAtMs,\n        getGauges: () => latestGauges,\n      });\n\n      const stopProgressHeartbeat = startLineageProgressHeartbeat({\n        cadenceMs: progressHeartbeatMs,\n        label: lineage.label,\n        ledgerPath,\n        getGauges: () => latestGauges,\n      });\n\n      // A codex leaf runs workspace-write, which can write anywhere in the repo.\n      // Snapshot the out-of-artifact dirty paths BEFORE dispatch so the post-\n      // dispatch guard can isolate the leaf's own NEW out-of-scope writes and\n      // never touch unrelated pre-existing dirty work. Native/cli-opencode/cli-\n      // claude-code lineages are intentionally excluded: their dispatch models may\n      // legitimately write outside lineageDir, and codex is the unguarded path.\n      const containmentEnabled = lineage.kind === 'cli-codex';\n      // Sibling lineages run concurrently and write their own artifacts after this\n      // leaf's baseline is captured. Those writes are indistinguishable from this\n      // leaf's, so treating them as its violations reverts a sibling's legitimate\n      // in-flight work — a completed lineage can be erased by an unrelated leaf\n      // tripping containment. Exclude them from attribution; everything outside\n      // both this leaf's dir and its siblings' stays guarded.\n      const siblingLineageDirs = allLineages\n        .filter((other) => other.label !== lineage.label)\n        .map((other) => path.join(lineagesDir, other.label));\n      const preDispatchDirtyPaths = containmentEnabled\n        ? snapshotOutOfScopeDirtyPaths({\n          repoRoot: process.cwd(),\n          artifactDir: lineageDir,\n          unattributableDirs: siblingLineageDirs,\n        })\n        : [];\n\n      let result;\n      try {\n        result = await runLineageProcess(command, cmdArgs, {\n          cwd: process.cwd(),\n          timeoutMs,\n          env: dispatchEnv,\n          maxBuffer: 20 * 1024 * 1024,\n          abortSignal: context.signal,\n          onOutput: markLineageEvent,\n          onSpawn: ({ pid }) => {\n            lineageProcessLiveness.set(livenessKey, { alive: true, pid });\n          },\n          onExit: ({ pid, exitedAtMs }) => {\n            lineageProcessLiveness.set(livenessKey, { alive: false, pid, exitedAtMs });\n          },\n          ...(typeof input === 'string' ? { input } : {}),\n        });\n      } finally {\n        stopProgressHeartbeat();\n        stopStallWatchdog();\n      }\n\n      // Save subprocess stdout for salvage sweep (write failures in weak CLI executors).\n      const logsDir = path.join(lineageDir, 'logs');\n      fs.mkdirSync(logsDir, { recursive: true });\n      const savedStdout = typeof result.stdout === 'string' ? result.stdout : '';\n      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(logsDir, 'fanout-lineage.out'), savedStdout, 'utf8');\n\n      // Recover missing iteration files from captured stdout when possible. Runs\n      // BEFORE the failure throw below so iteration recovery is never lost.\n      const salvage = runSalvageSweep(lineageDir, loopType, savedStdout);\n      const slotAccounting = buildSlotAccounting(hrStart, slotIntervalMs);\n      lineageSlotAccounting.set(lineage.label, slotAccounting);\n\n      // Structural write-containment for codex leaves: diff the working tree for\n      // NEW out-of-artifact-dir writes, revert exactly those paths, log a\n      // containment_violation event, and fail the iteration fail-closed. The leaf\n      // must still be free to write its iteration file/delta/state record inside\n      // lineageDir; only OUT-of-lineageDir writes are violations. Fails open when\n      // the artifact dir is outside the git worktree (hermetic test lineages).\n      if (containmentEnabled) {\n        const containment = enforceWriteContainment({\n          repoRoot: process.cwd(),\n          artifactDir: lineageDir,\n          unattributableDirs: siblingLineageDirs,\n          preDispatchDirtyPaths,\n          iteration: attempt,\n          label: lineage.label,\n        });\n        if (containment.violations.length > 0) {\n          if (containment.event) {\n            appendFanoutStatusLedger(ledgerPath, {\n              ...containment.event,\n              at: new Date().toISOString(),\n              label: lineage.label,\n              run_id: runId,\n              loop_type: loopType,\n              spec_folder: specFolder,\n              gauges: latestGauges,\n            });\n          }\n          const failure = new Error(\n            `lineage ${lineage.label} violated write containment: reverted `\n              + `${containment.violations.length} out-of-scope path(s): `\n              + `${containment.violations.map((v) => v.path).join(', ')}`,\n          );\n          failure.label = lineage.label;\n          failure.exitCode = 1;\n          failure.timedOut = false;\n          failure.containmentViolation = containment.violations;\n          failure.salvage = salvage;\n          throw failure;\n        }\n      }\n\n      const exitCode = result.status ?? (result.error ? 1 : 0);\n      const timedOut = result.signal === 'SIGTERM';\n      // Any signal-kill is abnormal, not just the orchestrator's own SIGTERM timeout — a\n      // stall-watchdog / lag-ceiling abort or an external SIGKILL leaves result.status null,\n      // so exitCode computes to 0 and the lineage would otherwise be masked as success.\n      const killedBySignal = result.signal != null;\n      const missingArtifacts = findMissingLineageArtifacts(loopType, lineageDir);\n      const stateRead = readLineageStateRecords(loopType, lineageDir);\n      const stopPolicyViolation = findMaxIterationsPolicyViolation({\n        loopType,\n        stateRead,\n        lineage,\n        stopPolicy,\n        lineageDir,\n      });\n\n      // A lineage whose CLI exits non-zero or is killed by the timeout is a FAILURE,\n      // not a success. Throw so the pool settles this item as rejected and counts it\n      // in summary.failed/all_failed, which drives the process exit code. Returning a\n      // plain object here would let the pool record any completed worker as fulfilled\n      // regardless of the underlying CLI exit, masking failed/timed-out lineages.\n      //\n      // Pi is the exception: it returns a non-zero exit code non-deterministically even\n      // on a successful dispatch (identical unauthenticated runs returned 0 then 1), so\n      // for cli-pi a non-zero exit is not a failure signal. The artifact validation below\n      // is its success gate instead — a genuinely failed pi run produces no artifact and\n      // is rejected there. Timeouts and signal kills remain real failures for every kind.\n      const exitCodeIsFailure = exitCode !== 0 && lineage.kind !== 'cli-pi';\n      if (timedOut || killedBySignal || exitCodeIsFailure) {\n        const reason = timedOut\n          ? 'timed out'\n          : killedBySignal\n            ? `killed by signal ${result.signal}`\n            : `exited with code ${exitCode}`;\n        const failure = new Error(`lineage ${lineage.label} ${reason}`);\n        failure.label = lineage.label;\n        failure.exitCode = exitCode;\n        failure.timedOut = timedOut;\n        failure.killedBySignal = killedBySignal;\n        failure.salvage = salvage;\n        throw failure;\n      }\n\n      if (missingArtifacts.length > 0) {\n        const failure = new Error(\n          `lineage ${lineage.label} exited 0 but did not produce expected artifact: ${missingArtifacts.join(', ')}`,\n        );\n        failure.label = lineage.label;\n        failure.exitCode = exitCode;\n        failure.timedOut = false;\n        failure.salvage = { salvaged: salvage.salvaged, failed: Math.max(1, salvage.failed) };\n        failure.missingArtifacts = missingArtifacts;\n        throw failure;\n      }\n\n      if (stopPolicyViolation) {\n        const failure = new Error(\n          `lineage ${lineage.label} violated max-iterations stop policy: ${stopPolicyViolation}`,\n        );\n        failure.label = lineage.label;\n        failure.exitCode = exitCode;\n        failure.timedOut = false;\n        failure.salvage = salvage;\n        failure.stopPolicyViolation = stopPolicyViolation;\n        throw failure;\n      }\n\n      // An exit-0 lineage whose salvage sweep could not recover every iteration\n      // markdown is NOT fulfilled, even when the top-level report exists. Returning\n      // here would let a lineage with a fanout_salvage_failed marker pass as complete,\n      // dropping durable per-iteration evidence from merge/synthesis. Throw so the\n      // pool retries it (the classifier maps salvage.failed > 0 to artifact_miss).\n      if (salvage && salvage.failed > 0) {\n        const failure = new Error(\n          `lineage ${lineage.label} exited 0 but ${salvage.failed} iteration markdown file(s) were unrecoverable`,\n        );\n        failure.label = lineage.label;\n        failure.exitCode = exitCode;\n        failure.timedOut = false;\n        failure.salvage = { salvaged: salvage.salvaged, failed: salvage.failed };\n        failure.missingArtifacts = [];\n        throw failure;\n      }\n\n      const output = { label: lineage.label, exitCode, timedOut, salvage, ...slotAccounting };\n      if (stateRead.statePath && !stateRead.missing && !stateRead.parseError) {\n        const slotWindowEndIso = new Date().toISOString();\n        try {\n          const timestampCheck = checkLineageTimestampWindow(stateRead.records, {\n            windowStart: slotWindowStartIso,\n            windowEnd: slotWindowEndIso,\n            toleranceMs: DEFAULT_LINEAGE_TIMESTAMP_TOLERANCE_MS,\n          });\n          if (timestampCheck.anomalous > 0) {\n            const timestampAnomaly = buildTimestampAnomalyPayload({\n              lineage,\n              statePath: stateRead.statePath,\n              check: timestampCheck,\n            });\n            appendFanoutStatusLedger(ledgerPath, {\n              event: 'timestamp_anomaly',\n              status: 'warning',\n              severity: 'warning',\n              label: lineage.label,\n              at: new Date().toISOString(),\n              ...timestampAnomaly,\n            });\n            output.timestamp_anomaly = timestampAnomaly;\n          }\n        } catch {\n          // Timestamp telemetry is advisory and cannot affect lineage fulfillment.\n        }\n      }\n\n      return output;\n    },\n  });\n\n  const timestampAnomalies = collectTimestampAnomalies(results);\n  const finalSummary = timestampAnomalies.length > 0\n    ? { ...summary, timestamp_anomalies: timestampAnomalies }\n    : summary;\n\n  writeOrchestrationSummary(summaryPath, {\n    run_id: runId,\n    loop_type: loopType,\n    spec_folder: specFolder,\n    base_artifact_dir: baseArtifactDir,\n    total_cli_lineages: cliLineages.length,\n    orphaned_lineages: orphanedLineages,\n    ...finalSummary,\n  });\n\n  const exitCode = finalSummary.all_failed ? 3 : finalSummary.failed > 0 ? 2 : 0;\n  jsonOut({ status: exitCode === 0 ? 'ok' : 'partial', run_id: runId, results, summary: finalSummary });\n  process.exit(exitCode);\n}\n\nif (require.main === module && isTsxLoaded) {\n  main().catch((err) => {\n    const code = classifyExitCode(err);\n    jsonOut({\n      status: 'error',\n      error: err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err),\n      code: err && err.code ? err.code : 'SCRIPT_ERROR',\n    });\n    if (code === 1) {\n      process.stderr.write(\n        JSON.stringify({ error: err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err), stack: err && err.stack }) + '\\n',\n      );\n    }\n    process.exit(code);\n  });\n}\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  DEVIN_ALLOWED_MODELS,\n  DEVIN_DEFAULT_MODEL,\n  CURSOR_ALLOWED_MODELS,\n  CURSOR_DEFAULT_MODEL,\n  PI_ALLOWED_MODELS,\n  PI_DEFAULT_MODEL,\n  buildLineageCommand,\n  buildInvocationFingerprintPayload,\n  isCodexBinaryAvailable,\n  isCursorBinaryAvailable,\n  isDevinBinaryAvailable,\n  isPiBinaryAvailable,\n  buildLoopPrompt,\n  findMaxIterationsPolicyViolation,\n  isMaxIterationsStopReason,\n  computeLineageTimeoutMs,\n  assertLineageTimeoutHoursOverrideWithinCeiling,\n  computeLineageBudgetUpperBound,\n  evaluateLineageBudgetCap,\n  computeAggregateBudgetUpperBound,\n  evaluateAggregateBudgetCap,\n  normalizeAggregateBudgetGuards,\n  normalizeProgressHeartbeatMs,\n  normalizePostExitGraceMs,\n  normalizeLineageBudgetGuards,\n  normalizeStallWatchdogMs,\n  computeSkippedCount,\n  decorateSlotAccountingEvent,\n  startLineageProgressHeartbeat,\n  startLineageStallWatchdog,\n  statusForLedgerEvent,\n  updateLineageSnapshot,\n  applyFlatPoolAssignmentGuard,\n};","lineStart":2260,"lineEnd":2648,"totalLines":2648,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs","time":{"start":1785758154563,"end":1785758154571}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b0bd10ae4263ca9016a7081c9a98881918ce009d2fba2d457"}},"id":"prt_fc77afbf4001lv70GBW0YqkG4M","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77aee1c0014Qi3O0kyIuOd8O"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1785758155916,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"id":"prt_fc77b0489001eoyvDhAWYUHhUT","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","messageID":"msg_fc77aee1c0014Qi3O0kyIuOd8O","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":177579,"input":18265,"output":62,"reasoning":20,"cache":{"write":0,"read":159232}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1785758162413,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"id":"prt_fc77b1deb001g2PidwyS4Dmk5f","messageID":"msg_fc77b0949001hmcFJW44pOnps0","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758172364,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_Du1oDSgmfGwmiu84VIxfUyrR","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts","offset":1560,"limit":180},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1560:     ], { env: { PATH: `${binDir}:${process.env.PATH ?? ''}` } });\n1561: \n1562:     expect(result.exitCode).toBe(3);\n1563:     expect(result.stdout).toContain(\"policy 'cached' is not supported by executor kind 'cli-opencode'\");\n1564:     expect(existsSync(markerPath)).toBe(false);\n1565:     expect(existsSync(join(baseDir, 'lineages'))).toBe(false);\n1566:     expect(existsSync(join(baseDir, 'orchestration-status.log'))).toBe(false);\n1567:     expect(existsSync(join(baseDir, 'orchestration-summary.json'))).toBe(false);\n1568:   });\n1569: \n1570:   it('feeds a deterministic 2-model by 3-branch by 2-replica manifest into the existing pool', async () => {\n1571:     const binDir = makeTempDir('fanout-run-manifest-bin-');\n1572:     writeStubBinary(binDir, 'opencode');\n1573:     const baseDir = makeTempDir('fanout-run-manifest-base-');\n1574:     const expectedLabels = [\n1575:       'discover-sol-r1', 'discover-sol-r2',\n1576:       'challenge-sol-r1', 'challenge-sol-r2',\n1577:       'synthesize-sol-r1', 'synthesize-sol-r2',\n1578:       'discover-glm-r1', 'discover-glm-r2',\n1579:       'challenge-glm-r1', 'challenge-glm-r2',\n1580:       'synthesize-glm-r1', 'synthesize-glm-r2',\n1581:     ];\n1582:     const fanoutConfig = JSON.stringify({\n1583:       models: [\n1584:         { id: 'sol', kind: 'cli-opencode', model: 'opencode-go/sol', liveTools: { webSearch: 'live' } },\n1585:         { id: 'glm', kind: 'cli-opencode', model: 'opencode-go/glm', liveTools: { webSearch: 'live' } },\n1586:       ],\n1587:       branches: [\n1588:         { id: 'discover', iterations: 1 },\n1589:         { id: 'challenge', iterations: 1 },\n1590:         { id: 'synthesize', iterations: 1 },\n1591:       ],\n1592:       replicas: 2,\n1593:       concurrency: 2,\n1594:       maxRetries: 0,\n1595:     });\n1596: \n1597:     const { result } = await spawnFanout('cartesian-manifest-dispatch', [\n1598:       '--spec-folder',\n1599:       'specs/test-fanout-manifest',\n1600:       '--loop-type',\n1601:       'research',\n1602:       '--fanout-config-json',\n1603:       fanoutConfig,\n1604:       '--base-artifact-dir',\n1605:       baseDir,\n1606:     ], { env: { PATH: `${binDir}:${process.env.PATH ?? ''}` }, timeoutMs: 30_000 });\n1607: \n1608:     expect(result.exitCode).toBe(0);\n1609:     for (const label of expectedLabels) {\n1610:       expect(existsSync(join(baseDir, 'lineages', label, 'research.md'))).toBe(true);\n1611:     }\n1612:     const payload = JSON.parse(result.stdout.split('\\n').filter(Boolean).at(-1) ?? '{}') as {\n1613:       results?: Array<{ output?: { label?: string } }>;\n1614:       summary?: { total?: number; succeeded?: number; failed?: number };\n1615:     };\n1616:     expect(payload.summary).toMatchObject({ total: 12, succeeded: 12, failed: 0 });\n1617:     expect(payload.results?.map((entry) => entry.output?.label)).toEqual(expectedLabels);\n1618:   });\n1619: });\n1620: \n1621: describe('fanout-run.cjs — buildLoopPrompt identity wording', () => {\n1622:   const { buildLoopPrompt } = requireCjs(fanoutRunScript) as {\n1623:     buildLoopPrompt: (\n1624:       loopType: 'research' | 'review',\n1625:       specFolder: string,\n1626:       lineageDir: string,\n1627:       sessionId: string,\n1628:       lineage: { kind: 'cli-opencode'; label: string; model?: string },\n1629:       researchTopic?: string,\n1630:       options?: { stopPolicy?: string; convergenceThreshold?: number },\n1631:     ) => string;\n1632:   };\n1633: \n1634:   it('does not claim LEAF-agent identity while preserving loop phase instructions', () => {\n1635:     for (const [loopType, agentName] of [\n1636:       ['research', 'deep-research'],\n1637:       ['review', 'deep-review'],\n1638:     ] as const) {\n1639:       const prompt = buildLoopPrompt(\n1640:         loopType,\n1641:         'specs/test-fanout-loop-identity',\n1642:         `/tmp/fanout-${loopType}-lineage`,\n1643:         `fanout-${loopType}-run-123`,\n1644:         { kind: 'cli-opencode', label: `${loopType}-seat`, model: 'opencode-go/glm-5.1' },\n1645:         loopType === 'research' ? 'test research topic' : undefined,\n1646:       );\n1647: \n1648:       expect(prompt).not.toContain(`You are a ${agentName} agent`);\n1649:       expect(prompt).not.toContain(`${agentName} agent running a fan-out lineage`);\n1650:       expect(prompt).toContain(\n1651:         `You are orchestrating the ${agentName} workflow YAML as a detached fan-out lineage.`,\n1652:       );\n1653:       expect(prompt).toContain(\n1654:         'Run phase_init, phase_main_loop (to legal convergence), and phase_synthesis.',\n1655:       );\n1656:     }\n1657:   });\n1658: \n1659:   it('rejects deprecated context fan-out prompt construction', () => {\n1660:     expect(() => buildLoopPrompt(\n1661:       'context' as never,\n1662:       'specs/test-fanout-loop-identity',\n1663:       '/tmp/fanout-context-lineage',\n1664:       'fanout-context-run-123',\n1665:       { kind: 'cli-opencode', label: 'context-seat', model: 'opencode-go/glm-5.1' },\n1666:     )).toThrow(/context fan-out is deprecated/);\n1667:   });\n1668: });\n1669: \n1670: describe('fanout-run.cjs — review session id propagation templates', () => {\n1671:   const { buildLineageCommand } = requireCjs(fanoutRunScript) as {\n1672:     buildLineageCommand: (\n1673:       lineage: { kind: 'native'; iterations?: number },\n1674:       prompt: string,\n1675:       resolvedSandbox: string,\n1676:       resolvedPermission: string,\n1677:       options: {\n1678:         loopType: 'review';\n1679:         specFolder: string;\n1680:         lineageDir: string;\n1681:         sessionId?: string;\n1682:       },\n1683:     ) => { command: string; args: string[]; input: string };\n1684:   };\n1685: \n1686:   it('uses a supplied session_id for review init artifacts and preserves the timestamp fallback', () => {\n1687:     const suppliedSessionId = 'fanout-lineage-a-run-123';\n1688: \n1689:     for (const workflowPath of reviewWorkflowPaths) {\n1690:       expect(renderReviewInitSessionIds(workflowPath, suppliedSessionId)).toEqual({\n1691:         config: suppliedSessionId,\n1692:         stateLog: suppliedSessionId,\n1693:         findingsRegistry: suppliedSessionId,\n1694:       });\n1695:       expect(renderReviewInitSessionIds(workflowPath)).toEqual({\n1696:         config: '2035-02-03T04:05:06.000Z',\n1697:         stateLog: '2035-02-03T04:05:06.000Z',\n1698:         findingsRegistry: '2035-02-03T04:05:06.000Z',\n1699:       });\n1700:     }\n1701: \n1702:     const withSession = buildLineageCommand(\n1703:       { kind: 'native', iterations: 2 },\n1704:       '',\n1705:       'workspace-write',\n1706:       'default',\n1707:       {\n1708:         loopType: 'review',\n1709:         specFolder: 'specs/test-session-id',\n1710:         lineageDir: '/tmp/fanout-lineage-a',\n1711:         sessionId: suppliedSessionId,\n1712:       },\n1713:     );\n1714:     const withoutSession = buildLineageCommand(\n1715:       { kind: 'native', iterations: 2 },\n1716:       '',\n1717:       'workspace-write',\n1718:       'default',\n1719:       {\n1720:         loopType: 'review',\n1721:         specFolder: 'specs/test-session-id',\n1722:         lineageDir: '/tmp/fanout-lineage-a',\n1723:       },\n1724:     );\n1725: \n1726:     expect(withSession.args.at(-1)).toContain(`session_id: ${suppliedSessionId}`);\n1727:     expect(withoutSession.args.at(-1)).not.toContain('session_id:');\n1728:   });\n1729: });\n1730: \n1731: describe('fanout-run.cjs — module basics', () => {\n1732:   it('exits 0 and emits ok JSON for native fanout through opencode command dispatch', async () => {\n1733:     const binDir = makeTempDir('fanout-run-native-bin-');\n1734:     writeNativeOpencodeStubBinary(binDir);\n1735:     const baseDir = makeTempDir('fanout-run-native-');\n1736:     const nativeOnlyConfig = JSON.stringify({\n1737:       executors: [{ label: 'native-a', kind: 'native', count: 1 }],\n1738:       concurrency: 2,\n1739:     });\n\n(Showing lines 1560-1739 of 3230. Use offset=1740 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"    ], { env: { PATH: `${binDir}:${process.env.PATH ?? ''}` } });\n\n    expect(result.exitCode).toBe(3);\n    expect(result.stdout).toContain(\"policy 'cached' is not supported by executor kind 'cli-opencode'\");\n    expect(existsSync(markerPath)).toBe(false);\n    expect(existsSync(join(baseDir, 'lineages'))).toBe(false);\n    expect(existsSync(join(baseDir, 'orchestration-status.log'))).toBe(false);\n    expect(existsSync(join(baseDir, 'orchestration-summary.json'))).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it('feeds a deterministic 2-model by 3-branch by 2-replica manifest into the existing pool', async () => {\n    const binDir = makeTempDir('fanout-run-manifest-bin-');\n    writeStubBinary(binDir, 'opencode');\n    const baseDir = makeTempDir('fanout-run-manifest-base-');\n    const expectedLabels = [\n      'discover-sol-r1', 'discover-sol-r2',\n      'challenge-sol-r1', 'challenge-sol-r2',\n      'synthesize-sol-r1', 'synthesize-sol-r2',\n      'discover-glm-r1', 'discover-glm-r2',\n      'challenge-glm-r1', 'challenge-glm-r2',","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts","text":"    ], { env: { PATH: `${binDir}:${process.env.PATH ?? ''}` } });\n\n    expect(result.exitCode).toBe(3);\n    expect(result.stdout).toContain(\"policy 'cached' is not supported by executor kind 'cli-opencode'\");\n    expect(existsSync(markerPath)).toBe(false);\n    expect(existsSync(join(baseDir, 'lineages'))).toBe(false);\n    expect(existsSync(join(baseDir, 'orchestration-status.log'))).toBe(false);\n    expect(existsSync(join(baseDir, 'orchestration-summary.json'))).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it('feeds a deterministic 2-model by 3-branch by 2-replica manifest into the existing pool', async () => {\n    const binDir = makeTempDir('fanout-run-manifest-bin-');\n    writeStubBinary(binDir, 'opencode');\n    const baseDir = makeTempDir('fanout-run-manifest-base-');\n    const expectedLabels = [\n      'discover-sol-r1', 'discover-sol-r2',\n      'challenge-sol-r1', 'challenge-sol-r2',\n      'synthesize-sol-r1', 'synthesize-sol-r2',\n      'discover-glm-r1', 'discover-glm-r2',\n      'challenge-glm-r1', 'challenge-glm-r2',\n      'synthesize-glm-r1', 'synthesize-glm-r2',\n    ];\n    const fanoutConfig = JSON.stringify({\n      models: [\n        { id: 'sol', kind: 'cli-opencode', model: 'opencode-go/sol', liveTools: { webSearch: 'live' } },\n        { id: 'glm', kind: 'cli-opencode', model: 'opencode-go/glm', liveTools: { webSearch: 'live' } },\n      ],\n      branches: [\n        { id: 'discover', iterations: 1 },\n        { id: 'challenge', iterations: 1 },\n        { id: 'synthesize', iterations: 1 },\n      ],\n      replicas: 2,\n      concurrency: 2,\n      maxRetries: 0,\n    });\n\n    const { result } = await spawnFanout('cartesian-manifest-dispatch', [\n      '--spec-folder',\n      'specs/test-fanout-manifest',\n      '--loop-type',\n      'research',\n      '--fanout-config-json',\n      fanoutConfig,\n      '--base-artifact-dir',\n      baseDir,\n    ], { env: { PATH: `${binDir}:${process.env.PATH ?? ''}` }, timeoutMs: 30_000 });\n\n    expect(result.exitCode).toBe(0);\n    for (const label of expectedLabels) {\n      expect(existsSync(join(baseDir, 'lineages', label, 'research.md'))).toBe(true);\n    }\n    const payload = JSON.parse(result.stdout.split('\\n').filter(Boolean).at(-1) ?? '{}') as {\n      results?: Array<{ output?: { label?: string } }>;\n      summary?: { total?: number; succeeded?: number; failed?: number };\n    };\n    expect(payload.summary).toMatchObject({ total: 12, succeeded: 12, failed: 0 });\n    expect(payload.results?.map((entry) => entry.output?.label)).toEqual(expectedLabels);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('fanout-run.cjs — buildLoopPrompt identity wording', () => {\n  const { buildLoopPrompt } = requireCjs(fanoutRunScript) as {\n    buildLoopPrompt: (\n      loopType: 'research' | 'review',\n      specFolder: string,\n      lineageDir: string,\n      sessionId: string,\n      lineage: { kind: 'cli-opencode'; label: string; model?: string },\n      researchTopic?: string,\n      options?: { stopPolicy?: string; convergenceThreshold?: number },\n    ) => string;\n  };\n\n  it('does not claim LEAF-agent identity while preserving loop phase instructions', () => {\n    for (const [loopType, agentName] of [\n      ['research', 'deep-research'],\n      ['review', 'deep-review'],\n    ] as const) {\n      const prompt = buildLoopPrompt(\n        loopType,\n        'specs/test-fanout-loop-identity',\n        `/tmp/fanout-${loopType}-lineage`,\n        `fanout-${loopType}-run-123`,\n        { kind: 'cli-opencode', label: `${loopType}-seat`, model: 'opencode-go/glm-5.1' },\n        loopType === 'research' ? 'test research topic' : undefined,\n      );\n\n      expect(prompt).not.toContain(`You are a ${agentName} agent`);\n      expect(prompt).not.toContain(`${agentName} agent running a fan-out lineage`);\n      expect(prompt).toContain(\n        `You are orchestrating the ${agentName} workflow YAML as a detached fan-out lineage.`,\n      );\n      expect(prompt).toContain(\n        'Run phase_init, phase_main_loop (to legal convergence), and phase_synthesis.',\n      );\n    }\n  });\n\n  it('rejects deprecated context fan-out prompt construction', () => {\n    expect(() => buildLoopPrompt(\n      'context' as never,\n      'specs/test-fanout-loop-identity',\n      '/tmp/fanout-context-lineage',\n      'fanout-context-run-123',\n      { kind: 'cli-opencode', label: 'context-seat', model: 'opencode-go/glm-5.1' },\n    )).toThrow(/context fan-out is deprecated/);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('fanout-run.cjs — review session id propagation templates', () => {\n  const { buildLineageCommand } = requireCjs(fanoutRunScript) as {\n    buildLineageCommand: (\n      lineage: { kind: 'native'; iterations?: number },\n      prompt: string,\n      resolvedSandbox: string,\n      resolvedPermission: string,\n      options: {\n        loopType: 'review';\n        specFolder: string;\n        lineageDir: string;\n        sessionId?: string;\n      },\n    ) => { command: string; args: string[]; input: string };\n  };\n\n  it('uses a supplied session_id for review init artifacts and preserves the timestamp fallback', () => {\n    const suppliedSessionId = 'fanout-lineage-a-run-123';\n\n    for (const workflowPath of reviewWorkflowPaths) {\n      expect(renderReviewInitSessionIds(workflowPath, suppliedSessionId)).toEqual({\n        config: suppliedSessionId,\n        stateLog: suppliedSessionId,\n        findingsRegistry: suppliedSessionId,\n      });\n      expect(renderReviewInitSessionIds(workflowPath)).toEqual({\n        config: '2035-02-03T04:05:06.000Z',\n        stateLog: '2035-02-03T04:05:06.000Z',\n        findingsRegistry: '2035-02-03T04:05:06.000Z',\n      });\n    }\n\n    const withSession = buildLineageCommand(\n      { kind: 'native', iterations: 2 },\n      '',\n      'workspace-write',\n      'default',\n      {\n        loopType: 'review',\n        specFolder: 'specs/test-session-id',\n        lineageDir: '/tmp/fanout-lineage-a',\n        sessionId: suppliedSessionId,\n      },\n    );\n    const withoutSession = buildLineageCommand(\n      { kind: 'native', iterations: 2 },\n      '',\n      'workspace-write',\n      'default',\n      {\n        loopType: 'review',\n        specFolder: 'specs/test-session-id',\n        lineageDir: '/tmp/fanout-lineage-a',\n      },\n    );\n\n    expect(withSession.args.at(-1)).toContain(`session_id: ${suppliedSessionId}`);\n    expect(withoutSession.args.at(-1)).not.toContain('session_id:');\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('fanout-run.cjs — module basics', () => {\n  it('exits 0 and emits ok JSON for native fanout through opencode command dispatch', async () => {\n    const binDir = makeTempDir('fanout-run-native-bin-');\n    writeNativeOpencodeStubBinary(binDir);\n    const baseDir = makeTempDir('fanout-run-native-');\n    const nativeOnlyConfig = JSON.stringify({\n      executors: [{ label: 'native-a', kind: 'native', count: 1 }],\n      concurrency: 2,\n    });","lineStart":1560,"lineEnd":1739,"totalLines":3230,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts","time":{"start":1785758172351,"end":1785758172361}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0740dd26755560fe016a7081dc2b4c8191b93406a5a8aa334c"}},"id":"prt_fc77b44bc001yfrg2b8Dqgh1I1","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77b0949001hmcFJW44pOnps0"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758172379,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_kDvgRwPLw7LLn1eP3QtC5gsw","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"buildLoopPrompt|executor: cli-opencode|This is an explicit parallel-detached","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests"},"output":"Found 9 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/workflow-session-id-parity.vitest.ts:\n  Line 26:   readonly buildLoopPrompt: (\n\n  Line 176:     const { buildLoopPrompt } = requireCjs(FANOUT_RUN_SCRIPT) as FanoutRunExports;\n\n  Line 180:       const prompt = buildLoopPrompt(\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts:\n  Line 1621: describe('fanout-run.cjs — buildLoopPrompt identity wording', () => {\n\n  Line 1622:   const { buildLoopPrompt } = requireCjs(fanoutRunScript) as {\n\n  Line 1623:     buildLoopPrompt: (\n\n  Line 1639:       const prompt = buildLoopPrompt(\n\n  Line 1660:     expect(() => buildLoopPrompt(\n\n  Line 3009: describe('fanout-run.cjs — buildLineageCommand / buildLoopPrompt via echo stub', () => {\n","metadata":{"matches":9,"truncated":false},"title":"buildLoopPrompt|executor: cli-opencode|This is an explicit parallel-detached","time":{"start":1785758172347,"end":1785758172365}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0740dd26755560fe016a7081dc2b388191bd3c9a73546f04ad"}},"id":"prt_fc77b446a001K4TxswE62TEIia","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77b0949001hmcFJW44pOnps0"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758172387,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_gkkjpCLbgJuaooJ51SFrBbJY","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts","offset":1,"limit":280},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Deep-Loop Executor Config\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: import { z } from 'zod';\n6: \n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: // 1. TYPE DEFINITIONS\n9: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: \n11: export const EXECUTOR_KINDS = ['native', 'cli-codex', 'cli-claude-code', 'cli-opencode', 'cli-cursor', 'cli-devin', 'cli-pi'] as const;\n12: export type ExecutorKind = typeof EXECUTOR_KINDS[number];\n13: \n14: // Ordered low→high. `ultra` is codex gpt-5.6-sol's top reasoning tier, above `max`.\n15: export const REASONING_EFFORTS = ['none', 'minimal', 'low', 'medium', 'high', 'xhigh', 'max', 'ultra'] as const;\n16: export type ReasoningEffort = typeof REASONING_EFFORTS[number];\n17: \n18: export const SERVICE_TIERS = ['priority', 'standard', 'fast'] as const;\n19: export type ServiceTier = typeof SERVICE_TIERS[number];\n20: \n21: export const WEB_SEARCH_POLICIES = ['inherit', 'disabled', 'cached', 'live'] as const;\n22: export type WebSearchPolicy = typeof WEB_SEARCH_POLICIES[number];\n23: \n24: /** Live-tool policies resolved for one executor invocation. */\n25: export interface LiveToolsConfig {\n26:   readonly webSearch: WebSearchPolicy;\n27: }\n28: \n29: /** Fan-out assignment models accepted by the schema. */\n30: export const FANOUT_ASSIGNMENT_MODELS = ['flat_pool', 'wave'] as const;\n31: \n32: /** Fan-out assignment model selected for a lineage or fan-out block. */\n33: export type FanoutAssignmentModel = typeof FANOUT_ASSIGNMENT_MODELS[number];\n34: \n35: const SANDBOX_MODES = ['read-only', 'workspace-write', 'danger-full-access'] as const;\n36: export type SandboxMode = typeof SANDBOX_MODES[number];\n37: export type ClaudePermissionMode = 'plan' | 'acceptEdits' | 'bypassPermissions';\n38: \n39: /**\n40:  * Cursor's real approval-flag family (live-verified against the installed CLI):\n41:  * `plan` is Cursor's `--mode plan` read-only/planning mode (reads allowed,\n42:  * edits/shell blocked), `auto-review` is `--auto-review` (\"Smart Auto\"), and\n43:  * `force` is `--force`/`--yolo` (\"Run Everything\"). The fan-out never selects\n44:  * `auto-review`: Smart Auto prompts for tool calls it deems unsafe, and a\n45:  * non-interactive leaf has no stdin to answer, so it could block until the\n46:  * lineage timeout — both write modes use `force` instead.\n47:  */\n48: export type CursorApprovalMode = 'plan' | 'auto-review' | 'force';\n49: \n50: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n51: // 2. CONSTANTS\n52: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n53: \n54: export const liveToolsSchema = z.object({\n55:   webSearch: z.enum(WEB_SEARCH_POLICIES).default('inherit'),\n56: }).default({ webSearch: 'inherit' });\n57: \n58: export const executorConfigSchema = z.object({\n59:   kind: z.enum(EXECUTOR_KINDS).default('native'),\n60:   model: z.string().min(1).nullable().default(null),\n61:   configDir: z.string().trim().min(1).nullable().default(null),\n62:   reasoningEffort: z.enum(REASONING_EFFORTS).nullable().default(null),\n63:   serviceTier: z.enum(SERVICE_TIERS).nullable().default(null),\n64:   sandboxMode: z.enum(SANDBOX_MODES).nullable().default(null),\n65:   // Hard ceiling of 1 hour per iteration: bounds a single executor invocation so a\n66:   // runaway per-iteration call cannot by itself consume the whole autonomous lifetime budget.\n67:   timeoutSeconds: z.number().int().positive().max(3600).default(900),\n68:   // Optional fable-5 governor capsule for this executor's prompts. Universal and\n69:   // kind-agnostic on purpose: intentionally absent from EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT\n70:   // and the unsupported-field scan, so any executor kind may carry it. null = none.\n71:   governor: z.string().min(1).nullable().default(null),\n72:   liveTools: liveToolsSchema,\n73: });\n74: \n75: export type ExecutorConfig = z.infer<typeof executorConfigSchema>;\n76: \n77: export const EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT: Record<ExecutorKind, readonly (keyof ExecutorConfig)[]> = {\n78:   native: ['liveTools'],\n79:   'cli-codex': ['model', 'reasoningEffort', 'serviceTier', 'sandboxMode', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n80:   'cli-claude-code': ['model', 'configDir', 'reasoningEffort', 'sandboxMode', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n81:   'cli-opencode': ['model', 'reasoningEffort', 'sandboxMode', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n82:   // No reasoningEffort: the live cursor-agent CLI (2026.07.23-e383d2b) rejects the\n83:   // parameterized `model[effort=...]` bracket outright (\"Cannot use this model\"),\n84:   // confirmed live 2026-07-24 — effort tiers are baked into the model id itself\n85:   // (e.g. `gpt-5.2-high`), not a separate flag. No configDir: no confirmed Cursor\n86:   // CLI flag isolates the shared `.cursor/` config dir (open question, deferred).\n87:   'cli-cursor': ['model', 'sandboxMode', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n88:   // No reasoningEffort and no serviceTier: `devin --help` (live 2026-07-27) lists\n89:   // only --model, --permission-mode, --sandbox, and --config. Both thinking tier\n90:   // and priority routing are baked into the model uid instead — `glm-5-2` vs\n91:   // `glm-5-2-max`, `gpt-5-6-sol-high` vs `gpt-5-6-sol-high-priority` — so neither\n92:   // is a separate flag. No configDir: --config takes a config *file* path\n93:   // (~/.config/devin/config.json), not a home directory, so it does not fit the\n94:   // configDir contract the way CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR does.\n95:   'cli-devin': ['model', 'sandboxMode', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n96:   // Pi exposes reasoning as a first-class `--thinking` flag (off..max), independent\n97:   // of the model id, so reasoningEffort is forwarded; it has no OS sandbox or\n98:   // service-tier surface, so neither sandboxMode nor serviceTier is supported.\n99:   'cli-pi': ['model', 'reasoningEffort', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n100: };\n101: \n102: /** Proven web-search policies for every shipped executor kind. */\n103: export const EXECUTOR_WEB_SEARCH_CAPABILITY_MATRIX = {\n104:   native: {\n105:     inherit: true,\n106:     disabled: false,\n107:     cached: false,\n108:     live: false,\n109:   },\n110:   'cli-codex': {\n111:     inherit: true,\n112:     disabled: true,\n113:     cached: false,\n114:     live: true,\n115:   },\n116:   'cli-claude-code': {\n117:     inherit: true,\n118:     disabled: false,\n119:     cached: false,\n120:     live: false,\n121:   },\n122:   'cli-opencode': {\n123:     inherit: true,\n124:     disabled: false,\n125:     cached: false,\n126:     live: true,\n127:   },\n128:   // No confirmed cursor-agent web-search flag (checked live, 2026-07-24): same\n129:   // flag-less shape as cli-claude-code — inherit only, nothing enforceable.\n130:   'cli-cursor': {\n131:     inherit: true,\n132:     disabled: false,\n133:     cached: false,\n134:     live: false,\n135:   },\n136:   // No web-search flag in `devin --help` (checked live 2026-07-27): same\n137:   // flag-less shape as cli-cursor and cli-claude-code — inherit only, nothing\n138:   // enforceable either way.\n139:   'cli-devin': {\n140:     inherit: true,\n141:     disabled: false,\n142:     cached: false,\n143:     live: false,\n144:   },\n145:   'cli-pi': {\n146:     inherit: true,\n147:     disabled: false,\n148:     cached: false,\n149:     live: false,\n150:   },\n151: } as const satisfies Record<ExecutorKind, Record<WebSearchPolicy, boolean>>;\n152: \n153: /**\n154:  * Pi is a provider pass-through with no house model. Keep dispatch scoped to\n155:  * the operator-confirmed picker roster so generic provider routing cannot broaden it.\n156:  */\n157: export const PI_SUPPORTED_MODELS = [\n158:   'deepseek-v4-pro',\n159:   'deepseek-v4-flash',\n160:   'minimax-m3',\n161:   'gpt-5.6-luna',\n162:   'gpt-5.6-sol',\n163:   'gpt-5.6-terra',\n164:   'mimo-v2.5-pro',\n165:   'mimo-v2.5-pro-ultraspeed',\n166: ] as const;\n167: export type PiSupportedModel = typeof PI_SUPPORTED_MODELS[number];\n168: \n169: /** Use the registry's first-listed, broadly adopted rotation model as the stable default; this is not Pi-specific usage history. */\n170: export const PI_DEFAULT_MODEL: PiSupportedModel = 'deepseek-v4-pro';\n171: \n172: /** True when `model` is in the enforced cli-pi allowlist. */\n173: export function isPiModelAllowed(model: string): model is PiSupportedModel {\n174:   return (PI_SUPPORTED_MODELS as readonly string[]).includes(model);\n175: }\n176: \n177: /**\n178:  * Enforced allowlist of cursor-agent --model ids. Cursor's live roster spans\n179:  * 150+ hosted-frontier ids across GPT/Claude/Gemini/Grok/GLM/Kimi families,\n180:  * with no per-model prompt-craft data for almost all of them and ids that\n181:  * drift over time — dispatch is scoped to this curated set only, confirmed\n182:  * live via `cursor-agent --list-models` (2026-07-24, account\n183:  * mkerkmeester@proton.me, cursor-agent 2026.07.23-e383d2b; no id here was\n184:  * ever fabricated). This is a hard gate, not a typo-checked reference: any\n185:  * caller-supplied model outside this set must be rejected before a command\n186:  * is constructed. `auto` (Cursor's own router) is deliberately excluded — it\n187:  * can silently resolve to a model outside this allowlist, defeating the\n188:  * point of enforcing one.\n189:  */\n190: export const CURSOR_SUPPORTED_MODELS = [\n191:   'cursor-grok-4.5-low',\n192:   'cursor-grok-4.5-low-fast',\n193:   'cursor-grok-4.5-medium',\n194:   'cursor-grok-4.5-medium-fast',\n195:   'cursor-grok-4.5-high',\n196:   'cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast',\n197:   'composer-2.5',\n198:   'composer-2.5-fast',\n199:   'glm-5.2-high',\n200:   'glm-5.2-max',\n201: ] as const;\n202: export type CursorSupportedModel = typeof CURSOR_SUPPORTED_MODELS[number];\n203: \n204: /** Default model when a cli-cursor dispatch omits one — Cursor's own native model, now that `auto` is no longer an allowed id. */\n205: export const CURSOR_DEFAULT_MODEL: CursorSupportedModel = 'composer-2.5';\n206: \n207: /** True when `model` is in the enforced cli-cursor allowlist. */\n208: export function isCursorModelAllowed(model: string): model is CursorSupportedModel {\n209:   return (CURSOR_SUPPORTED_MODELS as readonly string[]).includes(model);\n210: }\n211: \n212: /**\n213:  * Enforced allowlist of devin --model ids. Devin exposes 37 model families and\n214:  * accepts a family slug, an alias, or a full model uid, which is far more\n215:  * surface than deep-loop dispatch needs or has prompt-craft data for. This set\n216:  * is the curated four-family scope: GLM-5.2, SWE-1.7, Grok 4.5, and DeepSeek.\n217:  * Every entry was read from the live `devin models list` — no id here was\n218:  * inferred from documentation.\n219:  *\n220:  * Tier naming matters and is easy to get wrong: `glm-5-2` is \"GLM-5.2 High\" and\n221:  * is the free tier, while `glm-5-2-max` is the separate paid \"GLM-5.2 Max\"\n222:  * tier. The skill's reference table lists these uids without their tier names,\n223:  * so read the live list rather than the doc when picking one.\n224:  */\n225: export const DEVIN_SUPPORTED_MODELS = [\n226:   // SWE-1.7 default alias.\n227:   'swe',\n228:   // GLM-5.2 uids. `glm-5-2` = \"GLM-5.2 High\" [200K, Free].\n229:   'glm-5-2',\n230:   'glm-5-2-max',\n231:   'glm-5-2-1m',\n232:   'glm-5-2-max-1m',\n233:   'glm-5-2-none',\n234:   'glm-5-2-none-1m',\n235:   // SWE-1.7 tier uids.\n236:   'swe-1-7',\n237:   'swe-1-7-medium',\n238:   'swe-1-7-lightning',\n239:   // Grok 4.5 tier uids read from the live `devin models list`.\n240:   'grok-4-5-low',\n241:   'grok-4-5-medium',\n242:   'grok-4-5-high',\n243:   // DeepSeek family slug and model uid read from the live `devin models list`.\n244:   'deepseek-v4-pro',\n245:   'deepseek-v4',\n246: ] as const;\n247: export type DevinSupportedModel = typeof DEVIN_SUPPORTED_MODELS[number];\n248: \n249: /**\n250:  * Follows the skill's curated default: `swe` is the SWE-1.7 Lightning alias,\n251:  * rather than Devin's model router.\n252:  */\n253: export const DEVIN_DEFAULT_MODEL: DevinSupportedModel = 'swe';\n254: \n255: /** True when `model` is in the enforced cli-devin allowlist. */\n256: export function isDevinModelAllowed(model: string): model is DevinSupportedModel {\n257:   return (DEVIN_SUPPORTED_MODELS as readonly string[]).includes(model);\n258: }\n259: \n260: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n261: // 3. DOMAIN ERRORS\n262: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n263: \n264: type ExecutorConfigIssue = {\n265:   path: PropertyKey[];\n266:   message: string;\n267: };\n268: \n269: /** Error thrown when a reserved executor kind is selected before wiring exists. */\n270: export class ExecutorNotWiredError extends Error {\n271:   kind: Extract<ExecutorKind, 'cli-claude-code'>;\n272: \n273:   constructor(kind: Extract<ExecutorKind, 'cli-claude-code'>) {\n274:     super(`Executor kind '${kind}' is reserved in the schema but not yet wired. Awaiting future spec for ${kind} integration.`);\n275:     this.name = 'ExecutorNotWiredError';\n276:     this.kind = kind;\n277:   }\n278: }\n279: \n280: /** Error thrown when executor configuration validation fails. */\n\n(Showing lines 1-280 of 792. Use offset=281 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Deep-Loop Executor Config\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport { z } from 'zod';\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. TYPE DEFINITIONS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nexport const EXECUTOR_KINDS = ['native', 'cli-codex', 'cli-claude-code', 'cli-opencode', 'cli-cursor', 'cli-devin', 'cli-pi'] as const;\nexport type ExecutorKind = typeof EXECUTOR_KINDS[number];\n\n// Ordered low→high. `ultra` is codex gpt-5.6-sol's top reasoning tier, above `max`.\nexport const REASONING_EFFORTS = ['none', 'minimal', 'low', 'medium', 'high', 'xhigh', 'max', 'ultra'] as const;\nexport type ReasoningEffort = typeof REASONING_EFFORTS[number];\n\nexport const SERVICE_TIERS = ['priority', 'standard', 'fast'] as const;\nexport type ServiceTier = typeof SERVICE_TIERS[number];\n","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts","text":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Deep-Loop Executor Config\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport { z } from 'zod';\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. TYPE DEFINITIONS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nexport const EXECUTOR_KINDS = ['native', 'cli-codex', 'cli-claude-code', 'cli-opencode', 'cli-cursor', 'cli-devin', 'cli-pi'] as const;\nexport type ExecutorKind = typeof EXECUTOR_KINDS[number];\n\n// Ordered low→high. `ultra` is codex gpt-5.6-sol's top reasoning tier, above `max`.\nexport const REASONING_EFFORTS = ['none', 'minimal', 'low', 'medium', 'high', 'xhigh', 'max', 'ultra'] as const;\nexport type ReasoningEffort = typeof REASONING_EFFORTS[number];\n\nexport const SERVICE_TIERS = ['priority', 'standard', 'fast'] as const;\nexport type ServiceTier = typeof SERVICE_TIERS[number];\n\nexport const WEB_SEARCH_POLICIES = ['inherit', 'disabled', 'cached', 'live'] as const;\nexport type WebSearchPolicy = typeof WEB_SEARCH_POLICIES[number];\n\n/** Live-tool policies resolved for one executor invocation. */\nexport interface LiveToolsConfig {\n  readonly webSearch: WebSearchPolicy;\n}\n\n/** Fan-out assignment models accepted by the schema. */\nexport const FANOUT_ASSIGNMENT_MODELS = ['flat_pool', 'wave'] as const;\n\n/** Fan-out assignment model selected for a lineage or fan-out block. */\nexport type FanoutAssignmentModel = typeof FANOUT_ASSIGNMENT_MODELS[number];\n\nconst SANDBOX_MODES = ['read-only', 'workspace-write', 'danger-full-access'] as const;\nexport type SandboxMode = typeof SANDBOX_MODES[number];\nexport type ClaudePermissionMode = 'plan' | 'acceptEdits' | 'bypassPermissions';\n\n/**\n * Cursor's real approval-flag family (live-verified against the installed CLI):\n * `plan` is Cursor's `--mode plan` read-only/planning mode (reads allowed,\n * edits/shell blocked), `auto-review` is `--auto-review` (\"Smart Auto\"), and\n * `force` is `--force`/`--yolo` (\"Run Everything\"). The fan-out never selects\n * `auto-review`: Smart Auto prompts for tool calls it deems unsafe, and a\n * non-interactive leaf has no stdin to answer, so it could block until the\n * lineage timeout — both write modes use `force` instead.\n */\nexport type CursorApprovalMode = 'plan' | 'auto-review' | 'force';\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nexport const liveToolsSchema = z.object({\n  webSearch: z.enum(WEB_SEARCH_POLICIES).default('inherit'),\n}).default({ webSearch: 'inherit' });\n\nexport const executorConfigSchema = z.object({\n  kind: z.enum(EXECUTOR_KINDS).default('native'),\n  model: z.string().min(1).nullable().default(null),\n  configDir: z.string().trim().min(1).nullable().default(null),\n  reasoningEffort: z.enum(REASONING_EFFORTS).nullable().default(null),\n  serviceTier: z.enum(SERVICE_TIERS).nullable().default(null),\n  sandboxMode: z.enum(SANDBOX_MODES).nullable().default(null),\n  // Hard ceiling of 1 hour per iteration: bounds a single executor invocation so a\n  // runaway per-iteration call cannot by itself consume the whole autonomous lifetime budget.\n  timeoutSeconds: z.number().int().positive().max(3600).default(900),\n  // Optional fable-5 governor capsule for this executor's prompts. Universal and\n  // kind-agnostic on purpose: intentionally absent from EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT\n  // and the unsupported-field scan, so any executor kind may carry it. null = none.\n  governor: z.string().min(1).nullable().default(null),\n  liveTools: liveToolsSchema,\n});\n\nexport type ExecutorConfig = z.infer<typeof executorConfigSchema>;\n\nexport const EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT: Record<ExecutorKind, readonly (keyof ExecutorConfig)[]> = {\n  native: ['liveTools'],\n  'cli-codex': ['model', 'reasoningEffort', 'serviceTier', 'sandboxMode', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n  'cli-claude-code': ['model', 'configDir', 'reasoningEffort', 'sandboxMode', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n  'cli-opencode': ['model', 'reasoningEffort', 'sandboxMode', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n  // No reasoningEffort: the live cursor-agent CLI (2026.07.23-e383d2b) rejects the\n  // parameterized `model[effort=...]` bracket outright (\"Cannot use this model\"),\n  // confirmed live 2026-07-24 — effort tiers are baked into the model id itself\n  // (e.g. `gpt-5.2-high`), not a separate flag. No configDir: no confirmed Cursor\n  // CLI flag isolates the shared `.cursor/` config dir (open question, deferred).\n  'cli-cursor': ['model', 'sandboxMode', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n  // No reasoningEffort and no serviceTier: `devin --help` (live 2026-07-27) lists\n  // only --model, --permission-mode, --sandbox, and --config. Both thinking tier\n  // and priority routing are baked into the model uid instead — `glm-5-2` vs\n  // `glm-5-2-max`, `gpt-5-6-sol-high` vs `gpt-5-6-sol-high-priority` — so neither\n  // is a separate flag. No configDir: --config takes a config *file* path\n  // (~/.config/devin/config.json), not a home directory, so it does not fit the\n  // configDir contract the way CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR does.\n  'cli-devin': ['model', 'sandboxMode', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n  // Pi exposes reasoning as a first-class `--thinking` flag (off..max), independent\n  // of the model id, so reasoningEffort is forwarded; it has no OS sandbox or\n  // service-tier surface, so neither sandboxMode nor serviceTier is supported.\n  'cli-pi': ['model', 'reasoningEffort', 'timeoutSeconds', 'liveTools'],\n};\n\n/** Proven web-search policies for every shipped executor kind. */\nexport const EXECUTOR_WEB_SEARCH_CAPABILITY_MATRIX = {\n  native: {\n    inherit: true,\n    disabled: false,\n    cached: false,\n    live: false,\n  },\n  'cli-codex': {\n    inherit: true,\n    disabled: true,\n    cached: false,\n    live: true,\n  },\n  'cli-claude-code': {\n    inherit: true,\n    disabled: false,\n    cached: false,\n    live: false,\n  },\n  'cli-opencode': {\n    inherit: true,\n    disabled: false,\n    cached: false,\n    live: true,\n  },\n  // No confirmed cursor-agent web-search flag (checked live, 2026-07-24): same\n  // flag-less shape as cli-claude-code — inherit only, nothing enforceable.\n  'cli-cursor': {\n    inherit: true,\n    disabled: false,\n    cached: false,\n    live: false,\n  },\n  // No web-search flag in `devin --help` (checked live 2026-07-27): same\n  // flag-less shape as cli-cursor and cli-claude-code — inherit only, nothing\n  // enforceable either way.\n  'cli-devin': {\n    inherit: true,\n    disabled: false,\n    cached: false,\n    live: false,\n  },\n  'cli-pi': {\n    inherit: true,\n    disabled: false,\n    cached: false,\n    live: false,\n  },\n} as const satisfies Record<ExecutorKind, Record<WebSearchPolicy, boolean>>;\n\n/**\n * Pi is a provider pass-through with no house model. Keep dispatch scoped to\n * the operator-confirmed picker roster so generic provider routing cannot broaden it.\n */\nexport const PI_SUPPORTED_MODELS = [\n  'deepseek-v4-pro',\n  'deepseek-v4-flash',\n  'minimax-m3',\n  'gpt-5.6-luna',\n  'gpt-5.6-sol',\n  'gpt-5.6-terra',\n  'mimo-v2.5-pro',\n  'mimo-v2.5-pro-ultraspeed',\n] as const;\nexport type PiSupportedModel = typeof PI_SUPPORTED_MODELS[number];\n\n/** Use the registry's first-listed, broadly adopted rotation model as the stable default; this is not Pi-specific usage history. */\nexport const PI_DEFAULT_MODEL: PiSupportedModel = 'deepseek-v4-pro';\n\n/** True when `model` is in the enforced cli-pi allowlist. */\nexport function isPiModelAllowed(model: string): model is PiSupportedModel {\n  return (PI_SUPPORTED_MODELS as readonly string[]).includes(model);\n}\n\n/**\n * Enforced allowlist of cursor-agent --model ids. Cursor's live roster spans\n * 150+ hosted-frontier ids across GPT/Claude/Gemini/Grok/GLM/Kimi families,\n * with no per-model prompt-craft data for almost all of them and ids that\n * drift over time — dispatch is scoped to this curated set only, confirmed\n * live via `cursor-agent --list-models` (2026-07-24, account\n * mkerkmeester@proton.me, cursor-agent 2026.07.23-e383d2b; no id here was\n * ever fabricated). This is a hard gate, not a typo-checked reference: any\n * caller-supplied model outside this set must be rejected before a command\n * is constructed. `auto` (Cursor's own router) is deliberately excluded — it\n * can silently resolve to a model outside this allowlist, defeating the\n * point of enforcing one.\n */\nexport const CURSOR_SUPPORTED_MODELS = [\n  'cursor-grok-4.5-low',\n  'cursor-grok-4.5-low-fast',\n  'cursor-grok-4.5-medium',\n  'cursor-grok-4.5-medium-fast',\n  'cursor-grok-4.5-high',\n  'cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast',\n  'composer-2.5',\n  'composer-2.5-fast',\n  'glm-5.2-high',\n  'glm-5.2-max',\n] as const;\nexport type CursorSupportedModel = typeof CURSOR_SUPPORTED_MODELS[number];\n\n/** Default model when a cli-cursor dispatch omits one — Cursor's own native model, now that `auto` is no longer an allowed id. */\nexport const CURSOR_DEFAULT_MODEL: CursorSupportedModel = 'composer-2.5';\n\n/** True when `model` is in the enforced cli-cursor allowlist. */\nexport function isCursorModelAllowed(model: string): model is CursorSupportedModel {\n  return (CURSOR_SUPPORTED_MODELS as readonly string[]).includes(model);\n}\n\n/**\n * Enforced allowlist of devin --model ids. Devin exposes 37 model families and\n * accepts a family slug, an alias, or a full model uid, which is far more\n * surface than deep-loop dispatch needs or has prompt-craft data for. This set\n * is the curated four-family scope: GLM-5.2, SWE-1.7, Grok 4.5, and DeepSeek.\n * Every entry was read from the live `devin models list` — no id here was\n * inferred from documentation.\n *\n * Tier naming matters and is easy to get wrong: `glm-5-2` is \"GLM-5.2 High\" and\n * is the free tier, while `glm-5-2-max` is the separate paid \"GLM-5.2 Max\"\n * tier. The skill's reference table lists these uids without their tier names,\n * so read the live list rather than the doc when picking one.\n */\nexport const DEVIN_SUPPORTED_MODELS = [\n  // SWE-1.7 default alias.\n  'swe',\n  // GLM-5.2 uids. `glm-5-2` = \"GLM-5.2 High\" [200K, Free].\n  'glm-5-2',\n  'glm-5-2-max',\n  'glm-5-2-1m',\n  'glm-5-2-max-1m',\n  'glm-5-2-none',\n  'glm-5-2-none-1m',\n  // SWE-1.7 tier uids.\n  'swe-1-7',\n  'swe-1-7-medium',\n  'swe-1-7-lightning',\n  // Grok 4.5 tier uids read from the live `devin models list`.\n  'grok-4-5-low',\n  'grok-4-5-medium',\n  'grok-4-5-high',\n  // DeepSeek family slug and model uid read from the live `devin models list`.\n  'deepseek-v4-pro',\n  'deepseek-v4',\n] as const;\nexport type DevinSupportedModel = typeof DEVIN_SUPPORTED_MODELS[number];\n\n/**\n * Follows the skill's curated default: `swe` is the SWE-1.7 Lightning alias,\n * rather than Devin's model router.\n */\nexport const DEVIN_DEFAULT_MODEL: DevinSupportedModel = 'swe';\n\n/** True when `model` is in the enforced cli-devin allowlist. */\nexport function isDevinModelAllowed(model: string): model is DevinSupportedModel {\n  return (DEVIN_SUPPORTED_MODELS as readonly string[]).includes(model);\n}\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 3. DOMAIN ERRORS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ntype ExecutorConfigIssue = {\n  path: PropertyKey[];\n  message: string;\n};\n\n/** Error thrown when a reserved executor kind is selected before wiring exists. */\nexport class ExecutorNotWiredError extends Error {\n  kind: Extract<ExecutorKind, 'cli-claude-code'>;\n\n  constructor(kind: Extract<ExecutorKind, 'cli-claude-code'>) {\n    super(`Executor kind '${kind}' is reserved in the schema but not yet wired. Awaiting future spec for ${kind} integration.`);\n    this.name = 'ExecutorNotWiredError';\n    this.kind = kind;\n  }\n}\n\n/** Error thrown when executor configuration validation fails. */","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":280,"totalLines":792,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts","time":{"start":1785758172373,"end":1785758172384}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0740dd26755560fe016a7081dc2b588191943ad8a8e488d954"}},"id":"prt_fc77b44bf001vrmPkEpGnuiLfd","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77b0949001hmcFJW44pOnps0"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758172402,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_AnwthRKF7OMY5QgWDlLEJb0m","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS|parse.*Setup|executor:|config\\.executor","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md"},"output":"Found 10 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md:\n  Line 3: description: Canonical three-tier `:auto` setup-resolution contract shared by every user-invokable `/command:*:auto` surface. Defines tier semantics (resolve → targeted ask → fail-fast), `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` marker grammar, default-resolution table format, fail-fast error template, `:confirm` invariance, and verification protocol.\n\n  Line 17: This reference module defines the single canonical `:auto` setup-resolution contract used by every user-invokable `/command:*:auto` surface in spec-kit (`/spec_kit:*`, `/create:*`, `/deep:*`). Each command's §0 cites this contract and supplies only its own per-field Default Resolution Table + `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` field list. The contract semantics, marker grammar, error format, and verification protocol live here.\n\n  Line 34: 2. **`PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block in the prompt body** — see §2 for grammar. Caller's explicit prompt-body binding wins over `$ARGUMENTS` when both are present\n\n  Line 60: ## §2. PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS Schema\n\n  Line 62: The `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block is a structured marker the dispatched AI parses out of the prompt body. It allows callers to pre-bind setup field values without using individual `$ARGUMENTS` flags.\n\n  Line 67: PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:\n\n  Line 75: - The block opens with `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` (exact case-sensitive heading, followed by colon). Indentation MAY be inside a markdown fenced code block or inline in the prompt text.\n\n  Line 82: - A second `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block in the same prompt body produces a duplicate-block error.\n\n  Line 120: Resolution: provide via $ARGUMENTS flags, PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: block, or switch to :confirm mode for interactive setup.\n\n  Line 177: - [ ] Provides its own `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` field list (one row per setup field, matching the Default Resolution Table)\n","metadata":{"matches":10,"truncated":false},"title":"PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS|parse.*Setup|executor:|config\\.executor","time":{"start":1785758172376,"end":1785758172398}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0740dd26755560fe016a7081dc2b608191b17af6e2d6f66ade"}},"id":"prt_fc77b44d7001x3XtBLdVq2H0Ku","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77b0949001hmcFJW44pOnps0"}}
