{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758208356,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_v2Cq7BJqzuO9IIDrDPBu0VTn","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt","offset":1,"limit":150},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Start Research Loop Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: Presentation source of truth for `/deep:research`. The command router owns only mode selection, setup binding, and asset loading. Workflow YAML owns execution. This file owns visible prompts, dashboard/checkpoint layout, final result displays, examples, and next-step wording.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Startup Presentation\n6: \n7: This workflow gathers all setup inputs in one prompt. Confirm mode still includes multiple approval gates after setup; only the setup round-trip is consolidated here.\n8: \n9: For `:confirm` or no suffix, the consolidated setup prompt MUST be the first visible response. No implementation or file-modifying tool calls before asking. Lightweight read-only discovery to suggest a spec folder or load prior context is allowed, then ask ALL questions immediately and wait.\n10: \n11: For `:auto`, do not emit the consolidated prompt by default. Resolve setup with the three-tier branch below, then load the auto YAML only after all required values are bound.\n12: \n13: ### `:auto` Setup Resolution\n14: \n15: Setup contract: see `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md`.\n16: \n17: Under `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS` (from the `:auto` suffix), follow the three-tier flow:\n18: \n19: 1. **Tier 1 — Resolve confidently** (contract §1): parse `$ARGUMENTS` flags + `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block (§2) + the Default Resolution Table below (§3). When every required field is resolved, persist to `{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json` (shape: `researchTopic`, `specFolder`, `maxIterations`, `convergenceThreshold`, `antiConvergence.convergenceMode`, reserved `antiConvergence.divergent: {}`, `executionMode: \"auto\"`, `resource_map.emit`, `config.executor.*`), bind runtime YAML placeholders, set `STATUS: PASSED`, load `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml`. End §0.\n20: \n21: 2. **Tier 2 — Targeted ask** (contract §1): when 1-2 required fields are genuinely ambiguous AND no default exists, emit ONE narrow question per ambiguous field. Command-specific Tier-2-eligible fields (per the Default Resolution Table below): `spec_folder`. **Ordering rule**: none needed. Missing `research_topic` is absence, not ambiguity — go to Tier 3.\n22: \n23: 3. **Tier 3 — Fail fast** (contract §4): emit the named-missing-inputs error format with `/deep:research:auto` as the command name. Exit non-zero. Do not load YAML.\n24: \n25: `:confirm` path stays unchanged — see the consolidated setup prompt section below.\n26: \n27: ### PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS Schema (for `:auto` non-interactive dispatch)\n28: \n29: The dispatched prompt body may contain one structured marker block. Parse it before applying defaults. Grammar: see `auto-mode-contract.md` §2.\n30: \n31: ```yaml\n32: PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:\n33:   research_topic: WebSocket reconnection strategies  # string\n34:   spec_folder: <spec-folder>  # existing | new | update-related | phase-folder | explicit path\n35:   execution_mode: AUTONOMOUS  # from :auto suffix\n36:   maxIterations: 10  # positive integer\n37:   convergenceThreshold: 0.05  # decimal 0..1\n38:   convergence_mode: default  # default | off | sliding-window | divergent\n39:   executor: native  # native | cli-opencode | cli-claude-code\n40:   executor_model: \"\"  # optional executor-specific model id (cli-opencode e.g. xiaomi-token-plan-ams/mimo-v2.5-pro, minimax-coding-plan/MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed)\n41:   executor_config_dir: \"\"  # optional, cli-claude-code only; maps to CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\n42:   executor_reasoning: \"\"  # optional reasoning effort\n43:   executor_service_tier: \"\"  # optional service tier\n44:   executor_timeout: 900  # optional positive integer seconds\n45:   resource_map_emit: true  # boolean\n46: ```\n47: \n48: Rules: see `auto-mode-contract.md` §2 (unspecified fields fall back to default; marker fields take precedence over `$ARGUMENTS` flags; unknown fields warn; malformed lines parse-error).\n49: \n50: ### Default Resolution Table\n51: \n52: | Field                   | Required | Resolves Via                                                                                                                                                                                           | Default                            | Tier-2 Candidate                                        |\n53: | -------------------------| ----------| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------| ------------------------------------| ---------------------------------------------------------|\n54: | `research_topic`        | Y        | `$ARGUMENTS` positional topic, or marker `research_topic`                                                                                                                                              | none                               | N                                                       |\n55: | `spec_folder`           | Y        | flag `--spec-folder`, marker `spec_folder`, `scope-extract` → a spec-folder path named in the topic/`$ARGUMENTS` that resolves to an existing folder (auto-bound + stripped, per `auto_mode_contract` §1 source 3), or targeted choice among suggested existing/new/update-related/phase folder | none | Y, ONLY when topic is present, names no resolvable spec folder, and the folder choice is ambiguous |\n56: | `execution_mode`        | Y        | attached suffix `:auto` or marker `execution_mode`                                                                                                                                                     | `AUTONOMOUS` under `:auto`         | N                                                       |\n57: | `maxIterations`         | Y        | flag `--max-iterations`, marker `maxIterations`, or default                                                                                                                                            | `10`                               | N                                                       |\n58: | `convergenceThreshold`  | Y        | flag `--convergence`, marker `convergenceThreshold`, or default                                                                                                                                        | `0.05`                             | N                                                       |\n59: | `convergence_mode`      | Y        | flag `--convergence-mode=default|off|sliding-window|divergent`, marker `convergence_mode`, or default                                                                                                  | `default`                          | N                                                       |\n60: | `executor`              | N        | flag `--executor`, marker `executor`, config file, or default                                                                                                                                          | `native`                           | N                                                       |\n61: | `executor_model`        | N        | flag `--model`, marker `executor_model`, or executor-specific validation                                                                                                                               | none                               | N                                                       |\n62: | `executor_config_dir`   | N        | flag `--config-dir`, marker `executor_config_dir`, or executor-specific default                                                                                                                        | none                               | N                                                       |\n63: | `executor_reasoning`    | N        | flag `--reasoning-effort`, marker `executor_reasoning`, or executor default                                                                                                                            | none                               | N                                                       |\n64: | `executor_service_tier` | N        | flag `--service-tier`, marker `executor_service_tier`, or executor default                                                                                                                             | none                               | N                                                       |\n65: | `executor_timeout`      | N        | flag `--executor-timeout`, marker `executor_timeout`, or default                                                                                                                                       | `900`                              | N                                                       |\n66: | `resource_map_emit`     | N        | flag `--no-resource-map`, marker `resource_map_emit`, or default                                                                                                                                       | `true`                             | N                                                       |\n67: | `fanout_executors`      | N        | repeatable `--executor=<type>` flags or `--executors=<json>`; each `--executor` group accepts `--model`, `--config-dir`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--service-tier`, `--executor-timeout`, `--iters`, `--label`, `--count` | none (single-executor when absent) | N                                                       |\n68: | `fanout_concurrency`    | N        | flag `--concurrency=N`                                                                                                                                                                                 | `2`                                | N                                                       |\n69: \n70: **Fan-out default policy:** 0–1 `--executor` flags and no `--executors` → `config.executor` (single-executor, default, unchanged). 2+ `--executor` flags, `--executors`, or any `--count > 1` → `config.fanout`. Native fan-out (count N for `native` executor) runs N sequential `@deep-research` agent dispatches with isolated dirs. CLI fan-out runs N headless subprocesses concurrently in the capped pool.\n71: \n72: ### Consolidated Prompt Template\n73: \n74: **STATUS: ☐ BLOCKED**\n75: \n76: ```\n77: EXECUTE THIS SINGLE CONSOLIDATED PROMPT:\n78: \n79: 1. CHECK for mode suffix:\n80:    |-- \":auto\"         -> execution_mode = \"AUTONOMOUS\"\n81:    |-- \":confirm\"      -> execution_mode = \"INTERACTIVE\"\n82:    +-- No suffix       -> execution_mode = \"ASK\"\n83: \n84: 2. CHECK $ARGUMENTS for topic:\n85:    |-- Has content (ignoring suffixes and flags):\n86:    |     -> research_topic = $ARGUMENTS, omit Q0\n87:    +-- Empty -> include Q0\n88: \n89: 3. PARSE optional flags from $ARGUMENTS:\n90:    |-- --max-iterations=N -> maxIterations = N\n91:    |-- --convergence=N -> convergenceThreshold = N\n92:    |-- --convergence-mode=default|off|sliding-window|divergent -> antiConvergence.convergenceMode = value\n93:    |-- --spec-folder=PATH -> spec_path = PATH, omit Q1\n94:    |-- --executor=<type> -> config.executor.type (`native` | `cli-opencode` | `cli-claude-code`)\n95:    |-- --model=<id> -> config.executor.model (for example `gpt-5.4`)\n96:    |-- --config-dir=<path> -> config.executor.configDir (cli-claude-code only; fan-out sets CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR)\n97:    |-- --reasoning-effort=<level> -> config.executor.reasoningEffort (`none` | `minimal` | `low` | `medium` | `high` | `xhigh` | `max`)\n98:    |-- --service-tier=<tier> -> config.executor.serviceTier (`priority` | `standard` | `fast`)\n99:    |-- --executor-timeout=<seconds> -> config.executor.timeoutSeconds (positive integer, default `900`)\n100:    |-- --no-resource-map -> config.resource_map.emit = false\n101:    |-- --executor=<type> [--model=X] [--config-dir=PATH] [--reasoning-effort=Y] [--service-tier=Z] [--executor-timeout=N] [--iters=N] [--label=X] [--count=N]\n102:    |     (repeatable; each occurrence adds one entry to config.fanout.executors)\n103:    |-- --executors=<json> -> config.fanout.executors = parse(json) escape hatch for complex configs\n104:    |-- --concurrency=N -> config.fanout.concurrency (default 2)\n105:    |\n106:    |   Fan-out default policy:\n107:    |   - 0 or 1 --executor (no --executors, no count>1): write config.executor (single, unchanged)\n108:    |   - 2+ --executor flags, --executors, or any count>1: write config.fanout\n109:    |\n110:    +-- Defaults: maxIterations=10, convergenceThreshold=0.05, antiConvergence.convergenceMode=`default`, antiConvergence.divergent=`{}`, config.executor.type=`native`, config.executor.timeoutSeconds=900, config.resource_map.emit=`true`\n111: \n112:    Executor precedence for setup resolution:\n113:    - CLI flag > config file > schema defaults\n114:    - The generated `deep-research-config.json` stores executor settings under `config.executor.*`\n115: \n116:    Parsing to config mapping:\n117:    - `--executor` -> `config.executor.type`\n118:    - `--model` -> `config.executor.model`\n119:    - `--config-dir` -> `config.executor.configDir`\n120:    - `--reasoning-effort` -> `config.executor.reasoningEffort`\n121:    - `--service-tier` -> `config.executor.serviceTier`\n122:    - `--executor-timeout` -> `config.executor.timeoutSeconds`\n123:    - `--convergence-mode` -> `antiConvergence.convergenceMode`\n124: \n125:    Validation hook:\n126:    - `parseExecutorConfig` from `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` runs at config-write time\n127:    - Invalid combinations fail fast with clear errors, including `cli-opencode` without `--model` and reserved-but-unwired executor kinds\n128: \n129: 4. Search for related spec folders across alias roots:\n130:    $ find specs .opencode/specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 2 -type d 2>/dev/null | sort | tail -10\n131: \n132: 5. Search for prior work (background):\n133:    - memory_context({ input: research_topic OR \"deep-research\", mode: \"focused\", includeContent: true })\n134:    - Store: prior_work_found = [yes/no]\n135: \n136: 6. ASK with SINGLE prompt (include only applicable questions):\n137:    - Include Q-Exec only when `--executor` is NOT present and the topic text does NOT already mention executor hints such as `cli-opencode`, `cli-claude-code`, or `gpt-5.4`\n138:    - If Q-Exec is omitted and no executor is otherwise resolved, default to `native`\n139: \n140:    Q0. Research Topic (if not in command): What topic to research deeply?\n141: \n142:    Q1. Spec Folder (required):\n143:      A) Use existing [suggest if found]\n144:      B) Create new under `specs/[track]/[###]-[slug]/` (accept `.opencode/specs/` alias roots when already in use)\n145:      C) Update related [if match found]\n146:      D) Phase folder (e.g., `specs/NN-track/NNN-name/001-phase/` or matching `.opencode/specs/` alias)\n147: \n148:    Q2. Execution Mode (if no suffix):\n149:      A) Autonomous -- all iterations without approval\n150:      B) Interactive -- pause at each iteration for review\n\n(Showing lines 1-150 of 377. Use offset=151 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deep Start Research Loop Presentation Contract\n\nPresentation source of truth for `/deep:research`. The command router owns only mode selection, setup binding, and asset loading. Workflow YAML owns execution. This file owns visible prompts, dashboard/checkpoint layout, final result displays, examples, and next-step wording.\n\n## 1. Startup Presentation\n\nThis workflow gathers all setup inputs in one prompt. Confirm mode still includes multiple approval gates after setup; only the setup round-trip is consolidated here.\n\nFor `:confirm` or no suffix, the consolidated setup prompt MUST be the first visible response. No implementation or file-modifying tool calls before asking. Lightweight read-only discovery to suggest a spec folder or load prior context is allowed, then ask ALL questions immediately and wait.\n\nFor `:auto`, do not emit the consolidated prompt by default. Resolve setup with the three-tier branch below, then load the auto YAML only after all required values are bound.\n\n### `:auto` Setup Resolution\n\nSetup contract: see `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md`.\n\nUnder `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS` (from the `:auto` suffix), follow the three-tier flow:\n\n1. **Tier 1 — Resolve confidently** (contract §1): parse `$ARGUMENTS` flags + `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block (§2) + the Default Resolution Table below (§3). When every required field is resolved, persist to `{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json` (shape: `researchTopic`, `specFolder`, `maxIterations`, `convergenceThreshold`, `antiConvergence.convergenceMode`, reserved `antiConvergence.divergent: {}`, `executionMode: \"auto\"`, `resource_map.emit`, `config.executor.*`), bind runtime YAML placeholders, set `STATUS: PASSED`, load `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml`. End §0.\n","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt","text":"# Deep Start Research Loop Presentation Contract\n\nPresentation source of truth for `/deep:research`. The command router owns only mode selection, setup binding, and asset loading. Workflow YAML owns execution. This file owns visible prompts, dashboard/checkpoint layout, final result displays, examples, and next-step wording.\n\n## 1. Startup Presentation\n\nThis workflow gathers all setup inputs in one prompt. Confirm mode still includes multiple approval gates after setup; only the setup round-trip is consolidated here.\n\nFor `:confirm` or no suffix, the consolidated setup prompt MUST be the first visible response. No implementation or file-modifying tool calls before asking. Lightweight read-only discovery to suggest a spec folder or load prior context is allowed, then ask ALL questions immediately and wait.\n\nFor `:auto`, do not emit the consolidated prompt by default. Resolve setup with the three-tier branch below, then load the auto YAML only after all required values are bound.\n\n### `:auto` Setup Resolution\n\nSetup contract: see `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md`.\n\nUnder `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS` (from the `:auto` suffix), follow the three-tier flow:\n\n1. **Tier 1 — Resolve confidently** (contract §1): parse `$ARGUMENTS` flags + `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block (§2) + the Default Resolution Table below (§3). When every required field is resolved, persist to `{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json` (shape: `researchTopic`, `specFolder`, `maxIterations`, `convergenceThreshold`, `antiConvergence.convergenceMode`, reserved `antiConvergence.divergent: {}`, `executionMode: \"auto\"`, `resource_map.emit`, `config.executor.*`), bind runtime YAML placeholders, set `STATUS: PASSED`, load `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml`. End §0.\n\n2. **Tier 2 — Targeted ask** (contract §1): when 1-2 required fields are genuinely ambiguous AND no default exists, emit ONE narrow question per ambiguous field. Command-specific Tier-2-eligible fields (per the Default Resolution Table below): `spec_folder`. **Ordering rule**: none needed. Missing `research_topic` is absence, not ambiguity — go to Tier 3.\n\n3. **Tier 3 — Fail fast** (contract §4): emit the named-missing-inputs error format with `/deep:research:auto` as the command name. Exit non-zero. Do not load YAML.\n\n`:confirm` path stays unchanged — see the consolidated setup prompt section below.\n\n### PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS Schema (for `:auto` non-interactive dispatch)\n\nThe dispatched prompt body may contain one structured marker block. Parse it before applying defaults. Grammar: see `auto-mode-contract.md` §2.\n\n```yaml\nPRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:\n  research_topic: WebSocket reconnection strategies  # string\n  spec_folder: <spec-folder>  # existing | new | update-related | phase-folder | explicit path\n  execution_mode: AUTONOMOUS  # from :auto suffix\n  maxIterations: 10  # positive integer\n  convergenceThreshold: 0.05  # decimal 0..1\n  convergence_mode: default  # default | off | sliding-window | divergent\n  executor: native  # native | cli-opencode | cli-claude-code\n  executor_model: \"\"  # optional executor-specific model id (cli-opencode e.g. xiaomi-token-plan-ams/mimo-v2.5-pro, minimax-coding-plan/MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed)\n  executor_config_dir: \"\"  # optional, cli-claude-code only; maps to CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\n  executor_reasoning: \"\"  # optional reasoning effort\n  executor_service_tier: \"\"  # optional service tier\n  executor_timeout: 900  # optional positive integer seconds\n  resource_map_emit: true  # boolean\n```\n\nRules: see `auto-mode-contract.md` §2 (unspecified fields fall back to default; marker fields take precedence over `$ARGUMENTS` flags; unknown fields warn; malformed lines parse-error).\n\n### Default Resolution Table\n\n| Field                   | Required | Resolves Via                                                                                                                                                                                           | Default                            | Tier-2 Candidate                                        |\n| -------------------------| ----------| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------| ------------------------------------| ---------------------------------------------------------|\n| `research_topic`        | Y        | `$ARGUMENTS` positional topic, or marker `research_topic`                                                                                                                                              | none                               | N                                                       |\n| `spec_folder`           | Y        | flag `--spec-folder`, marker `spec_folder`, `scope-extract` → a spec-folder path named in the topic/`$ARGUMENTS` that resolves to an existing folder (auto-bound + stripped, per `auto_mode_contract` §1 source 3), or targeted choice among suggested existing/new/update-related/phase folder | none | Y, ONLY when topic is present, names no resolvable spec folder, and the folder choice is ambiguous |\n| `execution_mode`        | Y        | attached suffix `:auto` or marker `execution_mode`                                                                                                                                                     | `AUTONOMOUS` under `:auto`         | N                                                       |\n| `maxIterations`         | Y        | flag `--max-iterations`, marker `maxIterations`, or default                                                                                                                                            | `10`                               | N                                                       |\n| `convergenceThreshold`  | Y        | flag `--convergence`, marker `convergenceThreshold`, or default                                                                                                                                        | `0.05`                             | N                                                       |\n| `convergence_mode`      | Y        | flag `--convergence-mode=default|off|sliding-window|divergent`, marker `convergence_mode`, or default                                                                                                  | `default`                          | N                                                       |\n| `executor`              | N        | flag `--executor`, marker `executor`, config file, or default                                                                                                                                          | `native`                           | N                                                       |\n| `executor_model`        | N        | flag `--model`, marker `executor_model`, or executor-specific validation                                                                                                                               | none                               | N                                                       |\n| `executor_config_dir`   | N        | flag `--config-dir`, marker `executor_config_dir`, or executor-specific default                                                                                                                        | none                               | N                                                       |\n| `executor_reasoning`    | N        | flag `--reasoning-effort`, marker `executor_reasoning`, or executor default                                                                                                                            | none                               | N                                                       |\n| `executor_service_tier` | N        | flag `--service-tier`, marker `executor_service_tier`, or executor default                                                                                                                             | none                               | N                                                       |\n| `executor_timeout`      | N        | flag `--executor-timeout`, marker `executor_timeout`, or default                                                                                                                                       | `900`                              | N                                                       |\n| `resource_map_emit`     | N        | flag `--no-resource-map`, marker `resource_map_emit`, or default                                                                                                                                       | `true`                             | N                                                       |\n| `fanout_executors`      | N        | repeatable `--executor=<type>` flags or `--executors=<json>`; each `--executor` group accepts `--model`, `--config-dir`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--service-tier`, `--executor-timeout`, `--iters`, `--label`, `--count` | none (single-executor when absent) | N                                                       |\n| `fanout_concurrency`    | N        | flag `--concurrency=N`                                                                                                                                                                                 | `2`                                | N                                                       |\n\n**Fan-out default policy:** 0–1 `--executor` flags and no `--executors` → `config.executor` (single-executor, default, unchanged). 2+ `--executor` flags, `--executors`, or any `--count > 1` → `config.fanout`. Native fan-out (count N for `native` executor) runs N sequential `@deep-research` agent dispatches with isolated dirs. CLI fan-out runs N headless subprocesses concurrently in the capped pool.\n\n### Consolidated Prompt Template\n\n**STATUS: ☐ BLOCKED**\n\n```\nEXECUTE THIS SINGLE CONSOLIDATED PROMPT:\n\n1. CHECK for mode suffix:\n   |-- \":auto\"         -> execution_mode = \"AUTONOMOUS\"\n   |-- \":confirm\"      -> execution_mode = \"INTERACTIVE\"\n   +-- No suffix       -> execution_mode = \"ASK\"\n\n2. CHECK $ARGUMENTS for topic:\n   |-- Has content (ignoring suffixes and flags):\n   |     -> research_topic = $ARGUMENTS, omit Q0\n   +-- Empty -> include Q0\n\n3. PARSE optional flags from $ARGUMENTS:\n   |-- --max-iterations=N -> maxIterations = N\n   |-- --convergence=N -> convergenceThreshold = N\n   |-- --convergence-mode=default|off|sliding-window|divergent -> antiConvergence.convergenceMode = value\n   |-- --spec-folder=PATH -> spec_path = PATH, omit Q1\n   |-- --executor=<type> -> config.executor.type (`native` | `cli-opencode` | `cli-claude-code`)\n   |-- --model=<id> -> config.executor.model (for example `gpt-5.4`)\n   |-- --config-dir=<path> -> config.executor.configDir (cli-claude-code only; fan-out sets CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR)\n   |-- --reasoning-effort=<level> -> config.executor.reasoningEffort (`none` | `minimal` | `low` | `medium` | `high` | `xhigh` | `max`)\n   |-- --service-tier=<tier> -> config.executor.serviceTier (`priority` | `standard` | `fast`)\n   |-- --executor-timeout=<seconds> -> config.executor.timeoutSeconds (positive integer, default `900`)\n   |-- --no-resource-map -> config.resource_map.emit = false\n   |-- --executor=<type> [--model=X] [--config-dir=PATH] [--reasoning-effort=Y] [--service-tier=Z] [--executor-timeout=N] [--iters=N] [--label=X] [--count=N]\n   |     (repeatable; each occurrence adds one entry to config.fanout.executors)\n   |-- --executors=<json> -> config.fanout.executors = parse(json) escape hatch for complex configs\n   |-- --concurrency=N -> config.fanout.concurrency (default 2)\n   |\n   |   Fan-out default policy:\n   |   - 0 or 1 --executor (no --executors, no count>1): write config.executor (single, unchanged)\n   |   - 2+ --executor flags, --executors, or any count>1: write config.fanout\n   |\n   +-- Defaults: maxIterations=10, convergenceThreshold=0.05, antiConvergence.convergenceMode=`default`, antiConvergence.divergent=`{}`, config.executor.type=`native`, config.executor.timeoutSeconds=900, config.resource_map.emit=`true`\n\n   Executor precedence for setup resolution:\n   - CLI flag > config file > schema defaults\n   - The generated `deep-research-config.json` stores executor settings under `config.executor.*`\n\n   Parsing to config mapping:\n   - `--executor` -> `config.executor.type`\n   - `--model` -> `config.executor.model`\n   - `--config-dir` -> `config.executor.configDir`\n   - `--reasoning-effort` -> `config.executor.reasoningEffort`\n   - `--service-tier` -> `config.executor.serviceTier`\n   - `--executor-timeout` -> `config.executor.timeoutSeconds`\n   - `--convergence-mode` -> `antiConvergence.convergenceMode`\n\n   Validation hook:\n   - `parseExecutorConfig` from `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` runs at config-write time\n   - Invalid combinations fail fast with clear errors, including `cli-opencode` without `--model` and reserved-but-unwired executor kinds\n\n4. Search for related spec folders across alias roots:\n   $ find specs .opencode/specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 2 -type d 2>/dev/null | sort | tail -10\n\n5. Search for prior work (background):\n   - memory_context({ input: research_topic OR \"deep-research\", mode: \"focused\", includeContent: true })\n   - Store: prior_work_found = [yes/no]\n\n6. ASK with SINGLE prompt (include only applicable questions):\n   - Include Q-Exec only when `--executor` is NOT present and the topic text does NOT already mention executor hints such as `cli-opencode`, `cli-claude-code`, or `gpt-5.4`\n   - If Q-Exec is omitted and no executor is otherwise resolved, default to `native`\n\n   Q0. Research Topic (if not in command): What topic to research deeply?\n\n   Q1. Spec Folder (required):\n     A) Use existing [suggest if found]\n     B) Create new under `specs/[track]/[###]-[slug]/` (accept `.opencode/specs/` alias roots when already in use)\n     C) Update related [if match found]\n     D) Phase folder (e.g., `specs/NN-track/NNN-name/001-phase/` or matching `.opencode/specs/` alias)\n\n   Q2. Execution Mode (if no suffix):\n     A) Autonomous -- all iterations without approval\n     B) Interactive -- pause at each iteration for review","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":150,"totalLines":377,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt","time":{"start":1785758208336,"end":1785758208349}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0840730133ae3474016a7082002ae4819184cc09d24370b193"}},"id":"prt_fc77bd14c001S61eWh9gGBcT4k","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77bb0b7001diaWRBdzMY8TlU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758208356,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_qJMGWHnxNYBtJhm9789lMD4k","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md","offset":1,"limit":220},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Auto Mode Contract Reference\n3: description: Canonical three-tier `:auto` setup-resolution contract shared by every user-invokable `/command:*:auto` surface. Defines tier semantics (resolve → targeted ask → fail-fast), `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` marker grammar, default-resolution table format, fail-fast error template, `:confirm` invariance, and verification protocol.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"auto mode contract\"\n6:   - \"three-tier setup resolution\"\n7:   - \"pre-bound setup answers\"\n8:   - \"fail-fast error template\"\n9:   - \"confirm invariance\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 3.6.0.7\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Auto Mode Contract Reference\n16: \n17: This reference module defines the single canonical `:auto` setup-resolution contract used by every user-invokable `/command:*:auto` surface in spec-kit (`/spec_kit:*`, `/create:*`, `/deep:*`). Each command's §0 cites this contract and supplies only its own per-field Default Resolution Table + `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` field list. The contract semantics, marker grammar, error format, and verification protocol live here.\n18: \n19: Origin: shipped from the deep-review prototype and generalized in `.../002-auto-mode-contract-generalization-to-all-commands/` (12-command rollout).\n20: \n21: Related memory: `feedback_auto_mode_ask_only_when_ambiguous.md`, `feedback_opencode_spawnagent_allowlist.md`, `feedback_gate3_no_tmp_exemption.md`.\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## §1. Three-Tier Flow\n26: \n27: `:auto` mode does NOT mean \"never ask\" (too rigid) and does NOT mean \"always ask the full setup block\" (too soft). It means \"ask only when uncertain or ambiguous.\" This is achieved via three tiers, evaluated in order:\n28: \n29: ### Tier 1 — Resolve Confidently\n30: \n31: When `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS` (from `:auto` suffix), the command's §0 MUST attempt to resolve every required input from these sources in order:\n32: \n33: 1. **`$ARGUMENTS` flags** — explicit user-passed flags (e.g. `--max-iterations=10`, `--spec-folder=PATH`, command-specific flags)\n34: 2. **`PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block in the prompt body** — see §2 for grammar. Caller's explicit prompt-body binding wins over `$ARGUMENTS` when both are present\n35: 3. **Positional-scope spec-folder extraction** — for any `spec_folder`-class field: if the positional scope / `$ARGUMENTS` contains a path token that canonicalizes (alias roots resolved) to an EXISTING spec folder under `specs/` or `.opencode/specs/`, bind the field to that folder and STRIP the token from the scope. Match against the folder discovery the command already runs (e.g. `find specs .opencode/specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 2 -type d`). A spec folder named inline is a CONFIDENT resolution — NOT a Tier-2 ambiguity and NOT a Tier-3 absence. An explicit `--spec-folder` flag or marker (sources 1–2) still wins over an inline path.\n36: 4. **Documented per-field defaults** — see the command's own Default Resolution Table (§3) for which fields carry sensible defaults\n37: \n38: After resolution: if every required field has a value, persist the resolved map to the command's working-config file (e.g. `deep-review-config.json`, `plan-config.json`), set `STATUS: PASSED`, load the paired YAML workflow. Do NOT emit any setup question. End §0.\n39: \n40: **Standalone / no-folder fallback guard (fail-closed):** when a command offers a standalone (no-spec-folder) output mode, that mode is valid ONLY when no spec folder was named in the scope or otherwise derivable. If source 3 (or an interactive choice) identified a spec folder, the standalone mode MUST NOT be selected — bind the identified folder and write the packet under `{spec_folder}/`. Preflight MUST fail closed if a standalone target is bound while a spec folder was identifiable from the scope.\n41: \n42: ### Tier 2 — Targeted Ask\n43: \n44: Use Tier 2 ONLY when Tier 1 leaves one or two required inputs unresolved AND each unresolved field is genuinely ambiguous AND no sensible default exists.\n45: \n46: Constraints:\n47: - Emit ONE narrow question per ambiguous field, naming only the ambiguous field. NEVER the full consolidated Q-block from the legacy setup phase.\n48: - If two fields are ambiguous but one's resolution likely makes the other obvious (e.g. `review_target_type` may make `spec_folder` self-evident), ask the first one first; do not bundle multiple ambiguities into a single prompt.\n49: - Missing required input (e.g. empty `$ARGUMENTS` with no marker for a required positional) is NOT ambiguity. Absence is a Tier 3 case.\n50: - Wait briefly for user reply. If an answer arrives, merge it into the resolved map and re-run Tier 1 from the default-application step. If stdin is closed (`</dev/null`, redirected output, non-interactive dispatch) and no answer arrives, fall through to Tier 3. Never wait indefinitely.\n51: \n52: ### Tier 3 — Fail Fast\n53: \n54: Use Tier 3 when `:auto` still has unresolved required inputs after Tier 1 and Tier 2, OR when Tier 2 produced no answer because stdin is closed.\n55: \n56: Emit the named-missing-inputs error format (§4), exit non-zero, do NOT load the YAML workflow, do NOT emit any further setup question.\n57: \n58: ---\n59: \n60: ## §2. PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS Schema\n61: \n62: The `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block is a structured marker the dispatched AI parses out of the prompt body. It allows callers to pre-bind setup field values without using individual `$ARGUMENTS` flags.\n63: \n64: Grammar (YAML-style key/value, one field per line):\n65: \n66: ```\n67: PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:\n68:   <field_name>: <value>  # optional inline comment\n69:   <field_name>: <value>\n70:   ...\n71: ```\n72: \n73: Rules:\n74: \n75: - The block opens with `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` (exact case-sensitive heading, followed by colon). Indentation MAY be inside a markdown fenced code block or inline in the prompt text.\n76: - Each field is `  <key>: <value>` indented two spaces, one per line.\n77: - Values are interpreted by the command's Default Resolution Table (§3). Field types and value enums are command-specific.\n78: - Comments after `#` on a value line are ignored.\n79: - Unknown fields produce a warning (do not abort), so callers may include forward-compatible fields.\n80: - Fields not specified fall back to: command-specific Default Resolution Table → command-specific default value → unresolved (triggers Tier 2 or Tier 3 per §1).\n81: - Malformed lines (e.g. missing `:`, malformed value type) emit a parse error naming the line. Known fields parsed before the error may still be used; remaining unresolved fields continue to Tier 2 or Tier 3.\n82: - A second `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block in the same prompt body produces a duplicate-block error.\n83: \n84: The marker block applies ONLY under `:auto`. Under `:confirm`, the block is informational and does not skip the consolidated question prompt.\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## §3. Default Resolution Table\n89: \n90: Every command MUST publish a Default Resolution Table in its §0 (after citing this contract). The table lists each setup field with the following columns:\n91: \n92: | Field | Required | Resolves Via | Default | Tier-2 Candidate |\n93: |-------|----------|--------------|---------|------------------|\n94: \n95: Column meanings:\n96: \n97: - **Field**: the field name (matches the schema in §2 and the question label in the legacy consolidated Q-block).\n98: - **Required**: `Y` (must be resolved before YAML load) or `N` (optional).\n99: - **Resolves Via**: ordered list of resolution sources, e.g. `flag → $ARGUMENTS` / `marker → PRE-BOUND` / `scope-extract → spec-folder path named in scope (§1 source 3)` / `default → \"<value>\"` / `auto-detect from <other field>` / `requires-ask`. Any `spec_folder`-class field MUST list `scope-extract` so a folder named inline binds at Tier 1.\n100: - **Default**: the documented default value when no flag, marker, or auto-detection applies. May be `none` (no default — Tier 2 or Tier 3 candidate).\n101: - **Tier-2 Candidate**: `Y` if a missing value can be resolved by ONE targeted question (per §1); `N` if absence triggers fail-fast (Tier 3).\n102: \n103: A field is a Tier-2 candidate only when ALL of:\n104: - No flag exists for it.\n105: - No marker is provided.\n106: - No sensible default exists.\n107: - The field is genuinely required (Required=`Y`).\n108: - A user choice is the only resolution path (ambiguity, not absence).\n109: \n110: ---\n111: \n112: ## §4. Tier 3 Fail-Fast Error Template\n113: \n114: When Tier 3 fires, the command emits this exact format and exits non-zero:\n115: \n116: ```\n117: [ERROR] /<command>:auto — required inputs unresolved under autonomous mode:\n118:   - <field>: <why-unresolved>\n119:   - <field>: <why-unresolved>\n120: Resolution: provide via $ARGUMENTS flags, PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: block, or switch to :confirm mode for interactive setup.\n121: ```\n122: \n123: Rules:\n124: \n125: - Replace `<command>` with the canonical command name (e.g. `spec_kit:deep-review`).\n126: - One bulleted line per unresolved required field.\n127: - `<why-unresolved>` is one short phrase: \"missing — no flag, no marker, no default\" or \"ambiguous — Tier 2 received no answer (stdin closed)\".\n128: - Final line cites the three resolution paths verbatim.\n129: - Do NOT load the YAML workflow.\n130: - Do NOT emit setup questions in Tier 3.\n131: - Exit code: non-zero (1 is the convention).\n132: \n133: ---\n134: \n135: ## §5. `:confirm` Invariance\n136: \n137: The `:confirm` mode (interactive, with full consolidated Q-block) is unaffected by this contract. Commands MUST preserve their existing `:confirm` behavior exactly. The contract applies ONLY when `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS` (from `:auto` suffix or explicit `--mode=AUTONOMOUS` flag).\n138: \n139: Test invariant: a `:confirm` dispatch against any contract-adopting command MUST emit the original consolidated Q-block (Q0..Qn). Regression-check this per command after migration.\n140: \n141: ---\n142: \n143: ## §6. Verification Protocol\n144: \n145: Each contract-adopting command requires four verification traces (dry-run mental dispatch traces against the command's §0):\n146: \n147: ### Trace A — Tier 1 pass\n148: Dispatch with all required inputs resolvable (flags + markers + defaults). Expected: STATUS PASSED, YAML loaded, no question emitted.\n149: \n150: ### Trace B — Tier 2 targeted ask\n151: Dispatch with exactly one ambiguous required field. Expected: ONE narrow question naming only that field; NEVER the full consolidated block.\n152: \n153: ### Trace C — Tier 3 fail fast\n154: Dispatch with one or more truly missing required inputs (and stdin closed in non-interactive runtimes). Expected: error format from §4, exit non-zero, no YAML load.\n155: \n156: ### Trace D — `:confirm` regression\n157: Dispatch with `:confirm` suffix and any inputs. Expected: existing full consolidated Q-block emitted.\n158: \n159: Live verification (when feasible) extends the dry-run traces with actual non-interactive dispatches (opencode `exec </dev/null`, opencode `run --pure ... </dev/null`, claude `--print`) capturing transcripts as evidence. Live verification confirms the contract works under real runtime stdin-closure conditions.\n160: \n161: Evidence schema (one file per dispatch):\n162: - Command invocation verbatim\n163: - Full transcript\n164: - Verdict footer: PASS / PARTIAL / FAIL / SKIP\n165: - Optional: timing, model, runtime gotchas observed\n166: \n167: Stored under `<packet>/evidence/<command-slug>-<trace>.txt`.\n168: \n169: ---\n170: \n171: ## §7. Adoption Checklist\n172: \n173: For each command adopting this contract, the §0 of the command markdown:\n174: \n175: - [ ] Adds a one-line citation: `Setup contract: see references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md`\n176: - [ ] Provides its own per-field Default Resolution Table (§3) listing every Q-block field with the four columns\n177: - [ ] Provides its own `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` field list (one row per setup field, matching the Default Resolution Table)\n178: - [ ] Documents any command-specific Tier-2 ordering rule (e.g. \"ask review_target_type before spec_folder\")\n179: - [ ] Updates frontmatter `argument-hint` to reference the new bypass capability\n180: - [ ] Preserves the existing `:confirm` consolidated Q-block path untouched\n181: - [ ] Authors §0 dry-run traces (A/B/C/D) and stores them under the adopting packet's `evidence/`\n182: \n183: Commands that have adopted this contract:\n184: \n185: - `/deep:review` (prototype) — see `.../103/001-deep-review-three-tier-setup/`\n186: - (to be appended as `.../103/002-...` rolls out)\n187: \n188: ---\n189: \n190: ## §8. Out of Scope\n191: \n192: - Commands without paired YAML workflows (`/prompt`, `agent_router`, etc.) — they have no setup-phase surface where the contract applies.\n193: - Skill-internal `:auto` flows (sk-doc, sk-code routing, etc.) — those are skill SKILL.md surfaces, not `/command:*` surfaces.\n194: - YAML workflow internal interaction gates (e.g. mid-loop approval gates) — handled by each YAML's own non-interactivity rules, not this contract.\n195: - Cross-command `:auto` integration (e.g. `/spec_kit:plan:auto` chained into `/spec_kit:implement:auto`) — separate contract concern.\n\n(End of file - total 195 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Auto Mode Contract Reference\ndescription: Canonical three-tier `:auto` setup-resolution contract shared by every user-invokable `/command:*:auto` surface. Defines tier semantics (resolve → targeted ask → fail-fast), `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` marker grammar, default-resolution table format, fail-fast error template, `:confirm` invariance, and verification protocol.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"auto mode contract\"\n  - \"three-tier setup resolution\"\n  - \"pre-bound setup answers\"\n  - \"fail-fast error template\"\n  - \"confirm invariance\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 3.6.0.7\n---\n\n# Auto Mode Contract Reference\n\nThis reference module defines the single canonical `:auto` setup-resolution contract used by every user-invokable `/command:*:auto` surface in spec-kit (`/spec_kit:*`, `/create:*`, `/deep:*`). Each command's §0 cites this contract and supplies only its own per-field Default Resolution Table + `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` field list. The contract semantics, marker grammar, error format, and verification protocol live here.\n\nOrigin: shipped from the deep-review prototype and generalized in `.../002-auto-mode-contract-generalization-to-all-commands/` (12-command rollout).\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md","text":"---\ntitle: Auto Mode Contract Reference\ndescription: Canonical three-tier `:auto` setup-resolution contract shared by every user-invokable `/command:*:auto` surface. Defines tier semantics (resolve → targeted ask → fail-fast), `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` marker grammar, default-resolution table format, fail-fast error template, `:confirm` invariance, and verification protocol.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"auto mode contract\"\n  - \"three-tier setup resolution\"\n  - \"pre-bound setup answers\"\n  - \"fail-fast error template\"\n  - \"confirm invariance\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 3.6.0.7\n---\n\n# Auto Mode Contract Reference\n\nThis reference module defines the single canonical `:auto` setup-resolution contract used by every user-invokable `/command:*:auto` surface in spec-kit (`/spec_kit:*`, `/create:*`, `/deep:*`). Each command's §0 cites this contract and supplies only its own per-field Default Resolution Table + `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` field list. The contract semantics, marker grammar, error format, and verification protocol live here.\n\nOrigin: shipped from the deep-review prototype and generalized in `.../002-auto-mode-contract-generalization-to-all-commands/` (12-command rollout).\n\nRelated memory: `feedback_auto_mode_ask_only_when_ambiguous.md`, `feedback_opencode_spawnagent_allowlist.md`, `feedback_gate3_no_tmp_exemption.md`.\n\n---\n\n## §1. Three-Tier Flow\n\n`:auto` mode does NOT mean \"never ask\" (too rigid) and does NOT mean \"always ask the full setup block\" (too soft). It means \"ask only when uncertain or ambiguous.\" This is achieved via three tiers, evaluated in order:\n\n### Tier 1 — Resolve Confidently\n\nWhen `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS` (from `:auto` suffix), the command's §0 MUST attempt to resolve every required input from these sources in order:\n\n1. **`$ARGUMENTS` flags** — explicit user-passed flags (e.g. `--max-iterations=10`, `--spec-folder=PATH`, command-specific flags)\n2. **`PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block in the prompt body** — see §2 for grammar. Caller's explicit prompt-body binding wins over `$ARGUMENTS` when both are present\n3. **Positional-scope spec-folder extraction** — for any `spec_folder`-class field: if the positional scope / `$ARGUMENTS` contains a path token that canonicalizes (alias roots resolved) to an EXISTING spec folder under `specs/` or `.opencode/specs/`, bind the field to that folder and STRIP the token from the scope. Match against the folder discovery the command already runs (e.g. `find specs .opencode/specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 2 -type d`). A spec folder named inline is a CONFIDENT resolution — NOT a Tier-2 ambiguity and NOT a Tier-3 absence. An explicit `--spec-folder` flag or marker (sources 1–2) still wins over an inline path.\n4. **Documented per-field defaults** — see the command's own Default Resolution Table (§3) for which fields carry sensible defaults\n\nAfter resolution: if every required field has a value, persist the resolved map to the command's working-config file (e.g. `deep-review-config.json`, `plan-config.json`), set `STATUS: PASSED`, load the paired YAML workflow. Do NOT emit any setup question. End §0.\n\n**Standalone / no-folder fallback guard (fail-closed):** when a command offers a standalone (no-spec-folder) output mode, that mode is valid ONLY when no spec folder was named in the scope or otherwise derivable. If source 3 (or an interactive choice) identified a spec folder, the standalone mode MUST NOT be selected — bind the identified folder and write the packet under `{spec_folder}/`. Preflight MUST fail closed if a standalone target is bound while a spec folder was identifiable from the scope.\n\n### Tier 2 — Targeted Ask\n\nUse Tier 2 ONLY when Tier 1 leaves one or two required inputs unresolved AND each unresolved field is genuinely ambiguous AND no sensible default exists.\n\nConstraints:\n- Emit ONE narrow question per ambiguous field, naming only the ambiguous field. NEVER the full consolidated Q-block from the legacy setup phase.\n- If two fields are ambiguous but one's resolution likely makes the other obvious (e.g. `review_target_type` may make `spec_folder` self-evident), ask the first one first; do not bundle multiple ambiguities into a single prompt.\n- Missing required input (e.g. empty `$ARGUMENTS` with no marker for a required positional) is NOT ambiguity. Absence is a Tier 3 case.\n- Wait briefly for user reply. If an answer arrives, merge it into the resolved map and re-run Tier 1 from the default-application step. If stdin is closed (`</dev/null`, redirected output, non-interactive dispatch) and no answer arrives, fall through to Tier 3. Never wait indefinitely.\n\n### Tier 3 — Fail Fast\n\nUse Tier 3 when `:auto` still has unresolved required inputs after Tier 1 and Tier 2, OR when Tier 2 produced no answer because stdin is closed.\n\nEmit the named-missing-inputs error format (§4), exit non-zero, do NOT load the YAML workflow, do NOT emit any further setup question.\n\n---\n\n## §2. PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS Schema\n\nThe `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block is a structured marker the dispatched AI parses out of the prompt body. It allows callers to pre-bind setup field values without using individual `$ARGUMENTS` flags.\n\nGrammar (YAML-style key/value, one field per line):\n\n```\nPRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:\n  <field_name>: <value>  # optional inline comment\n  <field_name>: <value>\n  ...\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- The block opens with `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` (exact case-sensitive heading, followed by colon). Indentation MAY be inside a markdown fenced code block or inline in the prompt text.\n- Each field is `  <key>: <value>` indented two spaces, one per line.\n- Values are interpreted by the command's Default Resolution Table (§3). Field types and value enums are command-specific.\n- Comments after `#` on a value line are ignored.\n- Unknown fields produce a warning (do not abort), so callers may include forward-compatible fields.\n- Fields not specified fall back to: command-specific Default Resolution Table → command-specific default value → unresolved (triggers Tier 2 or Tier 3 per §1).\n- Malformed lines (e.g. missing `:`, malformed value type) emit a parse error naming the line. Known fields parsed before the error may still be used; remaining unresolved fields continue to Tier 2 or Tier 3.\n- A second `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block in the same prompt body produces a duplicate-block error.\n\nThe marker block applies ONLY under `:auto`. Under `:confirm`, the block is informational and does not skip the consolidated question prompt.\n\n---\n\n## §3. Default Resolution Table\n\nEvery command MUST publish a Default Resolution Table in its §0 (after citing this contract). The table lists each setup field with the following columns:\n\n| Field | Required | Resolves Via | Default | Tier-2 Candidate |\n|-------|----------|--------------|---------|------------------|\n\nColumn meanings:\n\n- **Field**: the field name (matches the schema in §2 and the question label in the legacy consolidated Q-block).\n- **Required**: `Y` (must be resolved before YAML load) or `N` (optional).\n- **Resolves Via**: ordered list of resolution sources, e.g. `flag → $ARGUMENTS` / `marker → PRE-BOUND` / `scope-extract → spec-folder path named in scope (§1 source 3)` / `default → \"<value>\"` / `auto-detect from <other field>` / `requires-ask`. Any `spec_folder`-class field MUST list `scope-extract` so a folder named inline binds at Tier 1.\n- **Default**: the documented default value when no flag, marker, or auto-detection applies. May be `none` (no default — Tier 2 or Tier 3 candidate).\n- **Tier-2 Candidate**: `Y` if a missing value can be resolved by ONE targeted question (per §1); `N` if absence triggers fail-fast (Tier 3).\n\nA field is a Tier-2 candidate only when ALL of:\n- No flag exists for it.\n- No marker is provided.\n- No sensible default exists.\n- The field is genuinely required (Required=`Y`).\n- A user choice is the only resolution path (ambiguity, not absence).\n\n---\n\n## §4. Tier 3 Fail-Fast Error Template\n\nWhen Tier 3 fires, the command emits this exact format and exits non-zero:\n\n```\n[ERROR] /<command>:auto — required inputs unresolved under autonomous mode:\n  - <field>: <why-unresolved>\n  - <field>: <why-unresolved>\nResolution: provide via $ARGUMENTS flags, PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: block, or switch to :confirm mode for interactive setup.\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Replace `<command>` with the canonical command name (e.g. `spec_kit:deep-review`).\n- One bulleted line per unresolved required field.\n- `<why-unresolved>` is one short phrase: \"missing — no flag, no marker, no default\" or \"ambiguous — Tier 2 received no answer (stdin closed)\".\n- Final line cites the three resolution paths verbatim.\n- Do NOT load the YAML workflow.\n- Do NOT emit setup questions in Tier 3.\n- Exit code: non-zero (1 is the convention).\n\n---\n\n## §5. `:confirm` Invariance\n\nThe `:confirm` mode (interactive, with full consolidated Q-block) is unaffected by this contract. Commands MUST preserve their existing `:confirm` behavior exactly. The contract applies ONLY when `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS` (from `:auto` suffix or explicit `--mode=AUTONOMOUS` flag).\n\nTest invariant: a `:confirm` dispatch against any contract-adopting command MUST emit the original consolidated Q-block (Q0..Qn). Regression-check this per command after migration.\n\n---\n\n## §6. Verification Protocol\n\nEach contract-adopting command requires four verification traces (dry-run mental dispatch traces against the command's §0):\n\n### Trace A — Tier 1 pass\nDispatch with all required inputs resolvable (flags + markers + defaults). Expected: STATUS PASSED, YAML loaded, no question emitted.\n\n### Trace B — Tier 2 targeted ask\nDispatch with exactly one ambiguous required field. Expected: ONE narrow question naming only that field; NEVER the full consolidated block.\n\n### Trace C — Tier 3 fail fast\nDispatch with one or more truly missing required inputs (and stdin closed in non-interactive runtimes). Expected: error format from §4, exit non-zero, no YAML load.\n\n### Trace D — `:confirm` regression\nDispatch with `:confirm` suffix and any inputs. Expected: existing full consolidated Q-block emitted.\n\nLive verification (when feasible) extends the dry-run traces with actual non-interactive dispatches (opencode `exec </dev/null`, opencode `run --pure ... </dev/null`, claude `--print`) capturing transcripts as evidence. Live verification confirms the contract works under real runtime stdin-closure conditions.\n\nEvidence schema (one file per dispatch):\n- Command invocation verbatim\n- Full transcript\n- Verdict footer: PASS / PARTIAL / FAIL / SKIP\n- Optional: timing, model, runtime gotchas observed\n\nStored under `<packet>/evidence/<command-slug>-<trace>.txt`.\n\n---\n\n## §7. Adoption Checklist\n\nFor each command adopting this contract, the §0 of the command markdown:\n\n- [ ] Adds a one-line citation: `Setup contract: see references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md`\n- [ ] Provides its own per-field Default Resolution Table (§3) listing every Q-block field with the four columns\n- [ ] Provides its own `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` field list (one row per setup field, matching the Default Resolution Table)\n- [ ] Documents any command-specific Tier-2 ordering rule (e.g. \"ask review_target_type before spec_folder\")\n- [ ] Updates frontmatter `argument-hint` to reference the new bypass capability\n- [ ] Preserves the existing `:confirm` consolidated Q-block path untouched\n- [ ] Authors §0 dry-run traces (A/B/C/D) and stores them under the adopting packet's `evidence/`\n\nCommands that have adopted this contract:\n\n- `/deep:review` (prototype) — see `.../103/001-deep-review-three-tier-setup/`\n- (to be appended as `.../103/002-...` rolls out)\n\n---\n\n## §8. Out of Scope\n\n- Commands without paired YAML workflows (`/prompt`, `agent_router`, etc.) — they have no setup-phase surface where the contract applies.\n- Skill-internal `:auto` flows (sk-doc, sk-code routing, etc.) — those are skill SKILL.md surfaces, not `/command:*` surfaces.\n- YAML workflow internal interaction gates (e.g. mid-loop approval gates) — handled by each YAML's own non-interactivity rules, not this contract.\n- Cross-command `:auto` integration (e.g. `/spec_kit:plan:auto` chained into `/spec_kit:implement:auto`) — separate contract concern.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":195,"totalLines":195,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/auto-mode-contract.md","time":{"start":1785758208331,"end":1785758208354}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0840730133ae3474016a7082002ad881919a42f1c3608936aa"}},"id":"prt_fc77bd148001S3fNiqHvdSTCO8","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77bb0b7001diaWRBdzMY8TlU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758208368,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_5cxuHacMPRB4ExcLB8q2ywwo","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts","offset":620,"limit":220},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n620: // that recovers it binds it separately.\n621: type CompletionFacts = {\n622:   childPid: number | null;\n623:   exitStatus: number | null;\n624:   signal: NodeJS.Signals | null;\n625:   sessionId: string | null;\n626: };\n627: \n628: function completeReceipt(\n629:   input: RunAuditedExecutorCommandInput,\n630:   ctx: ReceiptContext,\n631:   completion: CompletionFacts,\n632: ): void {\n633:   const facts = {\n634:     ...buildReceiptFacts(input),\n635:     childPid: completion.childPid,\n636:     exitStatus: completion.exitStatus,\n637:     signal: completion.signal,\n638:     sessionId: completion.sessionId,\n639:   };\n640:   const record = buildReceiptRecord('completion', ctx.dispatchId, facts, ctx.key);\n641:   tryWriteReceipt(input.stateLogPath, input.executor, input.iteration, 'completion', ctx.completionPath, record);\n642: }\n643: \n644: // ───── EXPORTS ─────\n645: \n646: /**\n647:  * Detect whether the same executor kind already appears in the dispatch stack.\n648:  *\n649:  * @param stack - The SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK env value.\n650:  * @param kind - The executor kind to check.\n651:  * @returns True if the kind is already present in the stack.\n652:  */\n653: export function detectSameKindFromStack(stack: string | undefined, kind: ExecutorKind): boolean {\n654:   if (kind === 'native') {\n655:     return false;\n656:   }\n657: \n658:   return splitDispatchStack(stack).includes(kind);\n659: }\n660: \n661: /**\n662:  * Detect whether an executor binary appears in the process ancestry.\n663:  *\n664:  * Reads Linux /proc ancestor cmdlines to find the executor binary.\n665:  *\n666:  * @param kind - The executor kind to check.\n667:  * @param ancestryCmdlines - Pre-computed ancestor command lines (optional).\n668:  * @returns True if the executor binary is found in the ancestry.\n669:  */\n670: export function detectFromAncestry(kind: ExecutorKind, ancestryCmdlines: string[] = readLinuxAncestorCmdlines()): boolean {\n671:   const binary = EXECUTOR_BINARY_BY_KIND[kind];\n672:   if (!binary) {\n673:     return false;\n674:   }\n675: \n676:   return ancestryCmdlines.some((commandLine) => commandLineContainsBinary(commandLine, binary));\n677: }\n678: \n679: /**\n680:  * Detect whether a runtime session environment variable is set for an executor.\n681:  *\n682:  * @param kind - The executor kind to check.\n683:  * @param env - Environment variable map (defaults to process.env).\n684:  * @returns True if the session environment variable is set.\n685:  */\n686: export function detectFromRuntimeEnv(\n687:   kind: ExecutorKind,\n688:   env: Record<string, string | undefined> = process.env,\n689: ): boolean {\n690:   const sessionEnvName = EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND[kind];\n691:   if (!sessionEnvName) {\n692:     return false;\n693:   }\n694: \n695:   return typeof env[sessionEnvName] === 'string' && env[sessionEnvName]?.trim() !== '';\n696: }\n697: \n698: /**\n699:  * Detect whether a dispatch lockfile exists in executor state directories.\n700:  *\n701:  * @param kind - The executor kind to check.\n702:  * @param statePaths - State directory paths to scan (defaults to auto-detected).\n703:  * @returns True if a lockfile is found.\n704:  */\n705: export function detectFromLockfile(kind: ExecutorKind, statePaths: string[] = getDefaultStatePaths(kind, process.env)): boolean {\n706:   if (kind === 'native') {\n707:     return false;\n708:   }\n709: \n710:   const names = candidateLockfileNames(kind);\n711:   for (const statePath of statePaths) {\n712:     const directories = [statePath, join(statePath, 'locks')];\n713:     for (const directory of directories) {\n714:       if (!pathIsReadableDirectory(directory)) {\n715:         continue;\n716:       }\n717:       const entries = new Set(readdirSync(directory));\n718:       if (names.some((name) => entries.has(name))) {\n719:         return true;\n720:       }\n721:     }\n722:   }\n723: \n724:   return false;\n725: }\n726: \n727: /**\n728:  * Validate that an executor dispatch is allowed.\n729:  *\n730:  * Checks stack, ancestry, runtime env, and lockfile layers for recursion\n731:  * guard violations per the deep-loop dispatch contract.\n732:  *\n733:  * @param config - Executor configuration.\n734:  * @param context - Optional environment, ancestry, and state path context.\n735:  * @returns Dispatch result indicating whether dispatch is allowed.\n736:  */\n737: export function validateExecutorDispatchAllowed(\n738:   config: ExecutorConfig,\n739:   context: ExecutorDispatchGuardContext = {},\n740: ): ExecutorDispatchAllowedResult {\n741:   const kind = getExecutorKind(config);\n742:   if (kind === 'native') {\n743:     return { allowed: true };\n744:   }\n745: \n746:   const env = context.env ?? process.env;\n747:   const stack = env[CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV];\n748:   if (detectSameKindFromStack(stack, kind)) {\n749:     return {\n750:       allowed: false,\n751:       layer: 'stack',\n752:       reason: recursionReasonForLayer('stack'),\n753:       detail: `${kind} already appears in ${CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV}`,\n754:     };\n755:   }\n756: \n757:   if (detectFromAncestry(kind, context.ancestryCmdlines)) {\n758:     return {\n759:       allowed: false,\n760:       layer: 'ancestry',\n761:       reason: recursionReasonForLayer('ancestry'),\n762:       detail: `${kind} executor binary appears in process ancestry`,\n763:     };\n764:   }\n765: \n766:   if (detectFromRuntimeEnv(kind, env)) {\n767:     const envName = EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND[kind] ?? 'runtime session env';\n768:     return {\n769:       allowed: false,\n770:       layer: 'env',\n771:       reason: recursionReasonForLayer('env'),\n772:       detail: `${envName} is set for ${kind}`,\n773:     };\n774:   }\n775: \n776:   const statePaths = context.statePaths ?? getDefaultStatePaths(kind, env);\n777:   if (detectFromLockfile(kind, statePaths)) {\n778:     return {\n779:       allowed: false,\n780:       layer: 'lockfile',\n781:       reason: recursionReasonForLayer('lockfile'),\n782:       detail: `${kind} dispatch lockfile exists in runtime state path`,\n783:     };\n784:   }\n785: \n786:   return { allowed: true };\n787: }\n788: \n789: /**\n790:  * Build the environment for a dispatched executor.\n791:  *\n792:  * Filters the parent environment to only include allowed keys per executor kind\n793:  * and appends the current kind to the dispatch stack.\n794:  *\n795:  * @param config - Executor configuration.\n796:  * @param parentEnv - Parent environment (defaults to process.env).\n797:  * @returns Filtered environment with dispatch stack updated.\n798:  */\n799: export function buildExecutorDispatchEnv(\n800:   config: ExecutorConfig,\n801:   parentEnv: Record<string, string | undefined> = process.env,\n802: ): Record<string, string | undefined> {\n803:   const kind = getExecutorKind(config);\n804:   if (kind === 'native') {\n805:     return { ...parentEnv };\n806:   }\n807: \n808:   const nextEnv: Record<string, string | undefined> = {};\n809:   for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(parentEnv)) {\n810:     if (value !== undefined && isAllowedExecutorEnvKey(key, kind)) {\n811:       nextEnv[key] = value;\n812:     }\n813:   }\n814:   nextEnv[CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV] = [...splitDispatchStack(parentEnv[CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV]), kind].join(':');\n815:   return nextEnv;\n816: }\n817: \n818: /**\n819:  * Build an executor audit record for provenance logging.\n820:  *\n821:  * @param executor - Executor configuration.\n822:  * @returns Audit record with kind, model, reasoning effort, and service tier.\n823:  */\n824: export function buildExecutorAuditRecord(executor: ExecutorConfig, lineageId?: string): Record<string, unknown> {\n825:   return {\n826:     kind: getExecutorKind(executor),\n827:     model: executor.model,\n828:     reasoningEffort: executor.reasoningEffort,\n829:     serviceTier: executor.serviceTier,\n830:     ...(lineageId !== undefined ? { lineageId } : {}),\n831:   };\n832: }\n833: \n834: /**\n835:  * Write the first executor provenance record for an iteration.\n836:  *\n837:  * Updates the iteration start record in the JSONL state log with executor\n838:  * audit data, or creates a new iteration_start record if none exists.\n839:  *\n\n(Showing lines 620-839 of 1208. Use offset=840 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"// that recovers it binds it separately.\ntype CompletionFacts = {\n  childPid: number | null;\n  exitStatus: number | null;\n  signal: NodeJS.Signals | null;\n  sessionId: string | null;\n};\n\nfunction completeReceipt(\n  input: RunAuditedExecutorCommandInput,\n  ctx: ReceiptContext,\n  completion: CompletionFacts,\n): void {\n  const facts = {\n    ...buildReceiptFacts(input),\n    childPid: completion.childPid,\n    exitStatus: completion.exitStatus,\n    signal: completion.signal,\n    sessionId: completion.sessionId,\n  };","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts","text":"// that recovers it binds it separately.\ntype CompletionFacts = {\n  childPid: number | null;\n  exitStatus: number | null;\n  signal: NodeJS.Signals | null;\n  sessionId: string | null;\n};\n\nfunction completeReceipt(\n  input: RunAuditedExecutorCommandInput,\n  ctx: ReceiptContext,\n  completion: CompletionFacts,\n): void {\n  const facts = {\n    ...buildReceiptFacts(input),\n    childPid: completion.childPid,\n    exitStatus: completion.exitStatus,\n    signal: completion.signal,\n    sessionId: completion.sessionId,\n  };\n  const record = buildReceiptRecord('completion', ctx.dispatchId, facts, ctx.key);\n  tryWriteReceipt(input.stateLogPath, input.executor, input.iteration, 'completion', ctx.completionPath, record);\n}\n\n// ───── EXPORTS ─────\n\n/**\n * Detect whether the same executor kind already appears in the dispatch stack.\n *\n * @param stack - The SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK env value.\n * @param kind - The executor kind to check.\n * @returns True if the kind is already present in the stack.\n */\nexport function detectSameKindFromStack(stack: string | undefined, kind: ExecutorKind): boolean {\n  if (kind === 'native') {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  return splitDispatchStack(stack).includes(kind);\n}\n\n/**\n * Detect whether an executor binary appears in the process ancestry.\n *\n * Reads Linux /proc ancestor cmdlines to find the executor binary.\n *\n * @param kind - The executor kind to check.\n * @param ancestryCmdlines - Pre-computed ancestor command lines (optional).\n * @returns True if the executor binary is found in the ancestry.\n */\nexport function detectFromAncestry(kind: ExecutorKind, ancestryCmdlines: string[] = readLinuxAncestorCmdlines()): boolean {\n  const binary = EXECUTOR_BINARY_BY_KIND[kind];\n  if (!binary) {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  return ancestryCmdlines.some((commandLine) => commandLineContainsBinary(commandLine, binary));\n}\n\n/**\n * Detect whether a runtime session environment variable is set for an executor.\n *\n * @param kind - The executor kind to check.\n * @param env - Environment variable map (defaults to process.env).\n * @returns True if the session environment variable is set.\n */\nexport function detectFromRuntimeEnv(\n  kind: ExecutorKind,\n  env: Record<string, string | undefined> = process.env,\n): boolean {\n  const sessionEnvName = EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND[kind];\n  if (!sessionEnvName) {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  return typeof env[sessionEnvName] === 'string' && env[sessionEnvName]?.trim() !== '';\n}\n\n/**\n * Detect whether a dispatch lockfile exists in executor state directories.\n *\n * @param kind - The executor kind to check.\n * @param statePaths - State directory paths to scan (defaults to auto-detected).\n * @returns True if a lockfile is found.\n */\nexport function detectFromLockfile(kind: ExecutorKind, statePaths: string[] = getDefaultStatePaths(kind, process.env)): boolean {\n  if (kind === 'native') {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  const names = candidateLockfileNames(kind);\n  for (const statePath of statePaths) {\n    const directories = [statePath, join(statePath, 'locks')];\n    for (const directory of directories) {\n      if (!pathIsReadableDirectory(directory)) {\n        continue;\n      }\n      const entries = new Set(readdirSync(directory));\n      if (names.some((name) => entries.has(name))) {\n        return true;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return false;\n}\n\n/**\n * Validate that an executor dispatch is allowed.\n *\n * Checks stack, ancestry, runtime env, and lockfile layers for recursion\n * guard violations per the deep-loop dispatch contract.\n *\n * @param config - Executor configuration.\n * @param context - Optional environment, ancestry, and state path context.\n * @returns Dispatch result indicating whether dispatch is allowed.\n */\nexport function validateExecutorDispatchAllowed(\n  config: ExecutorConfig,\n  context: ExecutorDispatchGuardContext = {},\n): ExecutorDispatchAllowedResult {\n  const kind = getExecutorKind(config);\n  if (kind === 'native') {\n    return { allowed: true };\n  }\n\n  const env = context.env ?? process.env;\n  const stack = env[CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV];\n  if (detectSameKindFromStack(stack, kind)) {\n    return {\n      allowed: false,\n      layer: 'stack',\n      reason: recursionReasonForLayer('stack'),\n      detail: `${kind} already appears in ${CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV}`,\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (detectFromAncestry(kind, context.ancestryCmdlines)) {\n    return {\n      allowed: false,\n      layer: 'ancestry',\n      reason: recursionReasonForLayer('ancestry'),\n      detail: `${kind} executor binary appears in process ancestry`,\n    };\n  }\n\n  if (detectFromRuntimeEnv(kind, env)) {\n    const envName = EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND[kind] ?? 'runtime session env';\n    return {\n      allowed: false,\n      layer: 'env',\n      reason: recursionReasonForLayer('env'),\n      detail: `${envName} is set for ${kind}`,\n    };\n  }\n\n  const statePaths = context.statePaths ?? getDefaultStatePaths(kind, env);\n  if (detectFromLockfile(kind, statePaths)) {\n    return {\n      allowed: false,\n      layer: 'lockfile',\n      reason: recursionReasonForLayer('lockfile'),\n      detail: `${kind} dispatch lockfile exists in runtime state path`,\n    };\n  }\n\n  return { allowed: true };\n}\n\n/**\n * Build the environment for a dispatched executor.\n *\n * Filters the parent environment to only include allowed keys per executor kind\n * and appends the current kind to the dispatch stack.\n *\n * @param config - Executor configuration.\n * @param parentEnv - Parent environment (defaults to process.env).\n * @returns Filtered environment with dispatch stack updated.\n */\nexport function buildExecutorDispatchEnv(\n  config: ExecutorConfig,\n  parentEnv: Record<string, string | undefined> = process.env,\n): Record<string, string | undefined> {\n  const kind = getExecutorKind(config);\n  if (kind === 'native') {\n    return { ...parentEnv };\n  }\n\n  const nextEnv: Record<string, string | undefined> = {};\n  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(parentEnv)) {\n    if (value !== undefined && isAllowedExecutorEnvKey(key, kind)) {\n      nextEnv[key] = value;\n    }\n  }\n  nextEnv[CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV] = [...splitDispatchStack(parentEnv[CLI_DISPATCH_STACK_ENV]), kind].join(':');\n  return nextEnv;\n}\n\n/**\n * Build an executor audit record for provenance logging.\n *\n * @param executor - Executor configuration.\n * @returns Audit record with kind, model, reasoning effort, and service tier.\n */\nexport function buildExecutorAuditRecord(executor: ExecutorConfig, lineageId?: string): Record<string, unknown> {\n  return {\n    kind: getExecutorKind(executor),\n    model: executor.model,\n    reasoningEffort: executor.reasoningEffort,\n    serviceTier: executor.serviceTier,\n    ...(lineageId !== undefined ? { lineageId } : {}),\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * Write the first executor provenance record for an iteration.\n *\n * Updates the iteration start record in the JSONL state log with executor\n * audit data, or creates a new iteration_start record if none exists.\n *","lineStart":620,"lineEnd":839,"totalLines":1208,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts","time":{"start":1785758208325,"end":1785758208364}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0840730133ae3474016a7082002ac08191b02f3a17ed5ed288"}},"id":"prt_fc77bd102001os1VQwY83h0EYn","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77bb0b7001diaWRBdzMY8TlU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758208368,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_1KcFj7mrpDRHn5Vs7OXTW553","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/workflow-session-id-parity.vitest.ts","offset":150,"limit":90},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/workflow-session-id-parity.vitest.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n150:     'step_create_config populate block',\n151:   );\n152: \n153:   expect(\n154:     readScalar(\n155:       configPopulate,\n156:       contract.configSessionKey,\n157:       contract.mode,\n158:       `${contract.configSessionKey} config consumption`,\n159:     ),\n160:     `${contract.mode}: config creation must consume {session_id_init} for ${contract.configSessionKey}`,\n161:   ).toBe('{session_id_init}');\n162: }\n163: \n164: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n165: // 4. TESTS\n166: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n167: \n168: describe('deep workflow session id parity', () => {\n169:   it('pins the auto-workflow resolve contract for review, context, and research', () => {\n170:     for (const contract of MODE_CONTRACTS) {\n171:       assertSessionIdContract(contract);\n172:     }\n173:   });\n174: \n175:   it('renders a session_id line in fan-out lineage prompts for active fan-out loop types', () => {\n176:     const { buildLoopPrompt } = requireCjs(FANOUT_RUN_SCRIPT) as FanoutRunExports;\n177: \n178:     for (const { mode } of MODE_CONTRACTS.filter((contract) => contract.mode !== 'context')) {\n179:       const sessionId = `fanout-${mode}-session`;\n180:       const prompt = buildLoopPrompt(\n181:         mode as ActiveFanoutMode,\n182:         'specs/test-session-id-parity',\n183:         `/tmp/${mode}-lineage`,\n184:         sessionId,\n185:         { kind: 'cli-opencode', label: `${mode}-seat`, model: 'opencode-go/glm-5.1' },\n186:         mode === 'research' ? 'session id parity research topic' : undefined,\n187:       );\n188: \n189:       expect(\n190:         prompt,\n191:         `${mode}: fan-out prompt missing session_id line`,\n192:       ).toContain(`\\n  session_id: ${sessionId}\\n`);\n193:     }\n194:   });\n195: });\n\n(End of file - total 195 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"    'step_create_config populate block',\n  );\n\n  expect(\n    readScalar(\n      configPopulate,\n      contract.configSessionKey,\n      contract.mode,\n      `${contract.configSessionKey} config consumption`,\n    ),\n    `${contract.mode}: config creation must consume {session_id_init} for ${contract.configSessionKey}`,\n  ).toBe('{session_id_init}');\n}\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 4. TESTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndescribe('deep workflow session id parity', () => {\n  it('pins the auto-workflow resolve contract for review, context, and research', () => {","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/workflow-session-id-parity.vitest.ts","text":"    'step_create_config populate block',\n  );\n\n  expect(\n    readScalar(\n      configPopulate,\n      contract.configSessionKey,\n      contract.mode,\n      `${contract.configSessionKey} config consumption`,\n    ),\n    `${contract.mode}: config creation must consume {session_id_init} for ${contract.configSessionKey}`,\n  ).toBe('{session_id_init}');\n}\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 4. TESTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndescribe('deep workflow session id parity', () => {\n  it('pins the auto-workflow resolve contract for review, context, and research', () => {\n    for (const contract of MODE_CONTRACTS) {\n      assertSessionIdContract(contract);\n    }\n  });\n\n  it('renders a session_id line in fan-out lineage prompts for active fan-out loop types', () => {\n    const { buildLoopPrompt } = requireCjs(FANOUT_RUN_SCRIPT) as FanoutRunExports;\n\n    for (const { mode } of MODE_CONTRACTS.filter((contract) => contract.mode !== 'context')) {\n      const sessionId = `fanout-${mode}-session`;\n      const prompt = buildLoopPrompt(\n        mode as ActiveFanoutMode,\n        'specs/test-session-id-parity',\n        `/tmp/${mode}-lineage`,\n        sessionId,\n        { kind: 'cli-opencode', label: `${mode}-seat`, model: 'opencode-go/glm-5.1' },\n        mode === 'research' ? 'session id parity research topic' : undefined,\n      );\n\n      expect(\n        prompt,\n        `${mode}: fan-out prompt missing session_id line`,\n      ).toContain(`\\n  session_id: ${sessionId}\\n`);\n    }\n  });\n});","lineStart":150,"lineEnd":195,"totalLines":195,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/workflow-session-id-parity.vitest.ts","time":{"start":1785758208340,"end":1785758208367}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0840730133ae3474016a7082002b488191ba4e309361879693"}},"id":"prt_fc77bd151001hkl19FgQxTeJxK","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77bb0b7001diaWRBdzMY8TlU"}}
