packet faithfully document the official Designer canvas, Bridge App, element tree, component, style, variable, and breakpoint model?\",\n87:       \"origin\": \"operator\",\n88:       \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n89:       \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n90:       \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n91:       \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n92:       \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n93:     },\n94:     {\n95:       \"id\": \"Q2\",\n96:       \"inboxId\": null,\n97:       \"text\": \"Does the packet cover CMS, publishing, branches, scripts, forms, localization, sites, assets, and compression semantics?\",\n98:       \"origin\": \"operator\",\n99:       \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n100:       \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n101:       \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n102:       \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n103:       \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n104:     },\n105:     {\n106:       \"id\": \"Q3\",\n107:       \"inboxId\": null,\n108:       \"text\": \"Does the packet cover webhooks, Enterprise, AI tools, Agent Instructions, WHTML, utility tools, and rate limits?\",\n109:       \"origin\": \"operator\",\n110:       \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n111:       \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n112:       \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n113:       \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n114:       \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n115:     },\n116:     {\n117:       \"id\": \"Q4\",\n118:       \"inboxId\": null,\n119:       \"text\": \"Does the local OSS/server documentation reconcile with the remote Webflow MCP surface and expose version or capability drift?\",\n120:       \"origin\": \"operator\",\n121:       \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n122:       \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n123:       \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n124:       \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n125:       \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n126:     },\n127:     {\n128:       \"id\": \"Q5\",\n129:       \"inboxId\": null,\n130:       \"text\": \"Which references, assets, feature cards, and manual scenarios are too concise or missing important logic?\",\n131:       \"origin\": \"operator\",\n132:       \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n133:       \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n134:       \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n135:       \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n136:       \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n137:     },\n138:     {\n139:       \"id\": \"Q6\",\n140:       \"inboxId\": null,\n141:       \"text\": \"What concrete P0/P1/P2, file-by-file additions are needed, with official or local citations?\",\n142:       \"origin\": \"operator\",\n143:       \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n144:       \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n145:       \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n146:       \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n147:       \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n148:     }\n149:   ],\n150:   \"resolvedQuestions\": [],\n151:   \"carriedForwardOpenQuestions\": [],\n152:   \"uncoveredQuestions\": [\n153:     \"Does the packet faithfully document the official Designer canvas, Bridge App, element tree, component, style, variable, and breakpoint model?\",\n154:     \"Does the packet cover CMS, publishing, branches, scripts, forms, localization, sites, assets, and compression semantics?\",\n155:     \"Does the packet cover webhooks, Enterprise, AI tools, Agent Instructions, WHTML, utility tools, and rate limits?\",\n156:     \"Does the local OSS/server documentation reconcile with the remote Webflow MCP surface and expose version or capability drift?\",\n157:     \"Which references, assets, feature cards, and manual scenarios are too concise or missing important logic?\",\n158:     \"What concrete P0/P1/P2, file-by-file additions are needed, with official or local citations?\"\n159:   ],\n160:   \"keyFindings\": [\n161:     {\n162:       \"id\": \"finding-1-5-p1-branch-isolation-is-documented-with-an-unsupported-or-underspecified-merge-im\",\n163:       \"text\": \"**P1 — Branch isolation is documented with an unsupported or underspecified merge implication.** Official documentation confirms creating, inspecting, and deleting page branches for isolated work. The local reference says edits remain isolated “until the branch merges” and calls branching a staging pattern, but the cited page action inventory contains create/delete/details/list operations and no merge action or merge procedure. Qualify the claim to the supported lifecycle and explicitly document whether merge is outside this MCP surface. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:133-137] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n164:       \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n165:       \"sources\": [\n166:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n167:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n168:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n169:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n170:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n171:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n172:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n173:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n174:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n175:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n176:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n177:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n178:       ]\n179:     },\n180:     {\n181:       \"id\": \"finding-1-4-p1-breakpoint-behavior-is-represented-as-read-only-and-indirect-while-the-offici\",\n182:       \"text\": \"**P1 — Breakpoint behavior is represented as read-only and indirect, while the official boundary includes changing the current breakpoint.** The packet documents `get_all_breakpoints` as a canvas-bound read and says responsive behavior flows indirectly through styles, but it does not state whether changing the active/current breakpoint is supported by the exposed remote version or is only a Designer UI operation. Official documentation explicitly includes reading or changing current breakpoints among the Bridge-App-dependent capabilities and separately promises responsive layouts across breakpoints. Reconcile the action inventory with the hosted capability claim, then add a version-qualified breakpoint-selection/verification scenario. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:123-129] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:71-82] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:443-469]\",\n183:       \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n184:       \"sources\": [\n185:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n186:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n187:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n188:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n189:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n190:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n191:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n192:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n193:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n194:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n195:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n196:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n197:       ]\n198:     },\n199:     {\n200:       \"id\": \"finding-1-1-p1-canvas-navigation-state-is-classified-inconsistently-the-packet-correctly-say\",\n201:       \"text\": \"**P1 — Canvas navigation/state is classified inconsistently.** The packet correctly says that canvas-bound page, mode, branch, component-view, selection, navigation, snapshots, and breakpoint operations need the Bridge App, and that data-plane operations can work without the canvas. However, `designer-capabilities.md` says that only `create_page_folder` and `open_canvas` are draft-write actions in this group, while the packet's own action table marks `close_component_view`, `open_component_view`, `select_element`, and `switch_page` as `DW`. The official documentation and repository README confirm the Bridge App/live-canvas boundary, but do not turn canvas navigation into site-tree content writes. The packet should distinguish Bridge-bound state/navigation mutations from site-tree draft writes and align the gate/class labels. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:25-48] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:443-469]\",\n202:       \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n203:       \"sources\": [\n204:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n205:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n206:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n207:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n208:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n209:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n210:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n211:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n212:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n213:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n214:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n215:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n216:       ]\n217:     },\n218:     {\n219:       \"id\": \"finding-1-2-p1-element-tree-discovery-is-too-concise-for-reliable-targeting-official-webflow\",\n220:       \"text\": \"**P1 — Element-tree discovery is too concise for reliable targeting.** Official Webflow documentation says elements can be found by type, text, style, tag, attribute, or component. The local packet names `query_elements` and `get_all_elements` but gives no query-key schema or worked selector examples; the action reference exposes only an opaque `queries[]` parameter. Add the supported query dimensions, target-id shape, and one discovery-to-mutation example to the shared Designer reference and payload/manual coverage. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:52-60] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-207]\",\n221:       \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n222:       \"sources\": [\n223:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n224:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n225:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n226:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n227:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n228:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n229:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n230:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n231:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n232:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n233:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n234:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n235:       ]\n236:     },\n237:     {\n238:       \"id\": \"finding-1-3-p1-style-coverage-omits-official-class-combo-class-and-raw-css-semantics-the-off\",\n239:       \"text\": \"**P1 — Style coverage omits official class/combo-class and raw-CSS semantics.** The official surface describes reusing or creating classes and combo classes, editing CSS properties, building styles from raw CSS, and managing styles across breakpoints. The local reference instead describes named styles, `properties[]`, and variable-mode bindings, without explaining class/combo-class identity or raw-CSS input. Add those distinctions and a safe create/update/read-back example; otherwise a reader can mistake the named-style lifecycle for the complete Designer style model. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:86-95] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-389]\",\n240:       \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n241:       \"sources\": [\n242:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n243:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n244:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n245:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n246:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n247:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n248:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n249:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n250:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n251:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n252:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n253:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n254:       ]\n255:     },\n256:     {\n257:       \"id\": \"finding-1-6-p1-the-component-variants-feature-card-is-stale-and-contradicts-the-packet-s-aut\",\n258:       \"text\": \"**P1 — The component-variants feature card is stale and contradicts the packet's authoritative action table.** Official documentation promises full component support for props, variants, slots, and metadata. The variant card claims “eight” actions but invents/assumes `update_variant`, `set_default_variant`, and generic list/get actions, while omitting the action-reference entries `duplicate_variant`, `set_variant_name`, `reorder_variants`, `set_variant_styles`, and `get_variant_styles`. Rewrite the card from the action table, including exact parameters and risk classes, and add a deterministic variant read/update/read-back scenario. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:173-184]\",\n259:       \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n260:       \"sources\": [\n261:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n262:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n263:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n264:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n265:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n266:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n267:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n268:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n269:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n270:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n271:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n272:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n273:       ]\n274:     },\n275:     {\n276:       \"id\": \"finding-1-7-p2-component-metadata-prop-constraints-and-slot-behavior-are-listed-but-not-oper\",\n277:       \"text\": \"**P2 — Component metadata, prop constraints, and slot behavior are listed but not operationally specified.** The shared reference gives useful high-level semantics for props, slots, variants, and component-view scoping, and it lists `set_component_metadata`, but it does not show metadata fields, prop type/default rules, slot validation, or a metadata/prop/slot read-back contract. This is concision/completeness debt rather than a missing safety boundary; add a component-builder example and verification checklist to the Designer card or payload/manual assets. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:98-119] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:71-82] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n278:       \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n279:       \"sources\": [\n280:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n281:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n282:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n283:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n284:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n285:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n286:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n287:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n288:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n289:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n290:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n291:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n292:       ]\n293:     },\n294:     {\n295:       \"id\": \"finding-1-8-p2-variable-mode-coverage-is-a-useful-workflow-summary-but-lacks-mode-value-read\",\n296:       \"text\": \"**P2 — Variable-mode coverage is a useful workflow summary but lacks mode/value/read-back detail.** The packet correctly describes collections, modes, typed variables, style bindings, and a second theme mode. It does not explain how per-mode values are populated and verified, how multiple bindings are inspected/removed, or whether the active canvas mode can be changed through the exposed action surface. Official documentation frames variables as design-system primitives for color schemes, typography, and spacing; expand the local mode matrix without claiming an unexposed active-mode operation. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:86-95] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-417]\",\n297:       \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n298:       \"sources\": [\n299:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n300:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n301:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n302:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n303:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n304:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n305:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n306:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n307:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n308:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n309:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n310:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n311:       ]\n312:     },\n313:     {\n314:       \"id\": \"finding-2-2-p0-contradictory-cms-publish-target-semantics-the-remote-action-inventory-and-da\",\n315:       \"text\": \"**P0 — Contradictory CMS publish-target semantics.** The remote action inventory and Data API publish endpoint define `publish_collection_items` with a collection and item IDs, not a domain or staging flag; the local baseline describes it as deploying drafts to live, and the CMS card explicitly says CMS item publish has no staging-domain target. However, the publish/deploy card labels the same action “staging-first” and its prompt says to publish collection drafts to the staging subdomain. That contradiction can make an operator believe an item publish is isolated to `*.webflow.io` when the item endpoint itself has no domain selector. Reconcile the card and prompts: describe item publish as a separate live CMS publish, reserve staging-subdomain language for `publish_site`, and add a confirmation/refusal scenario that prevents domain assumptions. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-73] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:26-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-35] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n316:       \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n317:       \"sources\": [\n318:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n319:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n320:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n321:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n322:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n323:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n324:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n325:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n326:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n327:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n328:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n329:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n330:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n331:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n332:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n333:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n334:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n335:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n336:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n337:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n338:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n339:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n340:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n341:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n342:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n343:       ]\n344:     },\n345:     {\n346:       \"id\": \"finding-2-1-p0-missing-unsafe-cms-draft-encoding-the-local-payload-example-labels-a-request-\",\n347:       \"text\": \"**P0 — Missing/unsafe CMS draft encoding.** The local payload example labels a request “CREATE A DRAFT COLLECTION ITEM” but sends only `fieldData`; the CMS pairing scenario likewise calls `create_collection_items` “(draft)” without an explicit draft field. Official Data API schemas expose `isDraft`, `isArchived`, `lastPublished`, and `cmsLocaleId`, while the official MCP guidance says items may be created directly in the live site or as queued/drafted items. The official OSS adapter accepts `isDraft` and defaults an omitted value to `false`, so the packet's example is not a reliable draft contract on the local surface. Add an explicit `isDraft: true` example, state remote/local differences beside the payload, and require a read-back assertion of `isDraft`, `lastPublished`, and locale before treating the write as draft-safe. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-55] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:24-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/SKILL.md:167-170] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n348:       \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n349:       \"sources\": [\n350:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n351:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n352:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n353:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n354:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n355:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n356:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n357:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n358:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n359:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n360:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n361:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n362:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n363:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n364:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n365:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n366:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n367:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n368:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n369:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n370:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n371:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n372:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n373:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n374:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n375:       ]\n376:     },\n377:     {\n378:       \"id\": \"finding-2-4-p1-missing-publish-completion-and-staged-blast-radius-checks-the-official-site-p\",\n379:       \"text\": \"**P1 — Missing publish completion and staged-blast-radius checks.** The official site-publish contract returns `202 Accepted`, requires either `customDomains` or `publishToWebflowSubdomain`, accepts an optional `pageId`, limits successful publish queues to one per minute, and warns that promoting staging to production publishes all staged changes after multiple page-to-staging publishes. The local feature card records the queue and broad staging rule, but the staging example and SAFE-001 scenario only capture a receipt and staged URL; they do not distinguish accepted from completed, assert `publishScope`, or test the “all staged changes” promotion case. Add a staging single-page scenario plus a separately gated production-promotion scenario with explicit domain choice, page/site scope, receipt fields, and post-publish verification. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:84-94]\",\n380:       \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n381:       \"sources\": [\n382:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n383:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n384:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n385:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n386:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n387:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n388:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n389:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n390:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n391:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n392:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n393:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n394:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n395:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n396:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n397:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n398:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n399:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n400:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n401:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n402:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n403:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n404:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n405:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n406:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n407:       ]\n408:     },\n409:     {\n410:       \"id\": \"finding-2-6-p1-missing-remote-local-page-branch-lifecycle-contract-official-mcp-documentatio\",\n411:       \"text\": \"**P1 — Missing remote/local page-branch lifecycle contract.** Official MCP documentation describes creating, inspecting, and deleting page branches. The remote action reference exposes `create_branch`, `list_branches`, `get_branch_details`, and `delete_branch`, but the local site-pages card says “page branches (create/update)” even though no `update_branch` action is listed, and the Designer reference says isolation lasts “until the branch merges” without identifying a merge action. The official OSS `dePages.ts` source exposes page creation/folders/current-page/switch-page but no branch lifecycle, so this is also a surface-boundary gap. Add a remote-only branch matrix with parent-page/current-branch readbacks, create/list/details/delete coverage, an explicit “merge is not exposed here” statement, and a deletion confirmation scenario; do not imply an automatic merge. This refines the prior merge concern with new surface-split and manual-coverage evidence. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:443-463] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:133-148] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-001.md:15]\",\n412:       \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n413:       \"sources\": [\n414:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n415:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n416:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n417:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n418:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n419:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n420:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n421:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n422:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n423:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n424:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n425:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n426:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n427:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n428:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n429:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n430:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n431:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n432:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n433:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n434:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n435:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n436:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n437:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n438:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n439:       ]\n440:     },\n441:     {\n442:       \"id\": \"finding-2-3-p1-too-concise-cms-read-verification-the-read-only-example-and-read-001-scenario\",\n443:       \"text\": \"**P1 — Too concise CMS read verification.** The read-only example and READ-001 scenario stop after “collection items returned,” and the draft pairing scenario stops after the create call. They do not require recording whether the returned item is draft or live, whether it is archived, which locale was addressed, or whether `lastPublished` changed. Those fields are part of the official item model, and the publish API also supports locale-specific item publication. Add before/after assertions and a locale-aware readback step to the CMS read and draft scenarios; otherwise a successful read cannot prove which content state the workflow inspected. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n444:       \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n445:       \"sources\": [\n446:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n447:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n448:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n449:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n450:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n451:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n452:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n453:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n454:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n455:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n456:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n457:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n458:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n459:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n460:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n461:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n462:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n463:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n464:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n465:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n466:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n467:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n468:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n469:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n470:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n471:       ]\n472:     },\n473:     {\n474:       \"id\": \"finding-2-5-p1-too-concise-page-settings-publish-boundary-the-official-repository-s-pages-to\",\n475:       \"text\": \"**P1 — Too concise page-settings publish boundary.** The official repository's pages tool describes page metadata reads as returning draft/published status and page-settings updates as including publishing status. The local packet acknowledges that `update_page_settings` can flip status, but the draft payload/example and DRAFT-001 scenario show no concrete body, status omission rule, or postcondition that the status stayed unchanged. The official changelog also records that slug updates can be silently ignored for home, collection-template, utility, and some secondary-locale pages. Add a status-safe DW payload, a separate explicit PB payload, and read-back checks for status and returned fields; document the slug/page-type/locale caveat so a `200` is not treated as proof that every requested setting applied. [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\",\n476:       \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n477:       \"sources\": [\n478:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n479:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n480:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n481:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n482:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n483:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n484:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n485:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n486:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n487:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n488:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n489:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n490:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n491:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n492:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n493:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n494:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n495:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n496:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n497:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n498:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n499:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n500:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n501:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n502:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n503:       ]\n504:     },\n505:     {\n506:       \"id\": \"finding-2-7-p2-missing-item-publish-unpublish-payload-and-manual-coverage-the-remote-action-\",\n507:       \"text\": \"**P2 — Missing item-publish/unpublish payload and manual coverage.** The remote action inventory includes both `publish_collection_items` and `unpublish_collection_items`, and the official publish schema supports bulk primary-locale IDs and locale-specific `cmsLocaleIds` with a response containing published IDs and errors. The packet has a CMS card row for publish/unpublish but its payload asset contains only draft creation and site publishing, while the manual playbook covers CMS reads and site publishing rather than item publish/unpublish. Add primary- and secondary-locale payload shapes, confirmation expectations, partial-error handling, and a deterministic publish-then-unpublish scenario. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-45] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n508:       \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n509:       \"sources\": [\n510:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n511:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n512:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n513:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n514:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n515:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n516:         \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n517:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n518:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n519:         \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n520:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n521:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n522:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n523:         \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n\n(Output capped at 50 KB. Showing lines 1-523. Use offset=524 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"sessionId\": \"fanout-luna-max-fast-1785753078466-rijm2e\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"terminalStop\": null,\n  \"keyQuestions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"Does the packet faithfully document the official Designer canvas, Bridge App, element tree, component, style, variable, and breakpoint model?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null,\n      \"resolved\": false\n    },","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/findings-registry.json","text":"{\n  \"sessionId\": \"fanout-luna-max-fast-1785753078466-rijm2e\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"terminalStop\": null,\n  \"keyQuestions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"Does the packet faithfully document the official Designer canvas, Bridge App, element tree, component, style, variable, and breakpoint model?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null,\n      \"resolved\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"Does the packet cover CMS, publishing, branches, scripts, forms, localization, sites, assets, and compression semantics?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null,\n      \"resolved\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"Does the packet cover webhooks, Enterprise, AI tools, Agent Instructions, WHTML, utility tools, and rate limits?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null,\n      \"resolved\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q4\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"Does the local OSS/server documentation reconcile with the remote Webflow MCP surface and expose version or capability drift?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null,\n      \"resolved\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q5\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"Which references, assets, feature cards, and manual scenarios are too concise or missing important logic?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null,\n      \"resolved\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q6\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"What concrete P0/P1/P2, file-by-file additions are needed, with official or local citations?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null,\n      \"resolved\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"openQuestions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"Does the packet faithfully document the official Designer canvas, Bridge App, element tree, component, style, variable, and breakpoint model?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"Does the packet cover CMS, publishing, branches, scripts, forms, localization, sites, assets, and compression semantics?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"Does the packet cover webhooks, Enterprise, AI tools, Agent Instructions, WHTML, utility tools, and rate limits?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q4\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"Does the local OSS/server documentation reconcile with the remote Webflow MCP surface and expose version or capability drift?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q5\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"Which references, assets, feature cards, and manual scenarios are too concise or missing important logic?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q6\",\n      \"inboxId\": null,\n      \"text\": \"What concrete P0/P1/P2, file-by-file additions are needed, with official or local citations?\",\n      \"origin\": \"operator\",\n      \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n      \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n      \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"resolvedQuestions\": [],\n  \"carriedForwardOpenQuestions\": [],\n  \"uncoveredQuestions\": [\n    \"Does the packet faithfully document the official Designer canvas, Bridge App, element tree, component, style, variable, and breakpoint model?\",\n    \"Does the packet cover CMS, publishing, branches, scripts, forms, localization, sites, assets, and compression semantics?\",\n    \"Does the packet cover webhooks, Enterprise, AI tools, Agent Instructions, WHTML, utility tools, and rate limits?\",\n    \"Does the local OSS/server documentation reconcile with the remote Webflow MCP surface and expose version or capability drift?\",\n    \"Which references, assets, feature cards, and manual scenarios are too concise or missing important logic?\",\n    \"What concrete P0/P1/P2, file-by-file additions are needed, with official or local citations?\"\n  ],\n  \"keyFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-1-5-p1-branch-isolation-is-documented-with-an-unsupported-or-underspecified-merge-im\",\n      \"text\": \"**P1 — Branch isolation is documented with an unsupported or underspecified merge implication.** Official documentation confirms creating, inspecting, and deleting page branches for isolated work. The local reference says edits remain isolated “until the branch merges” and calls branching a staging pattern, but the cited page action inventory contains create/delete/details/list operations and no merge action or merge procedure. Qualify the claim to the supported lifecycle and explicitly document whether merge is outside this MCP surface. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:133-137] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-1-4-p1-breakpoint-behavior-is-represented-as-read-only-and-indirect-while-the-offici\",\n      \"text\": \"**P1 — Breakpoint behavior is represented as read-only and indirect, while the official boundary includes changing the current breakpoint.** The packet documents `get_all_breakpoints` as a canvas-bound read and says responsive behavior flows indirectly through styles, but it does not state whether changing the active/current breakpoint is supported by the exposed remote version or is only a Designer UI operation. Official documentation explicitly includes reading or changing current breakpoints among the Bridge-App-dependent capabilities and separately promises responsive layouts across breakpoints. Reconcile the action inventory with the hosted capability claim, then add a version-qualified breakpoint-selection/verification scenario. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:123-129] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:71-82] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:443-469]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-1-1-p1-canvas-navigation-state-is-classified-inconsistently-the-packet-correctly-say\",\n      \"text\": \"**P1 — Canvas navigation/state is classified inconsistently.** The packet correctly says that canvas-bound page, mode, branch, component-view, selection, navigation, snapshots, and breakpoint operations need the Bridge App, and that data-plane operations can work without the canvas. However, `designer-capabilities.md` says that only `create_page_folder` and `open_canvas` are draft-write actions in this group, while the packet's own action table marks `close_component_view`, `open_component_view`, `select_element`, and `switch_page` as `DW`. The official documentation and repository README confirm the Bridge App/live-canvas boundary, but do not turn canvas navigation into site-tree content writes. The packet should distinguish Bridge-bound state/navigation mutations from site-tree draft writes and align the gate/class labels. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:25-48] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:443-469]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-1-2-p1-element-tree-discovery-is-too-concise-for-reliable-targeting-official-webflow\",\n      \"text\": \"**P1 — Element-tree discovery is too concise for reliable targeting.** Official Webflow documentation says elements can be found by type, text, style, tag, attribute, or component. The local packet names `query_elements` and `get_all_elements` but gives no query-key schema or worked selector examples; the action reference exposes only an opaque `queries[]` parameter. Add the supported query dimensions, target-id shape, and one discovery-to-mutation example to the shared Designer reference and payload/manual coverage. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:52-60] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-207]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-1-3-p1-style-coverage-omits-official-class-combo-class-and-raw-css-semantics-the-off\",\n      \"text\": \"**P1 — Style coverage omits official class/combo-class and raw-CSS semantics.** The official surface describes reusing or creating classes and combo classes, editing CSS properties, building styles from raw CSS, and managing styles across breakpoints. The local reference instead describes named styles, `properties[]`, and variable-mode bindings, without explaining class/combo-class identity or raw-CSS input. Add those distinctions and a safe create/update/read-back example; otherwise a reader can mistake the named-style lifecycle for the complete Designer style model. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:86-95] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-389]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-1-6-p1-the-component-variants-feature-card-is-stale-and-contradicts-the-packet-s-aut\",\n      \"text\": \"**P1 — The component-variants feature card is stale and contradicts the packet's authoritative action table.** Official documentation promises full component support for props, variants, slots, and metadata. The variant card claims “eight” actions but invents/assumes `update_variant`, `set_default_variant`, and generic list/get actions, while omitting the action-reference entries `duplicate_variant`, `set_variant_name`, `reorder_variants`, `set_variant_styles`, and `get_variant_styles`. Rewrite the card from the action table, including exact parameters and risk classes, and add a deterministic variant read/update/read-back scenario. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:173-184]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-1-7-p2-component-metadata-prop-constraints-and-slot-behavior-are-listed-but-not-oper\",\n      \"text\": \"**P2 — Component metadata, prop constraints, and slot behavior are listed but not operationally specified.** The shared reference gives useful high-level semantics for props, slots, variants, and component-view scoping, and it lists `set_component_metadata`, but it does not show metadata fields, prop type/default rules, slot validation, or a metadata/prop/slot read-back contract. This is concision/completeness debt rather than a missing safety boundary; add a component-builder example and verification checklist to the Designer card or payload/manual assets. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:98-119] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:71-82] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-1-8-p2-variable-mode-coverage-is-a-useful-workflow-summary-but-lacks-mode-value-read\",\n      \"text\": \"**P2 — Variable-mode coverage is a useful workflow summary but lacks mode/value/read-back detail.** The packet correctly describes collections, modes, typed variables, style bindings, and a second theme mode. It does not explain how per-mode values are populated and verified, how multiple bindings are inspected/removed, or whether the active canvas mode can be changed through the exposed action surface. Official documentation frames variables as design-system primitives for color schemes, typography, and spacing; expand the local mode matrix without claiming an unexposed active-mode operation. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:86-95] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-417]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-186]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:137-184]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:188-225]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:374-469]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:27-93]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-32]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-2-2-p0-contradictory-cms-publish-target-semantics-the-remote-action-inventory-and-da\",\n      \"text\": \"**P0 — Contradictory CMS publish-target semantics.** The remote action inventory and Data API publish endpoint define `publish_collection_items` with a collection and item IDs, not a domain or staging flag; the local baseline describes it as deploying drafts to live, and the CMS card explicitly says CMS item publish has no staging-domain target. However, the publish/deploy card labels the same action “staging-first” and its prompt says to publish collection drafts to the staging subdomain. That contradiction can make an operator believe an item publish is isolated to `*.webflow.io` when the item endpoint itself has no domain selector. Reconcile the card and prompts: describe item publish as a separate live CMS publish, reserve staging-subdomain language for `publish_site`, and add a confirmation/refusal scenario that prevents domain assumptions. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-73] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:26-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-35] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-2-1-p0-missing-unsafe-cms-draft-encoding-the-local-payload-example-labels-a-request-\",\n      \"text\": \"**P0 — Missing/unsafe CMS draft encoding.** The local payload example labels a request “CREATE A DRAFT COLLECTION ITEM” but sends only `fieldData`; the CMS pairing scenario likewise calls `create_collection_items` “(draft)” without an explicit draft field. Official Data API schemas expose `isDraft`, `isArchived`, `lastPublished`, and `cmsLocaleId`, while the official MCP guidance says items may be created directly in the live site or as queued/drafted items. The official OSS adapter accepts `isDraft` and defaults an omitted value to `false`, so the packet's example is not a reliable draft contract on the local surface. Add an explicit `isDraft: true` example, state remote/local differences beside the payload, and require a read-back assertion of `isDraft`, `lastPublished`, and locale before treating the write as draft-safe. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-55] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:24-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/SKILL.md:167-170] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-2-4-p1-missing-publish-completion-and-staged-blast-radius-checks-the-official-site-p\",\n      \"text\": \"**P1 — Missing publish completion and staged-blast-radius checks.** The official site-publish contract returns `202 Accepted`, requires either `customDomains` or `publishToWebflowSubdomain`, accepts an optional `pageId`, limits successful publish queues to one per minute, and warns that promoting staging to production publishes all staged changes after multiple page-to-staging publishes. The local feature card records the queue and broad staging rule, but the staging example and SAFE-001 scenario only capture a receipt and staged URL; they do not distinguish accepted from completed, assert `publishScope`, or test the “all staged changes” promotion case. Add a staging single-page scenario plus a separately gated production-promotion scenario with explicit domain choice, page/site scope, receipt fields, and post-publish verification. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:84-94]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-2-6-p1-missing-remote-local-page-branch-lifecycle-contract-official-mcp-documentatio\",\n      \"text\": \"**P1 — Missing remote/local page-branch lifecycle contract.** Official MCP documentation describes creating, inspecting, and deleting page branches. The remote action reference exposes `create_branch`, `list_branches`, `get_branch_details`, and `delete_branch`, but the local site-pages card says “page branches (create/update)” even though no `update_branch` action is listed, and the Designer reference says isolation lasts “until the branch merges” without identifying a merge action. The official OSS `dePages.ts` source exposes page creation/folders/current-page/switch-page but no branch lifecycle, so this is also a surface-boundary gap. Add a remote-only branch matrix with parent-page/current-branch readbacks, create/list/details/delete coverage, an explicit “merge is not exposed here” statement, and a deletion confirmation scenario; do not imply an automatic merge. This refines the prior merge concern with new surface-split and manual-coverage evidence. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:443-463] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:133-148] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-001.md:15]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-2-3-p1-too-concise-cms-read-verification-the-read-only-example-and-read-001-scenario\",\n      \"text\": \"**P1 — Too concise CMS read verification.** The read-only example and READ-001 scenario stop after “collection items returned,” and the draft pairing scenario stops after the create call. They do not require recording whether the returned item is draft or live, whether it is archived, which locale was addressed, or whether `lastPublished` changed. Those fields are part of the official item model, and the publish API also supports locale-specific item publication. Add before/after assertions and a locale-aware readback step to the CMS read and draft scenarios; otherwise a successful read cannot prove which content state the workflow inspected. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-2-5-p1-too-concise-page-settings-publish-boundary-the-official-repository-s-pages-to\",\n      \"text\": \"**P1 — Too concise page-settings publish boundary.** The official repository's pages tool describes page metadata reads as returning draft/published status and page-settings updates as including publishing status. The local packet acknowledges that `update_page_settings` can flip status, but the draft payload/example and DRAFT-001 scenario show no concrete body, status omission rule, or postcondition that the status stayed unchanged. The official changelog also records that slug updates can be silently ignored for home, collection-template, utility, and some secondary-locale pages. Add a status-safe DW payload, a separate explicit PB payload, and read-back checks for status and returned fields; document the slug/page-type/locale caveat so a `200` is not treated as proof that every requested setting applied. [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:20-37]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:21-46]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:31-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:31-40]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-30]\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"finding-2-7-p2-missing-item-publish-unpublish-payload-and-manual-coverage-the-remote-action-\",\n      \"text\": \"**P2 — Missing item-publish/unpublish payload and manual coverage.** The remote action inventory includes both `publish_collection_items` and `unpublish_collection_items`, and the official publish schema supports bulk primary-locale IDs and locale-specific `cmsLocaleIds` with a response containing published IDs and errors. The packet has a CMS card row for publish/unpublish but its payload asset contains only draft creation and site publishing, while the manual playbook covers CMS reads and site publishing rather than item publish/unpublish. Add primary- and secondary-locale payload shapes, confirmation expectations, partial-error handling, and a deterministic publish-then-unpublish scenario. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:22-45] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-30] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n      \"addedAtIteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/update-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/pages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:296-312]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:39-41]\",\n        \"[SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:67-89]\",","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":523,"totalLines":524,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/findings-registry.json","time":{"start":1785758249269,"end":1785758249274}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_042885e70c100df9016a708228b8208191804a1b8696fb704a"}},"id":"prt_fc77c70df001veDaGV78kqWc3L","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77c3232001xz8cdrrxNUA3rD"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758249367,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_IkAtdUt2LyYkIGR4mxA5DagM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/.deep-research.lock"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/.deep-research.lock</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"owner_pid\": 41624,\n3:   \"started_at_iso\": \"2026-08-03T10:37:41.595Z\",\n4:   \"ttl_ms\": 300000,\n5:   \"last_heartbeat_iso\": \"2026-08-03T10:37:41.595Z\",\n6:   \"packet_id\": \".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast\",\n7:   \"runtime_kind\": \"main\",\n8:   \"phase\": \"running\",\n9:   \"last_activity_iso\": \"2026-08-03T10:37:41.595Z\",\n10:   \"acquire_nonce\": \"41624-1785753461596-f3ab79f8-5b45-47e9-ae8a-61e95b19a72c\"\n11: }\n\n(End of file - total 11 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"owner_pid\": 41624,\n  \"started_at_iso\": \"2026-08-03T10:37:41.595Z\",\n  \"ttl_ms\": 300000,\n  \"last_heartbeat_iso\": \"2026-08-03T10:37:41.595Z\",\n  \"packet_id\": \".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast\",\n  \"runtime_kind\": \"main\",\n  \"phase\": \"running\",\n  \"last_activity_iso\": \"2026-08-03T10:37:41.595Z\",\n  \"acquire_nonce\": \"41624-1785753461596-f3ab79f8-5b45-47e9-ae8a-61e95b19a72c\"\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/.deep-research.lock","text":"{\n  \"owner_pid\": 41624,\n  \"started_at_iso\": \"2026-08-03T10:37:41.595Z\",\n  \"ttl_ms\": 300000,\n  \"last_heartbeat_iso\": \"2026-08-03T10:37:41.595Z\",\n  \"packet_id\": \".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast\",\n  \"runtime_kind\": \"main\",\n  \"phase\": \"running\",\n  \"last_activity_iso\": \"2026-08-03T10:37:41.595Z\",\n  \"acquire_nonce\": \"41624-1785753461596-f3ab79f8-5b45-47e9-ae8a-61e95b19a72c\"\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":11,"totalLines":11,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/.deep-research.lock","time":{"start":1785758249355,"end":1785758249366}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_042885e70c100df9016a708228b82881918606afc36ddc4d8b"}},"id":"prt_fc77c717a001qDbJtIeC2AYM37","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77c3232001xz8cdrrxNUA3rD"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758249447,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_pTUbjOsiFq6xYNDpE8oMX2iX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/research.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/research.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Progressive Research\n2: \n3: ## Iteration 1 — Designer canvas and Bridge App\n4: \n5: The packet has the core official boundary right: canvas-bound page/mode/branch/component-view/selection, snapshots, and breakpoint state require the Bridge App, while data-plane Designer modules can operate without the canvas; Designer edits remain draft-only until publish. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-30]\n6: \n7: The first audit identified eight packet-level gaps: inconsistent classification of Bridge-bound navigation, underspecified element queries, omitted class/combo-class/raw-CSS style semantics, ambiguous breakpoint-changing behavior, an unsupported/underspecified branch-merge implication, a stale component-variants card, concise component metadata/prop/slot rules, and concise variable-mode verification. [INFERENCE: based on the eight cited findings in `iterations/iteration-001.md`]\n8: \n9: ## Iteration 2 — CMS draft semantics, page/site publishing, and page branch lifecycle\n10: \n11: The CMS audit found two P0 contradictions: the draft example omits an explicit `isDraft: true` even though item state is explicit in the Data API and the local OSS adapter defaults an omitted value to false, and `publish_collection_items` is called “staging-first” in one card despite having no domain selector. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-55] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:24-35] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\n12: \n13: Four P1 gaps concern CMS state readback, site-publish completion/blast-radius checks, page-settings status-safe payloads, and remote/local branch lifecycle reconciliation. The branch result refines iteration 1: remote MCP documents create/inspect/delete branches, while the local OSS page source has no branch lifecycle and the packet supplies no merge or branch test contract. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\n14: \n15: One P2 gap is missing publish/unpublish payload and manual coverage, including locale-specific results and partial errors. The next pass should leave CMS item publish and branches closed and audit scripts, forms, localization, broader page/site metadata, and assets/compression. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\n16:  \n17: ## Iteration 3 — Scripts, forms, localization, metadata, and assets\n18: \n19: The remaining-Q2 audit found one P0 custom-code gate contradiction: the remote action table labels script registration/application as draft writes while `mcp-wiring.md` groups script registration with deploy confirmation, and the local OSS implementation has different register/apply/replacement semantics. Four P1 gaps concern forms/submission schemas and manual coverage, localization examples that promise unsupported locale management, omitted schema-markup/structured-data page actions, and missing asset/compression task lifecycle plus remote/local boundaries. One P2 gap is a page-metadata example/scenario that reads content instead of metadata. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-003.md:6-8]\n20: \n21: Official MCP, Data API, changelog, and repository evidence was compared with the action reference, local OSS baseline, feature cards, payload examples, and the 17-scenario index. No live MCP tool or credential was used. CMS item publish, page branches, and the prior slug-ignore result were intentionally not repeated. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/forms/forms/list.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/assets/assets/list.md] [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/webflow/mcp-server/contents/src/tools] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\n22: \n23: ## Iteration 4 — Webhooks, Enterprise, governance, WHTML, utility, and reliability\n24: \n25: The Q3 audit found one P0 robots safety gap: the packet treats whole-file `replace_robots_txt` as an ungated draft write without documenting the complete-replacement and unrestricted-user-agent consequences. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:228-244] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/SKILL.md:156-163] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/enterprise/site-configuration/robots-txt/put.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/enterprise/site-configuration/robots-txt/delete.md]\n26: \n27: Seven P1 gaps cover webhook delivery/signature/retry/auth lifecycle, Enterprise redirect/activity pagination and mixed-plan partial results, Agent Instruction provenance and resolution, utility/AI guide-first behavior, WHTML syntax/batching/readback, and structured error handling. One P2 gap records generic per-key/endpoint rate-limit guidance and an uncontrolled real-429 scenario. [INFERENCE: based on the eight cited findings in `iterations/iteration-004.md`]\n28: \n29: The current Data API webhook enum differs from the official OSS `main` enum, while the OSS Enterprise adapter preserves per-action successes and emits `isError`; these remain explicit version/surface contradictions because live discovery was prohibited. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/webhooks/create.md] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/webhooks.ts] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/enterprise.ts]\n30: \n31: ## Iteration 5 — Cross-focus completeness and residual authority reconciliation\n32: \n33: The final inventory audit covered all 5 named references, 2 shared assets, 5 worked examples, the feature-catalog root plus 9 cards, and all 17 manual scenarios. It found seven residual cross-focus issues rather than repeating the prior feature findings: one P0 reproducibility gap across the current hosted page, OSS README, and local endpoint/version claims; four P1 control defects covering release counts/metadata, wrong cross-reference destinations, invalid variable/sitemap payload shapes, and missing action-family traceability; and two P2 completeness gaps covering the seven-action Analyze slice and shared example provenance. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-005.md:1-16]\n34: \n35: The official OSS export list matches the local 18-module baseline at module level, but the deployed surface remains unresolved: the official hosted page, OSS README, and packet disagree on remote endpoint/capabilities, while local registration still uses `@latest`. Final synthesis should require a dated endpoint/package/commit/tool-schema fixture and keep the live-discovery gate explicit. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/index.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:113-138]\n\n(End of file - total 35 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Progressive Research\n\n## Iteration 1 — Designer canvas and Bridge App\n\nThe packet has the core official boundary right: canvas-bound page/mode/branch/component-view/selection, snapshots, and breakpoint state require the Bridge App, while data-plane Designer modules can operate without the canvas; Designer edits remain draft-only until publish. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-30]\n\nThe first audit identified eight packet-level gaps: inconsistent classification of Bridge-bound navigation, underspecified element queries, omitted class/combo-class/raw-CSS style semantics, ambiguous breakpoint-changing behavior, an unsupported/underspecified branch-merge implication, a stale component-variants card, concise component metadata/prop/slot rules, and concise variable-mode verification. [INFERENCE: based on the eight cited findings in `iterations/iteration-001.md`]\n\n## Iteration 2 — CMS draft semantics, page/site publishing, and page branch lifecycle\n\nThe CMS audit found two P0 contradictions: the draft example omits an explicit `isDraft: true` even though item state is explicit in the Data API and the local OSS adapter defaults an omitted value to false, and `publish_collection_items` is called “staging-first” in one card despite having no domain selector. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-55] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:24-35] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\n\nFour P1 gaps concern CMS state readback, site-publish completion/blast-radius checks, page-settings status-safe payloads, and remote/local branch lifecycle reconciliation. The branch result refines iteration 1: remote MCP documents create/inspect/delete branches, while the local OSS page source has no branch lifecycle and the packet supplies no merge or branch test contract. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\n\nOne P2 gap is missing publish/unpublish payload and manual coverage, including locale-specific results and partial errors. The next pass should leave CMS item publish and branches closed and audit scripts, forms, localization, broader page/site metadata, and assets/compression. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\n \n## Iteration 3 — Scripts, forms, localization, metadata, and assets\n\nThe remaining-Q2 audit found one P0 custom-code gate contradiction: the remote action table labels script registration/application as draft writes while `mcp-wiring.md` groups script registration with deploy confirmation, and the local OSS implementation has different register/apply/replacement semantics. Four P1 gaps concern forms/submission schemas and manual coverage, localization examples that promise unsupported locale management, omitted schema-markup/structured-data page actions, and missing asset/compression task lifecycle plus remote/local boundaries. One P2 gap is a page-metadata example/scenario that reads content instead of metadata. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-003.md:6-8]\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/research.md","text":"# Progressive Research\n\n## Iteration 1 — Designer canvas and Bridge App\n\nThe packet has the core official boundary right: canvas-bound page/mode/branch/component-view/selection, snapshots, and breakpoint state require the Bridge App, while data-plane Designer modules can operate without the canvas; Designer edits remain draft-only until publish. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-30]\n\nThe first audit identified eight packet-level gaps: inconsistent classification of Bridge-bound navigation, underspecified element queries, omitted class/combo-class/raw-CSS style semantics, ambiguous breakpoint-changing behavior, an unsupported/underspecified branch-merge implication, a stale component-variants card, concise component metadata/prop/slot rules, and concise variable-mode verification. [INFERENCE: based on the eight cited findings in `iterations/iteration-001.md`]\n\n## Iteration 2 — CMS draft semantics, page/site publishing, and page branch lifecycle\n\nThe CMS audit found two P0 contradictions: the draft example omits an explicit `isDraft: true` even though item state is explicit in the Data API and the local OSS adapter defaults an omitted value to false, and `publish_collection_items` is called “staging-first” in one card despite having no domain selector. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-55] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/create-item.md] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/cms.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:24-35] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\n\nFour P1 gaps concern CMS state readback, site-publish completion/blast-radius checks, page-settings status-safe payloads, and remote/local branch lifecycle reconciliation. The branch result refines iteration 1: remote MCP documents create/inspect/delete branches, while the local OSS page source has no branch lifecycle and the packet supplies no merge or branch test contract. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-30] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server/blob/main/src/tools/dePages.ts]\n\nOne P2 gap is missing publish/unpublish payload and manual coverage, including locale-specific results and partial errors. The next pass should leave CMS item publish and branches closed and audit scripts, forms, localization, broader page/site metadata, and assets/compression. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:100-119] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/cms/collection-items/staged-items/publish-item.md]\n \n## Iteration 3 — Scripts, forms, localization, metadata, and assets\n\nThe remaining-Q2 audit found one P0 custom-code gate contradiction: the remote action table labels script registration/application as draft writes while `mcp-wiring.md` groups script registration with deploy confirmation, and the local OSS implementation has different register/apply/replacement semantics. Four P1 gaps concern forms/submission schemas and manual coverage, localization examples that promise unsupported locale management, omitted schema-markup/structured-data page actions, and missing asset/compression task lifecycle plus remote/local boundaries. One P2 gap is a page-metadata example/scenario that reads content instead of metadata. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-003.md:6-8]\n\nOfficial MCP, Data API, changelog, and repository evidence was compared with the action reference, local OSS baseline, feature cards, payload examples, and the 17-scenario index. No live MCP tool or credential was used. CMS item publish, page branches, and the prior slug-ignore result were intentionally not repeated. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/forms/forms/list.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/assets/assets/list.md] [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/webflow/mcp-server/contents/src/tools] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/5/12.md]\n\n## Iteration 4 — Webhooks, Enterprise, governance, WHTML, utility, and reliability\n\nThe Q3 audit found one P0 robots safety gap: the packet treats whole-file `replace_robots_txt` as an ungated draft write without documenting the complete-replacement and unrestricted-user-agent consequences. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:228-244] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/SKILL.md:156-163] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/enterprise/site-configuration/robots-txt/put.md] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/enterprise/site-configuration/robots-txt/delete.md]\n\nSeven P1 gaps cover webhook delivery/signature/retry/auth lifecycle, Enterprise redirect/activity pagination and mixed-plan partial results, Agent Instruction provenance and resolution, utility/AI guide-first behavior, WHTML syntax/batching/readback, and structured error handling. One P2 gap records generic per-key/endpoint rate-limit guidance and an uncontrolled real-429 scenario. [INFERENCE: based on the eight cited findings in `iterations/iteration-004.md`]\n\nThe current Data API webhook enum differs from the official OSS `main` enum, while the OSS Enterprise adapter preserves per-action successes and emits `isError`; these remain explicit version/surface contradictions because live discovery was prohibited. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/webhooks/create.md] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/webhooks.ts] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/enterprise.ts]\n\n## Iteration 5 — Cross-focus completeness and residual authority reconciliation\n\nThe final inventory audit covered all 5 named references, 2 shared assets, 5 worked examples, the feature-catalog root plus 9 cards, and all 17 manual scenarios. It found seven residual cross-focus issues rather than repeating the prior feature findings: one P0 reproducibility gap across the current hosted page, OSS README, and local endpoint/version claims; four P1 control defects covering release counts/metadata, wrong cross-reference destinations, invalid variable/sitemap payload shapes, and missing action-family traceability; and two P2 completeness gaps covering the seven-action Analyze slice and shared example provenance. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-005.md:1-16]\n\nThe official OSS export list matches the local 18-module baseline at module level, but the deployed surface remains unresolved: the official hosted page, OSS README, and packet disagree on remote endpoint/capabilities, while local registration still uses `@latest`. Final synthesis should require a dated endpoint/package/commit/tool-schema fixture and keep the live-discovery gate explicit. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/index.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:113-138]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":35,"totalLines":35,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/research.md","time":{"start":1785758249433,"end":1785758249442}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_042885e70c100df9016a708228b82c8191b60ce7e08749b547"}},"id":"prt_fc77c718c001Fb7eyi0jKuUsFQ","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc77c3232001xz8cdrrxNUA3rD"}}
