-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md\",\".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md\",\".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/utcp-manual-reference.md\",\".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md\",\".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md\",\".opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-03T08:50:00Z\",\"durationMs\":420...","metadata":{"matches":21,"truncated":false},"title":"resolvedQuestions|answeredQuestions|metrics|iterationsCompleted|terminalStop|sessionId|sourceFindings","time":{"start":1785758542585,"end":1785758542599}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0279449cd724e0ba016a70834e5bac819196c2901a8d2fb1e6"}},"id":"prt_fc780ea720017jO63o2RoqrHgT","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc7806c81001lp4f9k5O0rIvX5"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785758542621,"sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_Qy7fzrP5P0Y7QGm2BzZhg684","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-005.md","offset":1,"limit":260},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-005.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Iteration 5: Cross-focus completeness and residual authority reconciliation\n2: \n3: ## Focus\n4: \n5: This final iteration audited the requested inventory as one documentation system rather than reopening the feature-level gaps already recorded in iterations 1–4. The explicit iteration-005 override was followed over the reducer's stale prior next-focus text. The audit covered **5/5 named references**, **2/2 shared assets**, **5/5 `assets/examples/*` files**, **1/1 feature-catalog root plus 9/9 cards**, and **17/17 manual-testing-playbook scenarios**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:5-13] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-31]\n6: \n7: ## Findings\n8: \n9: 1. **P0 — The remote/local authority boundary is still not reproducible from the packet.** The current official hosted landing page directs AI-client integration to `developers.webflow.com/_mcp/server`, the official OSS README configures the remote service at `https://mcp.webflow.com/sse` and says the OSS implementation has no MCP `prompts` or `resources`, while the packet treats `https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp` as the hosted endpoint and describes remote resources/Agent Instructions. Separately, the local registration and server pointer still launch `webflow-mcp-server@latest`; the packet says to pin after discovery but contains no pinned package version, OSS commit, endpoint fixture, or `tool_info`/schema evidence. The official OSS export list does align with the packet's 18-module baseline, so the unresolved problem is provenance and reproducibility, not an invented module mismatch. Add one dated surface fixture containing transport, endpoint, package version/commit, tool count, action-schema digest, and `prompts`/`resources` presence; make DISCOVER-001/002/003 and the first-session example consume that fixture, and replace `@latest` after pinning. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/index.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:22-39] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:113-138] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:18-24] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md:12-18] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-30]\n10: \n11: 2. **P1 — Packet release metadata and scenario counts disagree.** The packet README and manual playbook release-readiness text say “16” scenarios even though the playbook inventory and the actual files contain 17; the five named references also carry mixed versions (`1.0.0.0` through `1.2.0.0`), while the feature root is `1.2.0.0` and the skill/README are `1.3.0.0`. Several feature cards omit a version field entirely. This is a release-integrity defect: an operator cannot tell whether the 17-file corpus and the 31-tool/220-action inventory were audited from one coherent packet revision. Add a single packet freshness/version table, correct every 16→17 claim, require version metadata on every card/example/scenario, and add a CI check that counts files and rejects mixed release stamps. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/README.md:33-38] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/README.md:51-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:79-84] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:1-10] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:1-14] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:1-11] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:1-13] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/troubleshooting.md:1-12] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:1-9]\n12: \n13: 3. **P1 — The catalog and playbook cross-reference graph contains wrong destinations.** The feature-catalog root's CMS “Source Files” row points to `design/component-variants.md` instead of `content/cms.md`. The manual root maps PAIR-002, whose contract is explicitly data-family transport-only, to the Designer card, and `pairing/pair-data.md` repeats that wrong feature path. Correct those links and add a link-integrity check that validates each scenario's feature file against its category/action family; otherwise a reader following the canonical map can load the opposite pairing rule or the wrong capability card. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:64-77] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:128-147] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:63-86] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:48-69] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:102-127]\n14: \n15: 4. **P1 — The shared payload asset contains shapes that do not match the named action contract.** It claims to provide shapes built from official required-parameter lists, but the color-variable example supplies only `siteId`, `pageId`, and `value`, while `create_color_variable` requires `variable_collection_id`, `variable_name`, and `value`; the sitemap example uses `pageIds`/`sitemapStatus`, while the action reference names `bulk_update_pages_sitemap_status` with `site_id` and `pages[]` and separate item/page `includeInSitemap` operations. These are not merely omitted optional fields: they cannot be used to identify a valid payload for the cited MCP actions. Rewrite each block with its exact tool/action name, surface, global parameters, required fields, and expected response; label any illustrative REST/UI shape separately. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:60-79] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:345-358] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:393-408]\n16: \n17: 5. **P1 — The 17-scenario corpus is category-complete but not capability-traceable.** The root correctly enumerates 17 scenarios, yet the scenario index records category and file only; it does not map each remote action family or each scenario to an exact action schema, surface, version fixture, or explicit `UNTESTED/SKIP` state. DISCOVER-001/002/003 compare `list_tools()` and counts, but do not require `tool_info`/action-schema comparison, endpoint recording, or resource/prompt capability checks. As a result, the corpus can report readiness while leaving remote-only families and remote/local drift unverified. This is a residual control defect, not a re-listing of the feature-specific gaps already recorded in iterations 1–4. Add a coverage matrix to `manual-testing-playbook.md` with action-family → scenario IDs → surface/version → evidence/skip reason, and make the discovery scenarios verify the pinned fixture before any action call. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-43] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:99-119] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:34-491] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/discover.md:20-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/discover-drift.md:20-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-50] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\n18: \n19: 6. **P2 — Analyze is represented as a card and one scenario, but not as an operational seven-action slice.** The action reference names seven Analyze actions with distinct parameters; `intelligence/analyze.md` collapses four report families into generic prose, and READ-003 exercises only `get_query_guide` plus `get_traffic_report`. Add exact names/parameters for top pages, top dimensions, top events, and time-on-page, then either add deterministic scenarios or explicitly mark those actions as untested/skip-eligible when the Analyze add-on is absent. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:51-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/analyze.md:20-39] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/analyze.md:20-59] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\n20: \n21: 7. **P2 — The five worked examples lack a shared surface/provenance/postcondition contract.** `first-session-discovery.md`, `read-cms-content.md`, `destructive-refused.md`, `staging-publish.md`, and `draft-page-settings.md` all provide useful operator narratives, but after their generic `list_tools()` step they do not carry a common exact surface/version field, action-schema source, or machine-checkable expected response. The first-session example says to pin and update fixtures, while the other four remain version-neutral, so examples can drift away from the action reference without being recognized as stale. Add frontmatter or a table to every example for `surface`, pinned version/fixture, tool/action, required schema source, postcondition, and known-unknowns; keep feature-specific corrections from iterations 1–4 in their existing findings rather than duplicating them here. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/first-session-discovery.md:19-38] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:19-41] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/destructive-refused.md:19-40] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:19-40] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:19-40]\n22: \n23: ## Residual Recommendation Matrix\n24: \n25: | Severity | Exact files | Required addition |\n26: |---|---|---|\n27: | P0 | `references/mcp-wiring.md`, `references/tool-surface.md`, `assets/utcp-manual-reference.md`, `mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md`, `manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/{discover,discover-drift,remote-surface}.md`, `assets/examples/first-session-discovery.md` | One dated endpoint/transport/package-or-commit/tool-schema/resource fixture; pin the server after capture; make discovery consume and verify it. |\n28: | P1 | `README.md`, `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`, all five named references, all nine feature cards, all five examples, and all 17 scenario files | One packet freshness/version stamp and generated count check; correct 16→17 claims and reject missing/mixed metadata. |\n29: | P1 | `feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md`, `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`, `manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md` | Correct CMS and PAIR-002 destinations; add category/action-family link-integrity validation. |\n30: | P1 | `assets/payload-examples.md`, `references/action-reference.md` | Replace variable/sitemap examples with exact MCP tool/action schemas, global parameters, required fields, and response assertions. |\n31: | P1 | `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`, all 17 scenario files, `references/action-reference.md` | Add action-family → scenario → surface/version → evidence/skip traceability and schema-aware discovery checks. |\n32: | P2 | `feature-catalog/intelligence/analyze.md`, `manual-testing-playbook/read-only/analyze.md`, `references/action-reference.md` | Enumerate all seven Analyze actions and cover or explicitly skip the four report families not exercised by READ-003. |\n33: | P2 | `assets/examples/*.md` (all five) | Add shared surface, pinned fixture, tool/action, schema source, postcondition, and known-unknown fields. |\n34: \n35: ## Coverage Matrix\n36: \n37: ### Five named references\n38: \n39: | Artifact | Audit result | Residual disposition |\n40: |---|---|---|\n41: | `references/action-reference.md` | Present; the remote 31-tool/220-action inventory and required-parameter tables are complete as a static snapshot. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:17-33] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:494-498] | Participates in Findings 1, 2, and 5; no prior feature gap reissued. |\n42: | `references/designer-capabilities.md` | Present; supplies the canvas/edit-loop, element, style, component, breakpoint, and worked-flow model. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-30] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:154-186] | Shared metadata/fixture debt only; prior Designer findings remain in iteration 1. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-001.md:7-23] |\n43: | `references/tool-surface.md` | Present; its 18-module OSS inventory matches the official OSS export family at the module-list level and explicitly labels itself a baseline. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:18-24] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/index.ts] | No pinned commit/package fixture; Findings 1, 2, and 5. |\n44: | `references/mcp-wiring.md` | Present; documents local stdio, remote alternative, auth, scopes, Bridge App, and the endpoint contradiction. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:22-39] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:113-138] | P0 reproducibility/endpoint fixture; Finding 1. |\n45: | `references/troubleshooting.md` | Present; covers discovery, auth, rate, publish, Bridge App, drift, workflows/webhooks, and redaction. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/troubleshooting.md:19-23] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/troubleshooting.md:79-103] | Its pinned-version recovery path depends on the missing fixture; Findings 1–2, with prior error/rate findings not reissued. |\n46: \n47: ### Shared assets and `examples/*`\n48: \n49: | Artifact | Audit result | Residual disposition |\n50: |---|---|---|\n51: | `assets/utcp-manual-reference.md` | Present; accurately describes the registered stdio shape and says exact pinning is required, but its canonical example remains `@latest`. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/utcp-manual-reference.md:19-33] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/utcp-manual-reference.md:37-71] | Finding 1. |\n52: | `assets/payload-examples.md` | Present; five representative sections exist, but variable and sitemap blocks are not valid shapes for the named action contracts. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94] | Finding 4; prior CMS/publish findings are not repeated. |\n53: | `assets/examples/first-session-discovery.md` | Present; useful discovery/pin narrative, but no concrete fixture fields or `tool_info`/schema step. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/first-session-discovery.md:19-38] | Findings 1 and 7. |\n54: | `assets/examples/read-cms-content.md` | Present; read-only narrative and evidence step are present. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:19-41] | Finding 7; feature-level CMS/page readback issue remains only in iteration 2–3. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-002.md:7-19] |\n55: | `assets/examples/destructive-refused.md` | Present; refusal and rollback narrative is present. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/destructive-refused.md:19-40] | Finding 7; no new destructive-feature gap reissued. |\n56: | `assets/examples/staging-publish.md` | Present; confirmation, staging target, page scope, queue, and evidence narrative are present. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:19-40] | Finding 7; prior publish-completion finding remains in iteration 2. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-002.md:13] |\n57: | `assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md` | Present; before/after and no-status-flip narrative is present. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:19-40] | Finding 7; prior page-settings finding remains in iteration 2. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-002.md:15] |\n58: \n59: ### Feature-catalog root and all nine cards\n60: \n61: | Artifact | Audit result | Residual disposition |\n62: |---|---|---|\n63: | `feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` | Present; lists 21 remote groups and links nine cards, but the CMS source link is wrong and its release stamp/count claims need the shared freshness check. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:20-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:61-77] | Findings 2–3. |\n64: | `feature-catalog/design/designer.md` | Present; usable card with Bridge, edit-loop, action, safety, and source sections. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:19-69] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:102-127] | Shared metadata/traceability only; prior Designer findings not reissued. |\n65: | `feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md` | Present; card is discoverable and linked, but its feature-level action contradiction is already recorded. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/component-variants.md:11-41] | Prior P1 retained from iteration 1; no duplicate finding. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-001.md:17] |\n66: | `feature-catalog/content/cms.md` | Present; card includes capabilities, gates, semantics, examples, and links. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:18-45] | Prior CMS P0/P1 findings retained from iteration 2; root link defect is Finding 3. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-002.md:7-19] |\n67: | `feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md` | Present; card covers site/CMS/workflow classes, staging boundary, queue, rollback, and examples. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/publish-deploy.md:18-43] | Prior publish/P0–P1 findings retained from iteration 2; not reissued. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-002.md:9-19] |\n68: | `feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md` | Present; aggregates sites, pages, scripts, webhooks, Enterprise, AI, comments, and rules. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/site-pages-scripts.md:17-45] | Prior scripts/forms/site/webhook/Enterprise/utility findings retained; no feature reissue. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-003.md:7-17] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-004.md:7-21] |\n69: | `feature-catalog/content/localization-fonts-forms.md` | Present; groups localization, fonts, and forms with actions, semantics, examples, and links. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/localization-fonts-forms.md:17-55] | Prior localization/forms findings retained from iteration 3; not reissued. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-003.md:9-15] |\n70: | `feature-catalog/operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md` | Present; groups sitemap, scripts, assets, and WHTML with action classes and examples. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/operations/sitemap-scripts-assets-whtml.md:17-61] | Prior scripts/assets/WHTML findings retained from iterations 3–4; not reissued. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-003.md:7-17] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-004.md:17] |\n71: | `feature-catalog/intelligence/agent-instructions.md` | Present; action table, path/cascade semantics, examples, and source sections are present. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/agent-instructions.md:20-44] | Prior provenance/read-resolution finding retained from iteration 4; no duplicate. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-004.md:13] |\n72: | `feature-catalog/intelligence/analyze.md` | Present; add-on, three named actions, generic report families, semantics, and prompts are present, but the seven-action surface is not enumerated. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/analyze.md:11-39] | Finding 6. |\n73: \n74: ### All seventeen manual-testing-playbook scenarios\n75: \n76: | ID / file | Audit result | Residual disposition |\n77: |---|---|---|\n78: | DISCOVER-001 / `discovery-setup/discover.md` | Present; discovery, namespace filter, baseline comparison, evidence, and triage are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/discover.md:20-59] | Findings 1, 2, and 5: add fixture/schema verification. |\n79: | DISCOVER-002 / `discovery-setup/discover-drift.md` | Present; drift diff, refusal, dated fixture, and triage are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/discover-drift.md:20-59] | Findings 1 and 5. |\n80: | DISCOVER-003 / `discovery-setup/remote-surface.md` | Present; remote/local counts, surface verdict, and version pin are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-59] | Findings 1 and 5: counts alone cannot close the endpoint/version edge. |\n81: | READ-001 / `read-only/readcms.md` | Present; RO classification, CMS read, evidence, and scope triage are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readcms.md:20-59] | Prior CMS readback finding only; no new reissue. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-002.md:11] |\n82: | READ-002 / `read-only/readpages.md` | Present; RO page/content read, evidence, and scope triage are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/readpages.md:20-59] | Prior page-metadata finding only; no new reissue. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-003.md:15] |\n83: | READ-003 / `read-only/analyze.md` | Present; guide-first traffic report and add-on skip behavior are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/analyze.md:20-59] | Finding 6: extend or explicitly mark the other Analyze actions. |\n84: | DRAFT-001 / `draft-write/draftset.md` | Present; DW page settings, before/after evidence, and no publish receipt are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/draftset.md:20-59] | Prior page-settings finding only; no new reissue. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-002.md:15] |\n85: | DRAFT-002 / `draft-write/instructions.md` | Present; create/update DW and cascading delete DS gate are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/draft-write/instructions.md:20-59] | Prior Agent Instructions finding only; no new reissue. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-004.md:13] |\n86: | DRAFT-003 / `designer-edit/designer-edit.md` | Present; Bridge/edit loop, sk-design pairing, before/after snapshots, and no publish are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/designer-edit/designer-edit.md:20-59] | Prior Designer findings only; no new reissue. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-001.md:7-23] |\n87: | SAFE-001 / `safety-gate/pubgate.md` | Present; PB confirmation, staging flag, single page, receipt, and queue evidence are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-59] | Prior publish-completion finding only; no new reissue. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-002.md:13] |\n88: | SAFE-002 / `safety-gate/refuse.md` | Present; DS and production-publish refusal with zero-call evidence are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/refuse.md:20-59] | No new residual beyond Findings 1–2 provenance controls. |\n89: | SAFE-003 / `safety-gate/rate-limit.md` | Present; real-429 trigger, headers, Retry-After, and no-replay evidence are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/rate-limit.md:20-59] | Prior rate-limit finding only; no new reissue. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-004.md:21] |\n90: | SAFE-004 / `safety-gate/deploygate.md` | Present; local-OSS `run_workflow` DP confirmation, environment, rollback, and receipt are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/deploygate.md:20-59] | Local-only scope is named; no new feature finding. |\n91: | SAFE-005 / `safety-gate/bulkgate.md` | Present; selection enumeration and destructive bulk confirmation are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/bulkgate.md:20-59] | Included in Finding 5's capability-traceability gap; no prior feature issue reissued. |\n92: | PAIR-001 / `pairing/pair.md` | Present; sk-design-before-Designer-call order and DW class are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair.md:20-59] | No new residual. |\n93: | PAIR-002 / `pairing/pair-data.md` | Present; transport-only data-family behavior is specified, but its feature-file cross-reference points to the Designer card. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:63-86] | Finding 3. |\n94: | NEG-001 / `negative/non-webflow.md` | Present; non-Webflow and sibling-intent deferral with zero Webflow calls are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/negative/non-webflow.md:20-59] | No new residual. |\n95: \n96: ## Ruled Out\n97: \n98: - No Webflow MCP tool, credential, OAuth flow, mutation, publish call, or live-site test was attempted; the final prompt explicitly prohibited those actions. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:11-13]\n99: - Prior Designer, CMS/publish, scripts/forms/localization/assets, webhook/Enterprise/WHTML/utility, and rate-limit feature findings were not reissued; this pass records only cross-focus residuals and the Analyze slice not previously audited. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-001.md:25-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-002.md:21-28] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-003.md:19-27] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-004.md:23-30]\n100: - No static source was treated as proof of the deployed endpoint or live action schema; the unresolved three-way hosted/OSS/local contradiction remains an explicit unknown for a future permitted fixture. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:127-138]\n101: \n102: ## Dead Ends\n103: \n104: - Static comparison cannot resolve which remote endpoint, package release, action schema, or `prompts`/`resources` capability the operator's pinned session will expose; live discovery is the smallest missing evidence, not a reason to infer a winner. [INFERENCE: based on the official hosted page, official OSS README, OSS module export list, and local surface-reconciliation contract] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/index.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:127-138]\n105: - Counting `list_tools()` entries alone is insufficient to validate the 220-action remote snapshot or its safety classes; no further static count variation was found after the complete inventory audit. [INFERENCE: based on action-reference counts and the three discovery scenario contracts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:17-24] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/discover.md:20-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-50]\n106: \n107: ## Edge Cases\n108: \n109: - Ambiguous input: the reducer's prior next focus mentions rate limits, but the explicit iteration-005 prompt selects cross-focus completeness and overrides that suggestion; the narrower explicit focus was used. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/deep-research-strategy.md:224-226] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:5-13]\n110: - Contradictory evidence: current hosted Webflow guidance, the official OSS README, and the local packet disagree on the remote endpoint and capability surface; all claims are preserved, and no resolution is asserted without live discovery. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:113-138]\n111: - Missing dependency: authenticated `list_tools`/`tool_info` and a provisioned test site were unavailable by explicit constraint; official hosted/OSS static sources and complete local inventory supplied the fallback. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/README.md:27-29] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:11-13]\n112: - Partial success: none for the selected static audit; every requested artifact was read and classified, but live endpoint/version behavior remains unknown. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-31]\n113: \n114: ## Sources Consulted\n115: \n116: - [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\n117: - [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md]\n118: - [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/index.ts]\n119: - [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:17-33]\n120: - [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:18-56]\n121: - [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:22-39]\n122: - [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:113-138]\n123: - [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/utcp-manual-reference.md:19-71]\n124: - [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-94]\n125: - [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:20-233]\n126: - [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-148]\n127: - All five named references, both shared assets, all five worked examples, the feature-catalog root and nine cards, and all 17 scenario files listed in the Coverage Matrix.\n128: \n129: ## Assessment\n130: \n131: - New information ratio: **1.00** — seven fully new cross-focus findings; no prior feature-level finding was counted again.\n132: - Severity: **1 P0**, **4 P1**, **2 P2**.\n133: - Inventory coverage: **5/5 references**, **2/2 shared assets**, **5/5 examples**, **1/1 feature root**, **9/9 cards**, **17/17 scenarios**.\n134: - Questions addressed: Q4 residual remote/local/version reconciliation, Q5 complete artifact inventory, and Q6 residual file-by-file severity recommendations.\n135: - Questions answered: Q5 inventory completeness and Q6 residual recommendation matrix. Q4 remains partially unresolved until a permitted pinned live fixture exists.\n136: - Bounded live-discovery checks still unknown: record the actual remote/local endpoint and transport, package version or OSS commit, `list_tools` plus `tool_info` action schemas, 31/220 versus 18-module surface, resource/prompt availability, and the two payload schemas called out in Finding 4. [INFERENCE: based on Findings 1, 4, and 5]\n137: \n138: ## Reflection\n139: \n140: - What worked and why: reading the complete requested inventory before synthesis exposed cross-file defects that individual feature passes could not: wrong canonical links, stale corpus counts, invalid shared payload shapes, and missing provenance between a static reference and a live surface. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:61-77] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-31]\n141: - What did not work and why: live discovery could not be used because the dispatch prohibited Webflow MCP tools and credentials, so endpoint/version/resource contradictions remain unresolved rather than being collapsed into a confident claim. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:11-13]\n142: - What I would do differently: with an authorized fixture, run the discovery matrix first, persist the endpoint/package/commit/schema evidence, then use it as the sole authority for card, payload, example, and scenario validation; do not infer remote behavior from OSS `main`. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:20-24] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:135-138]\n143: \n144: ## Recommended Next Focus\n145: \n146: Synthesis/closeout should merge only these seven residual cross-focus findings into the final research output, preserve the prior iteration findings without duplication, and mark the endpoint/version/action-schema fixture as the explicit unresolved verification gate. No further broad research iteration is recommended under the five-iteration stop policy. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/deep-research-config.json:4-16] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:5-9]\n\n(End of file - total 146 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Iteration 5: Cross-focus completeness and residual authority reconciliation\n\n## Focus\n\nThis final iteration audited the requested inventory as one documentation system rather than reopening the feature-level gaps already recorded in iterations 1–4. The explicit iteration-005 override was followed over the reducer's stale prior next-focus text. The audit covered **5/5 named references**, **2/2 shared assets**, **5/5 `assets/examples/*` files**, **1/1 feature-catalog root plus 9/9 cards**, and **17/17 manual-testing-playbook scenarios**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:5-13] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-31]\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **P0 — The remote/local authority boundary is still not reproducible from the packet.** The current official hosted landing page directs AI-client integration to `developers.webflow.com/_mcp/server`, the official OSS README configures the remote service at `https://mcp.webflow.com/sse` and says the OSS implementation has no MCP `prompts` or `resources`, while the packet treats `https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp` as the hosted endpoint and describes remote resources/Agent Instructions. Separately, the local registration and server pointer still launch `webflow-mcp-server@latest`; the packet says to pin after discovery but contains no pinned package version, OSS commit, endpoint fixture, or `tool_info`/schema evidence. The official OSS export list does align with the packet's 18-module baseline, so the unresolved problem is provenance and reproducibility, not an invented module mismatch. Add one dated surface fixture containing transport, endpoint, package version/commit, tool count, action-schema digest, and `prompts`/`resources` presence; make DISCOVER-001/002/003 and the first-session example consume that fixture, and replace `@latest` after pinning. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/index.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:22-39] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:113-138] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:18-24] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md:12-18] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-30]\n\n2. **P1 — Packet release metadata and scenario counts disagree.** The packet README and manual playbook release-readiness text say “16” scenarios even though the playbook inventory and the actual files contain 17; the five named references also carry mixed versions (`1.0.0.0` through `1.2.0.0`), while the feature root is `1.2.0.0` and the skill/README are `1.3.0.0`. Several feature cards omit a version field entirely. This is a release-integrity defect: an operator cannot tell whether the 17-file corpus and the 31-tool/220-action inventory were audited from one coherent packet revision. Add a single packet freshness/version table, correct every 16→17 claim, require version metadata on every card/example/scenario, and add a CI check that counts files and rejects mixed release stamps. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/README.md:33-38] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/README.md:51-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:79-84] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:1-10] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:1-14] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:1-11] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:1-13] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/troubleshooting.md:1-12] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:1-9]\n\n3. **P1 — The catalog and playbook cross-reference graph contains wrong destinations.** The feature-catalog root's CMS “Source Files” row points to `design/component-variants.md` instead of `content/cms.md`. The manual root maps PAIR-002, whose contract is explicitly data-family transport-only, to the Designer card, and `pairing/pair-data.md` repeats that wrong feature path. Correct those links and add a link-integrity check that validates each scenario's feature file against its category/action family; otherwise a reader following the canonical map can load the opposite pairing rule or the wrong capability card. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:64-77] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:128-147] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:63-86] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:48-69] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:102-127]\n\n4. **P1 — The shared payload asset contains shapes that do not match the named action contract.** It claims to provide shapes built from official required-parameter lists, but the color-variable example supplies only `siteId`, `pageId`, and `value`, while `create_color_variable` requires `variable_collection_id`, `variable_name`, and `value`; the sitemap example uses `pageIds`/`sitemapStatus`, while the action reference names `bulk_update_pages_sitemap_status` with `site_id` and `pages[]` and separate item/page `includeInSitemap` operations. These are not merely omitted optional fields: they cannot be used to identify a valid payload for the cited MCP actions. Rewrite each block with its exact tool/action name, surface, global parameters, required fields, and expected response; label any illustrative REST/UI shape separately. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:60-79] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:345-358] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:393-408]\n\n5. **P1 — The 17-scenario corpus is category-complete but not capability-traceable.** The root correctly enumerates 17 scenarios, yet the scenario index records category and file only; it does not map each remote action family or each scenario to an exact action schema, surface, version fixture, or explicit `UNTESTED/SKIP` state. DISCOVER-001/002/003 compare `list_tools()` and counts, but do not require `tool_info`/action-schema comparison, endpoint recording, or resource/prompt capability checks. As a result, the corpus can report readiness while leaving remote-only families and remote/local drift unverified. This is a residual control defect, not a re-listing of the feature-specific gaps already recorded in iterations 1–4. Add a coverage matrix to `manual-testing-playbook.md` with action-family → scenario IDs → surface/version → evidence/skip reason, and make the discovery scenarios verify the pinned fixture before any action call. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-43] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:99-119] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:34-491] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/discover.md:20-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/discover-drift.md:20-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-50] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\n\n6. **P2 — Analyze is represented as a card and one scenario, but not as an operational seven-action slice.** The action reference names seven Analyze actions with distinct parameters; `intelligence/analyze.md` collapses four report families into generic prose, and READ-003 exercises only `get_query_guide` plus `get_traffic_report`. Add exact names/parameters for top pages, top dimensions, top events, and time-on-page, then either add deterministic scenarios or explicitly mark those actions as untested/skip-eligible when the Analyze add-on is absent. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:51-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/analyze.md:20-39] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/analyze.md:20-59] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-005.md","text":"# Iteration 5: Cross-focus completeness and residual authority reconciliation\n\n## Focus\n\nThis final iteration audited the requested inventory as one documentation system rather than reopening the feature-level gaps already recorded in iterations 1–4. The explicit iteration-005 override was followed over the reducer's stale prior next-focus text. The audit covered **5/5 named references**, **2/2 shared assets**, **5/5 `assets/examples/*` files**, **1/1 feature-catalog root plus 9/9 cards**, and **17/17 manual-testing-playbook scenarios**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:5-13] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-31]\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **P0 — The remote/local authority boundary is still not reproducible from the packet.** The current official hosted landing page directs AI-client integration to `developers.webflow.com/_mcp/server`, the official OSS README configures the remote service at `https://mcp.webflow.com/sse` and says the OSS implementation has no MCP `prompts` or `resources`, while the packet treats `https://mcp.webflow.com/mcp` as the hosted endpoint and describes remote resources/Agent Instructions. Separately, the local registration and server pointer still launch `webflow-mcp-server@latest`; the packet says to pin after discovery but contains no pinned package version, OSS commit, endpoint fixture, or `tool_info`/schema evidence. The official OSS export list does align with the packet's 18-module baseline, so the unresolved problem is provenance and reproducibility, not an invented module mismatch. Add one dated surface fixture containing transport, endpoint, package version/commit, tool count, action-schema digest, and `prompts`/`resources` presence; make DISCOVER-001/002/003 and the first-session example consume that fixture, and replace `@latest` after pinning. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/index.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:22-39] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:113-138] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:18-24] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md:12-18] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md:33-35] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-30]\n\n2. **P1 — Packet release metadata and scenario counts disagree.** The packet README and manual playbook release-readiness text say “16” scenarios even though the playbook inventory and the actual files contain 17; the five named references also carry mixed versions (`1.0.0.0` through `1.2.0.0`), while the feature root is `1.2.0.0` and the skill/README are `1.3.0.0`. Several feature cards omit a version field entirely. This is a release-integrity defect: an operator cannot tell whether the 17-file corpus and the 31-tool/220-action inventory were audited from one coherent packet revision. Add a single packet freshness/version table, correct every 16→17 claim, require version metadata on every card/example/scenario, and add a CI check that counts files and rejects mixed release stamps. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/README.md:33-38] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/README.md:51-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:79-84] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:1-10] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:1-14] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:1-11] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:1-13] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/troubleshooting.md:1-12] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:1-9]\n\n3. **P1 — The catalog and playbook cross-reference graph contains wrong destinations.** The feature-catalog root's CMS “Source Files” row points to `design/component-variants.md` instead of `content/cms.md`. The manual root maps PAIR-002, whose contract is explicitly data-family transport-only, to the Designer card, and `pairing/pair-data.md` repeats that wrong feature path. Correct those links and add a link-integrity check that validates each scenario's feature file against its category/action family; otherwise a reader following the canonical map can load the opposite pairing rule or the wrong capability card. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:64-77] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:128-147] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:63-86] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/content/cms.md:48-69] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/design/designer.md:102-127]\n\n4. **P1 — The shared payload asset contains shapes that do not match the named action contract.** It claims to provide shapes built from official required-parameter lists, but the color-variable example supplies only `siteId`, `pageId`, and `value`, while `create_color_variable` requires `variable_collection_id`, `variable_name`, and `value`; the sitemap example uses `pageIds`/`sitemapStatus`, while the action reference names `bulk_update_pages_sitemap_status` with `site_id` and `pages[]` and separate item/page `includeInSitemap` operations. These are not merely omitted optional fields: they cannot be used to identify a valid payload for the cited MCP actions. Rewrite each block with its exact tool/action name, surface, global parameters, required fields, and expected response; label any illustrative REST/UI shape separately. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:60-79] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:345-358] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:393-408]\n\n5. **P1 — The 17-scenario corpus is category-complete but not capability-traceable.** The root correctly enumerates 17 scenarios, yet the scenario index records category and file only; it does not map each remote action family or each scenario to an exact action schema, surface, version fixture, or explicit `UNTESTED/SKIP` state. DISCOVER-001/002/003 compare `list_tools()` and counts, but do not require `tool_info`/action-schema comparison, endpoint recording, or resource/prompt capability checks. As a result, the corpus can report readiness while leaving remote-only families and remote/local drift unverified. This is a residual control defect, not a re-listing of the feature-specific gaps already recorded in iterations 1–4. Add a coverage matrix to `manual-testing-playbook.md` with action-family → scenario IDs → surface/version → evidence/skip reason, and make the discovery scenarios verify the pinned fixture before any action call. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-43] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:99-119] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:34-491] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/discover.md:20-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/discover-drift.md:20-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-50] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\n\n6. **P2 — Analyze is represented as a card and one scenario, but not as an operational seven-action slice.** The action reference names seven Analyze actions with distinct parameters; `intelligence/analyze.md` collapses four report families into generic prose, and READ-003 exercises only `get_query_guide` plus `get_traffic_report`. Add exact names/parameters for top pages, top dimensions, top events, and time-on-page, then either add deterministic scenarios or explicitly mark those actions as untested/skip-eligible when the Analyze add-on is absent. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:51-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/intelligence/analyze.md:20-39] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/read-only/analyze.md:20-59] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\n\n7. **P2 — The five worked examples lack a shared surface/provenance/postcondition contract.** `first-session-discovery.md`, `read-cms-content.md`, `destructive-refused.md`, `staging-publish.md`, and `draft-page-settings.md` all provide useful operator narratives, but after their generic `list_tools()` step they do not carry a common exact surface/version field, action-schema source, or machine-checkable expected response. The first-session example says to pin and update fixtures, while the other four remain version-neutral, so examples can drift away from the action reference without being recognized as stale. Add frontmatter or a table to every example for `surface`, pinned version/fixture, tool/action, required schema source, postcondition, and known-unknowns; keep feature-specific corrections from iterations 1–4 in their existing findings rather than duplicating them here. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/first-session-discovery.md:19-38] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/read-cms-content.md:19-41] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/destructive-refused.md:19-40] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/staging-publish.md:19-40] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/examples/draft-page-settings.md:19-40]\n\n## Residual Recommendation Matrix\n\n| Severity | Exact files | Required addition |\n|---|---|---|\n| P0 | `references/mcp-wiring.md`, `references/tool-surface.md`, `assets/utcp-manual-reference.md`, `mcp-servers/webflow-mcp/README.md`, `manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/{discover,discover-drift,remote-surface}.md`, `assets/examples/first-session-discovery.md` | One dated endpoint/transport/package-or-commit/tool-schema/resource fixture; pin the server after capture; make discovery consume and verify it. |\n| P1 | `README.md`, `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`, all five named references, all nine feature cards, all five examples, and all 17 scenario files | One packet freshness/version stamp and generated count check; correct 16→17 claims and reject missing/mixed metadata. |\n| P1 | `feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md`, `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`, `manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md` | Correct CMS and PAIR-002 destinations; add category/action-family link-integrity validation. |\n| P1 | `assets/payload-examples.md`, `references/action-reference.md` | Replace variable/sitemap examples with exact MCP tool/action schemas, global parameters, required fields, and response assertions. |\n| P1 | `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`, all 17 scenario files, `references/action-reference.md` | Add action-family → scenario → surface/version → evidence/skip traceability and schema-aware discovery checks. |\n| P2 | `feature-catalog/intelligence/analyze.md`, `manual-testing-playbook/read-only/analyze.md`, `references/action-reference.md` | Enumerate all seven Analyze actions and cover or explicitly skip the four report families not exercised by READ-003. |\n| P2 | `assets/examples/*.md` (all five) | Add shared surface, pinned fixture, tool/action, schema source, postcondition, and known-unknown fields. |\n\n## Coverage Matrix\n\n### Five named references\n\n| Artifact | Audit result | Residual disposition |\n|---|---|---|\n| `references/action-reference.md` | Present; the remote 31-tool/220-action inventory and required-parameter tables are complete as a static snapshot. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:17-33] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:494-498] | Participates in Findings 1, 2, and 5; no prior feature gap reissued. |\n| `references/designer-capabilities.md` | Present; supplies the canvas/edit-loop, element, style, component, breakpoint, and worked-flow model. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:23-30] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/designer-capabilities.md:154-186] | Shared metadata/fixture debt only; prior Designer findings remain in iteration 1. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-001.md:7-23] |\n| `references/tool-surface.md` | Present; its 18-module OSS inventory matches the official OSS export family at the module-list level and explicitly labels itself a baseline. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:18-24] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/index.ts] | No pinned commit/package fixture; Findings 1, 2, and 5. |\n| `references/mcp-wiring.md` | Present; documents local stdio, remote alternative, auth, scopes, Bridge App, and the endpoint contradiction. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:22-39] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:113-138] | P0 reproducibility/endpoint fixture; Finding 1. |\n| `references/troubleshooting.md` | Present; covers discovery, auth, rate, publish, Bridge App, drift, workflows/webhooks, and redaction. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/troubleshooting.md:19-23] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/troubleshooting.md:79-103] | Its pinned-version recovery path depends on the missing fixture; Findings 1–2, with prior error/rate findings not reissued. |\n\n### Shared assets and `examples/*`\n\n| Artifact | Audit result | Residual disposition |\n|---|---|---|\n| `assets/utcp-manual-reference.md` | Present; accurately describes the registered stdio shape and says exact pinning is required, but its canonical example remains `@latest`. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/utcp-manual-reference.md:19-33] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/utcp-manual-reference.md:37-71] | Finding 1. |\n| `assets/payload-examples.md` | Present; five representative sections exist, but variable and sitemap blocks are not valid shapes for the named action contracts. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:48-94] | Finding 4; prior CMS/publish findings are not repeated. |\n| `assets/examples/first-session-discovery.md` | Present; useful discovery/pin narrative, but no concrete fixture fields or `tool_info`/schema step. [SOU