:7-23] |\n| SAFE-001 / `safety-gate/pubgate.md` | Present; PB confirmation, staging flag, single page, receipt, and queue evidence are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/pubgate.md:20-59] | Prior publish-completion finding only; no new reissue. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-002.md:13] |\n| SAFE-002 / `safety-gate/refuse.md` | Present; DS and production-publish refusal with zero-call evidence are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/refuse.md:20-59] | No new residual beyond Findings 1–2 provenance controls. |\n| SAFE-003 / `safety-gate/rate-limit.md` | Present; real-429 trigger, headers, Retry-After, and no-replay evidence are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/rate-limit.md:20-59] | Prior rate-limit finding only; no new reissue. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-004.md:21] |\n| SAFE-004 / `safety-gate/deploygate.md` | Present; local-OSS `run_workflow` DP confirmation, environment, rollback, and receipt are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/deploygate.md:20-59] | Local-only scope is named; no new feature finding. |\n| SAFE-005 / `safety-gate/bulkgate.md` | Present; selection enumeration and destructive bulk confirmation are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/safety-gate/bulkgate.md:20-59] | Included in Finding 5's capability-traceability gap; no prior feature issue reissued. |\n| PAIR-001 / `pairing/pair.md` | Present; sk-design-before-Designer-call order and DW class are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair.md:20-59] | No new residual. |\n| PAIR-002 / `pairing/pair-data.md` | Present; transport-only data-family behavior is specified, but its feature-file cross-reference points to the Designer card. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:20-30] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/pairing/pair-data.md:63-86] | Finding 3. |\n| NEG-001 / `negative/non-webflow.md` | Present; non-Webflow and sibling-intent deferral with zero Webflow calls are specified. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/negative/non-webflow.md:20-59] | No new residual. |\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- No Webflow MCP tool, credential, OAuth flow, mutation, publish call, or live-site test was attempted; the final prompt explicitly prohibited those actions. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:11-13]\n- Prior Designer, CMS/publish, scripts/forms/localization/assets, webhook/Enterprise/WHTML/utility, and rate-limit feature findings were not reissued; this pass records only cross-focus residuals and the Analyze slice not previously audited. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-001.md:25-31] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-002.md:21-28] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-003.md:19-27] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-004.md:23-30]\n- No static source was treated as proof of the deployed endpoint or live action schema; the unresolved three-way hosted/OSS/local contradiction remains an explicit unknown for a future permitted fixture. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:127-138]\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Static comparison cannot resolve which remote endpoint, package release, action schema, or `prompts`/`resources` capability the operator's pinned session will expose; live discovery is the smallest missing evidence, not a reason to infer a winner. [INFERENCE: based on the official hosted page, official OSS README, OSS module export list, and local surface-reconciliation contract] [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/index.ts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:127-138]\n- Counting `list_tools()` entries alone is insufficient to validate the 220-action remote snapshot or its safety classes; no further static count variation was found after the complete inventory audit. [INFERENCE: based on action-reference counts and the three discovery scenario contracts] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:17-24] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/discover.md:20-50] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/discovery-setup/remote-surface.md:20-50]\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: the reducer's prior next focus mentions rate limits, but the explicit iteration-005 prompt selects cross-focus completeness and overrides that suggestion; the narrower explicit focus was used. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/deep-research-strategy.md:224-226] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:5-13]\n- Contradictory evidence: current hosted Webflow guidance, the official OSS README, and the local packet disagree on the remote endpoint and capability surface; all claims are preserved, and no resolution is asserted without live discovery. [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:113-138]\n- Missing dependency: authenticated `list_tools`/`tool_info` and a provisioned test site were unavailable by explicit constraint; official hosted/OSS static sources and complete local inventory supplied the fallback. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/README.md:27-29] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:11-13]\n- Partial success: none for the selected static audit; every requested artifact was read and classified, but live endpoint/version behavior remains unknown. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-31]\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- [SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp]\n- [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md]\n- [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/index.ts]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/action-reference.md:17-33]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:18-56]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:22-39]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:113-138]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/utcp-manual-reference.md:19-71]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/assets/payload-examples.md:19-94]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:20-233]\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-148]\n- All five named references, both shared assets, all five worked examples, the feature-catalog root and nine cards, and all 17 scenario files listed in the Coverage Matrix.\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: **1.00** — seven fully new cross-focus findings; no prior feature-level finding was counted again.\n- Severity: **1 P0**, **4 P1**, **2 P2**.\n- Inventory coverage: **5/5 references**, **2/2 shared assets**, **5/5 examples**, **1/1 feature root**, **9/9 cards**, **17/17 scenarios**.\n- Questions addressed: Q4 residual remote/local/version reconciliation, Q5 complete artifact inventory, and Q6 residual file-by-file severity recommendations.\n- Questions answered: Q5 inventory completeness and Q6 residual recommendation matrix. Q4 remains partially unresolved until a permitted pinned live fixture exists.\n- Bounded live-discovery checks still unknown: record the actual remote/local endpoint and transport, package version or OSS commit, `list_tools` plus `tool_info` action schemas, 31/220 versus 18-module surface, resource/prompt availability, and the two payload schemas called out in Finding 4. [INFERENCE: based on Findings 1, 4, and 5]\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: reading the complete requested inventory before synthesis exposed cross-file defects that individual feature passes could not: wrong canonical links, stale corpus counts, invalid shared payload shapes, and missing provenance between a static reference and a live surface. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:61-77] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:21-31]\n- What did not work and why: live discovery could not be used because the dispatch prohibited Webflow MCP tools and credentials, so endpoint/version/resource contradictions remain unresolved rather than being collapsed into a confident claim. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:11-13]\n- What I would do differently: with an authorized fixture, run the discovery matrix first, persist the endpoint/package/commit/schema evidence, then use it as the sole authority for card, payload, example, and scenario validation; do not infer remote behavior from OSS `main`. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/tool-surface.md:20-24] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-webflow/references/mcp-wiring.md:135-138]\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nSynthesis/closeout should merge only these seven residual cross-focus findings into the final research output, preserve the prior iteration findings without duplication, and mark the endpoint/version/action-schema fixture as the explicit unresolved verification gate. No further broad research iteration is recommended under the five-iteration stop policy. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/deep-research-config.json:4-16] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/prompts/iteration-005.md:5-9]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":146,"totalLines":146,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/011-deep-research-quality-gaps/research/lineages/luna-max-fast/iterations/iteration-005.md","time":{"start":1785758542610,"end":1785758542618}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0279449cd724e0ba016a70834e5bd88191b8ea910dd94584bd"}},"id":"prt_fc780eb0e0014Bp2IaqnCu7QlR","sessionID":"ses_0388746ecffe5jux7SFKY5sCCH","messageID":"msg_fc7806c81001lp4f9k5O0rIvX5"}}
